eviantart.co...ikar-595192085</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://jason-felix.deviantart.com/art/MTG-Battle-For-Zendikar-Eldrazi-Destroyed-564929033\" target=\"_blank\">http://jason-felix.deviantart.com/ar...oyed-564929033</a><br /> <br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-11-2016, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:03:14-07:00","id":854006,"title":"","content":"I see a lot of Dragon: The Hunted influence in this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I like the ideas you're exploring here. While they may superficially appear to flirt with some of the themes of other gamelines (such as Mage or Mummy), this feels firmly anchored in the world of mortals and their relationship with the divine, rather than on external cosmologies.<br /> <br /> I quite like this, and I'd definitely like to see more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T07:29:45-07:00","id":854017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854006#post854006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see a lot of Dragon: The Hunted influence in this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I like the ideas you're exploring here. While they may superficially appear to flirt with some of the themes of other gamelines (such as Mage or Mummy), this feels firmly anchored in the world of mortals and their relationship with the divine, rather than on external cosmologies.<br /> <br /> I quite like this, and I'd definitely like to see more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rest of the concept work is coming.<br /> <br /> This is kind of why I've given up on Dragon for the moment. It felt too disconnected with humanity. With this I'm hoping to capture some of the same themes with a more human element. A lot of the inspiration is coming from the old Demon: the Fallen and from Demon: the Return.<br /> <br /> As for the stuff about external cosmologies, there's not a great deal of that, at least no more than in Werewolf. There is an alternate world that demigods can visit called the Drasil (yes, it has to do with Yggdrasil) and that realm sort of exists within the Temenos (sorta, kinda, not really) but it is very much focussed on action within the mortal world. Expect plenty of cults and cult-wars.<br /> <br /> Sneak peek: there's a mechanic called the Rapture which the demigods can't turn off. Care to hazard a guess at what it does?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-27-2016, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:28:41-07:00","id":854056,"title":"","content":"Might I perhaps suggest perhaps if looking for more inspiration into this, perhaps using Skullgirls? The Parasites (those that aren't living weapons) were mentioned to once have been worshipped like Gods and they need to be bound to a human host to use their powers. The best examples are Filia, Squigly and Eliza (especially Eliza).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:42:53-07:00","id":854062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854056#post854056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I perhaps suggest perhaps if looking for more inspiration into this, perhaps using Skullgirls? The Parasites (those that aren't living weapons) were mentioned to once have been worshipped like Gods and they need to be bound to a human host to use their powers. The best examples are Filia, Squigly and Eliza (especially Eliza).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thanks, I'll look into it. never come across the Skullgirls before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:54:14-07:00","id":854066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854017#post854017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest of the concept work is coming.<br /> <br /> This is kind of why I've given up on Dragon for the moment. It felt too disconnected with humanity. With this I'm hoping to capture some of the same themes with a more human element. A lot of the inspiration is coming from the old Demon: the Fallen and from Demon: the Return.<br /> <br /> As for the stuff about external cosmologies, there's not a great deal of that, at least no more than in Werewolf. There is an alternate world that demigods can visit called the Drasil (yes, it has to do with Yggdrasil) and that realm sort of exists within the Temenos (sorta, kinda, not really) but it is very much focussed on action within the mortal world. Expect plenty of cults and cult-wars.<br /> <br /> Sneak peek: there's a mechanic called the Rapture which the demigods can't turn off. Care to hazard a guess at what it does?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, I know exactly what you mean. I had a feeling that Dragon could've benefited from the titular dragons being more invested in humanity. IMO that's the beauty of Touchstones. With the CoD's talent for cosmologies, supernatural weirdness and metaphysical philosophy, there needs to be something that grounds the characters to the mortal world we can all relate to.<br /> <br /> Drasil sounds very interesting, as does the focus on action and cult-wars. It definitely fits the themes and mood you're going for in a way no other game has really touched (except maybe Geist with the Krewes, but that's a completely different flavour).<br /> <br /> Hmmm. The traditional meanings of Rapture involve joyful ecstasy and carrying someone to another plane of existence. So if I had to guess, then I'd say that Demigods either provoke ecstasy on onlookers when they use their powers (or perhaps only their cultists?) or can inadvertently carry mortals with them when they travel to another plane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T09:49:04-07:00","id":854089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854066#post854066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm. The traditional meanings of Rapture involve joyful ecstasy and carrying someone to another plane of existence. So if I had to guess, then I'd say that Demigods either provoke ecstasy on onlookers when they use their powers (or perhaps only their cultists?) or can inadvertently carry mortals with them when they travel to another plane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Close, but I've named with my penchant for irony very much in evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:14:47-07:00","id":854110,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit stuck on what to do for the Virtue/Vice equivalents. I'd kind of like it to be something a little like Beast's Legend/Life without being too close. Any suggestions would be welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:31:04-07:00","id":854116,"title":"","content":"The concept work is mostly up. The Introduction is coming next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:11:21-07:00","id":854133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854110#post854110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit stuck on what to do for the Virtue/Vice equivalents. I'd kind of like it to be something a little like Beast's Legend/Life without being too close. Any suggestions would be welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd say &quot;Myth&quot; and &quot;Impulse&quot;. The Myth is the Demigod reaching for the divine, regaining Willpower when they act towards the mythology they've built up for themselves. Their Impulse, instead, rewards them for giving into that one weakness they have. Zeus was promiscuous, Hera was jealous, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854116#post854116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The concept work is mostly up. The Introduction is coming next.</div> </div> </div> </div>All really good stuff! I very much like the Domain ideas (*eyes the Cold Domain with interest*), and I find it interesting you chose to make the Y-Splat so varied. I think it lends a cool uniqueness to the splat. I think the Rapture mechanics are very intriguing. The Drasil sidebar about the Supernal Realms is a bit outdated. In 2E, the Supernal Realms are not actual places that can be reached, but rather they are qualities/aspects of reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:15:16-07:00","id":854138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854133#post854133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Drasil sidebar about the Supernal Realms is a bit outdated. In 2E, the Supernal Realms are not actual places that can be reached, but rather they are qualities/aspects of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I was running off of the Mage 1e corebook for that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:17:26-07:00","id":854139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854133#post854133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'd say &amp;quot;Myth&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Impulse&amp;quot;. The Myth is the Demigod reaching for the divine, regaining Willpower when they act towards the mythology they've built up for themselves. Their Impulse, instead, rewards them for giving into that one weakness they have. Zeus was promiscuous, Hera was jealous, and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All really good stuff! I very much like the Domain ideas (*eyes the Cold Domain with interest*), and I find it interesting you chose to make the Y-Splat so varied. I think it lends a cool uniqueness to the splat. I think the Rapture mechanics are very intriguing. The Drasil sidebar about the Supernal Realms is a bit outdated. In 2E, the Supernal Realms are not actual places that can be reached, but rather they are qualities/aspects of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to make it as open and customisable as I could without compromising playability. Something I've always liked with magic systems is being able to be creative with spells. It's one of the big reasons why I like Mage and Ars Magica so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:19:32-07:00","id":854141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854138#post854138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. I was running off of the Mage 1e corebook for that part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you have the 2e development blogs to keep you up to date if you want to take a read! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\"> Revelations &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/revelations/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Mage Sight is now also tied up with the Supernal World \u2014 while the \u201cSupernal Realms\u201d have been described as other dimensions in the past, we\u2019re going to be much clearer in this edition that the Supernal is everywhere. The Aether is in every thunderclap, every wire, and every time a human approaches the divine.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854139#post854139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was trying to make it as open and customisable as I could without compromising playability. Something I've always liked with magic systems is being able to be creative with spells. It's one of the big reasons why I like Mage and Ars Magica so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I am a huge fan of customisable mechanics like that. So long as they're approachable, I'll be the #1 fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:48:54-07:00","id":854159,"title":"","content":"Having just written up the bit on Impulses and Myths, i can't help but want to play a narcissistic demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:53:42-07:00","id":854167,"title":"","content":"Hah! I think the contrast between the Myth and the Impulse is going to both evoke the classical stories of old while simultaneously giving the players something to aspire to and something to keep them grounded into their more human nature.<br /> <br /> And yes, I bet the narcissistic demigod is going to be a popular archetype. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T02:57:59-07:00","id":854400,"title":"","content":"A new mechanic is up: Halysis. <br /> <br /> Also, here's the power scaling for Domains.<br /> <br /> <b>O</b><br /> <br /> <u>Minor manipulation, minor creation, understanding, basic protection</u><br /> <br /> e.g. causing a plant to grow in a particular way, conjuring a small flame, seeing ghosts, becoming able to breathe underwater<br /> <br /> <b>OO</b><br /> <br /> <u>Minor transformation, </u><u>median</u><u> manipulation, </u><u>median</u><u> creation, </u><u>median</u><u> protection</u><br /> <br /> e.g. turning water into wine, causing a fire to leap from one place to another, creating a sapling, becoming immune to fire up to Bonfire intensity<br /> <br /> <b>OOO</b><br /> <br /> <u>Median transformation, greater manipulation, greater creation, greater protection, basic animation</u><br /> <br /> e.g. turning self into an animal, causing the earth to shake in a small radius, creating a downpour, becoming immune to any and all extremes of cold, animating a tree so that it can slowly move and speak <br /> <br /> <b>OOOO</b><br /> <br /> <u>Greater transformation, divine manipulation, divine creation, divine protection, greater animation</u><br /> <br /> e.g. turning another into an animal, causing fire to burn without damaging whatever it is burning, creating a tornado centered on the demigod, rendering others immune to all fire, creating a stone golem with the intelligence of a dull human<br /> <br /> <b>OOOOO</b><br /> <br /> <u>Divine transformation, mass manipulation, mass creation, mass protection, divine animation</u><br /> <br /> e.g. transmuting iron into a material that strikes a the soul, parting the Red Sea, summoning fire from the skies, creating protections against water that allow a city to be built on the seabed with a great dome of air above it, creating a race of sentient creatures that can reproduce freely<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T05:24:30-07:00","id":854421,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on Domains?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T05:31:08-07:00","id":854422,"title":"","content":"You got any plans on putting up a section concerning interactions between Demigods and other supernaturals? If so, I can say that those for Beasts, Mages, and Mummies would be my three most wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T05:54:26-07:00","id":854431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854422#post854422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got any plans on putting up a section concerning interactions between Demigods and other supernaturals? If so, I can say that those for Beasts, Mages, and Mummies would be my three most wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is going to be one yes. that's one of the parts I intend to do fairly swiftish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T11:43:37-07:00","id":854571,"title":"","content":"The part on supernatural interactions is up under 'Other Splats' in the opening post. Next comes the chart for Avatar followed by the process of becoming a demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T12:04:11-07:00","id":854583,"title":"","content":"The Avatar chart is up, along with a new and important mechanic: the Fading.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on the new stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-28-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T15:55:55-07:00","id":854706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854421#post854421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thoughts on Domains?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's still missing proper mechanics, but I quite like what I'm seeing!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854583#post854583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Avatar chart is up, along with a new and important mechanic: the Fading.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on the new stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick thoughts:<br /> <br /> IMO, Halysis needs a contested roll. Presence + Avatar vs. Composure + Supernatural Advantage should do the trick. At the end of every scene, the mortals roll, and those who fail take one step closer to Halysis. Mortals can purge the effects by spending [Avatar] days without contact with the Demigod. Disciples add their Disciple merit dots to the resistance roll and cleanse the Halysis effect in [Avatar] scenes, instead of days.<br /> <br /> The Fading: I understand what you're going for, but it might prove to be hard to keep track of, in terms of book keeping. I'd recommend simply reducing all Attributes by 1 every day, instead.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Relationships: Why do Demigods count as descending from the Dark Mother for Beasts? Even if we go back to the old myths about Titans and the like, you'd think Demigods would be the Beast-equivalents that descended from other Titans/Ancient Mythical Progenitors, rather than an offshoot of the Dark Mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:13:37-07:00","id":854717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854706#post854706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's still missing proper mechanics, but I quite like what I'm seeing!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They'll be coming soon. I know how I want them to work, it's just a matter of writing them down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854706#post854706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quick thoughts:<br /> <br /> IMO, Halysis needs a contested roll. Presence + Avatar vs. Composure + Supernatural Advantage should do the trick. At the end of every scene, the mortals roll, and those who fail take one step closer to Halysis. Mortals can purge the effects by spending [Avatar] days without contact with the Demigod. Disciples add their Disciple merit dots to the resistance roll and cleanse the Halysis effect in [Avatar] scenes, instead of days.<br /> <br /> The Fading: I understand what you're going for, but it might prove to be hard to keep track of, in terms of book keeping. I'd recommend simply reducing all Attributes by 1 every day, instead.<br /> <br /> Supernatural Relationships: Why do Demigods count as descending from the Dark Mother for Beasts? Even if we go back to the old myths about Titans and the like, you'd think Demigods would be the Beast-equivalents that descended from other Titans/Ancient Mythical Progenitors, rather than an offshoot of the Dark Mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice!<br /> <br /> In relation to the Dark Mother, my headcanon is that it's not so much being descended from Her as being of the same family tree. If I use Greek mythology as a metaphor, Gaia would be the Dark Mother and the other Protogenoi creatures of her ilk. Beasts would be titans and the other creatures (vampires, werewolves etc.) would be the Olympian gods. Demigods are part of a 'parallel' branch to Beasts, not strictly descended from the Dark Mother but from one of Her brothers or sisters. The connection is there and it works, but it's not quite the same as others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-28-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:33:07-07:00","id":854728,"title":"","content":"Well, my knowledge of Beast is very superficial, so if you say that it works, I'll take your word for it.<br /> <br /> Is there room for Domains that aren't physical? I was thinking it'd be interesting to have a Domain of Protection, that manifests as wards, shields, walls, force fields and the like. I'm thinking 4 dots of Domains are probably good, right? With a Mage-like cap on your max amount of starting dots in a single Domain based on your Avatar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:38:38-07:00","id":854730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854728#post854728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there room for Domains that aren't physical? I was thinking it'd be interesting to have a Domain of Protection, that manifests as wards, shields, walls, force fields and the like. I'm thinking 4 dots of Domains are probably good, right? With a Mage-like cap on your max amount of starting dots in a single Domain based on your Avatar?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is absolutely room for non-physical Domains. Basically anything that a god could be a god of is fine. I was looking for between 15 and 12 Domains by the end. <br /> <br /> What I was thinking for starting Domains was 2 dots in your Purview, 1 dot in a second Domain and 1 dot to put wherever you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:49:47-07:00","id":854733,"title":"","content":"That's probably quite fair. You can have a 2/1/1 spread or a 3/1 spread. It works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:57:08-07:00","id":854738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854733#post854733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably quite fair. You can have a 2/1/1 spread or a 3/1 spread. It works.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do a 2/2 as well if you wanted to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:53:21-07:00","id":854756,"title":"","content":"Indeed, and I quite like the symmetry of that. Especially for closely-related but still ultimately different Domains, like Cold + Water, Cold + Air, Life + Nature, War + Blood and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T04:10:08-07:00","id":854979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854706#post854706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it's still missing proper mechanics, but I quite like what I'm seeing!</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics for invoking Domains are up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T07:23:43-07:00","id":855061,"title":"","content":"A google Drive folder is up with a description of Ascension and, in broad terms, how it works.<br /> <br /> Some feedback would be more than welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:33:50-07:00","id":855291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=854979#post854979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics for invoking Domains are up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the mechanics, but they'll need some additional rules to gauge correlation between dots and mechanics (for example, a miracle of protection can grant &quot; */* Armour&quot; where * equals the Domain dots used). I would also advise some more detail as to what's allowed for the Exceptional Success (something like &quot;one effect from a lesser dot rating, or equal if it's a 1-dot miracle&quot; thing might be good).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=855061#post855061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A google Drive folder is up with a description of Ascension and, in broad terms, how it works.<br /> <br /> Some feedback would be more than welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension looks fine, not sure what you want feedback with, specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T01:45:09-07:00","id":855582,"title":"","content":"If anyone would like to help, some ideas for Numinous Form traits would be wonderful. Traits can have prerequisites of both Domains and Avatar rating.<br /> <br /> Here's some to start off with:<br /> <br /> Wings<br /> <br /> Serpentine form<br /> <br /> Aquatic<br /> <br /> Burning Touch<br /> <br /> Long Limbs<br /> <br /> Twilight Form<br /> <br /> Deathsight<br /> <br /> Holy Majesty<br /> <br /> Armoured Form","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T06:14:18-07:00","id":855644,"title":"","content":"More detailed rules for miracles are up in the GDrive folder as well as the chart for Attachment in the first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-30-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:41:35-07:00","id":856074,"title":"","content":"I really like the more detailed Miracle rules! Some comments:<br /> <br /> Manipulation miracles should use Manipulation/Dexterity/Finesse, IMO. Shaping something physically should call for Dexterity/Finesse, and shaping something socially or mentally should call for Manipulation/Finesse.<br /> <br /> Protection miracles should use Resolve/Composure/Resistance, to me.<br /> <br /> Transformation is pretty much the same as Manipulation, so they should be merged. Same with Animation and Creation.<br /> <br /> You might also want a Veiling-equivalent, unless you intend it to fall under Protection.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, looks pretty good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:01:45-07:00","id":856388,"title":"","content":"I'd would like to explore how Demigods interact with some of the other fan-created groups, particularly Irin, Leviathans, and the Demons from Demon: the Return, each which overlaps in an interesting way.<br /> <br /> Irin are based on the stories of angels, but one group themselves to be gods; Demigods are based on polytheistic accounts, but some may percieve themselves as angels - could their be some overlap or interact between the subgroups which adhere to a particular theology? Might they actually be the same kind of being on a some fundamental, but for some reason some become associated with the Divine Fire, while others grow associated with the Empyrean, the expression of human virtue and the opposite of the Inferno? If so, it might be possible for each to have a Z-type which represents evolution toward the other kind of being.<br /> <br /> In particular, this group would be nice to combine with Leviathan, representing the type of supernatural (or one of the types) that empowers the Empyrean Theurgists. Halysis could be changed to distinguish it more from the Wake of Leviathans, for those who (like me) would like to play up the contrast between the two types of divinity. To contrast with the brainwashed cults created by the latter effect, I would reverse the effect of Halysis in part: instead of causing mortals to lose their own opinions and adopt those of the Demigod, mortals caught up in Halysis become <i>more</i> filled with their own ideals and virtues, but attribute these to the Demigod (As in <a href=\"http://www.religioustolerance.org/god_pra6.htm#sum\" target=\"_blank\">this study </a>from the Ontario Consultants for Religious Tolerance: attempts to assess divine will almost invariably confirmed the worshipper's own beliefs). Naturally, this will make creating a stable cult very difficult, since the tendency will be for any such organization to fracture into warring groups (each using the same Demigod as a figurehead) based on the true beliefs of the members. The Disciple merit would represent the humility to look past one's own beliefs and towards what the Demigod is actually saying. For mortals that are effected, it might be interesting to encourage a more frenzied pursuit of preexisting virtues mechanically. Maybe they can now indulge virtues more frequently for the full willpower benefit, but automatically lose a few points of Willpower each day, which becomes free-floating faith either consumed by the Demigod or influencing the environment/other people in strange ways.<br /> <br /> The Erinyes sound as if they might be the Demigods' interpretation of the new Paragon fangroup that is being developed on this same forum. It isn't automatically clear the themes overlap quite yet, but both have a CoD take on mythology, which could be the basis for interesting crossover as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:01:10-07:00","id":856416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856388#post856388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd would like to explore how Demigods interact with some of the other fan-created groups, particularly Irin, Leviathans, and the Demons from Demon: the Return, each which overlaps in an interesting way.<br /> <br /> Irin are based on the stories of angels, but one group themselves to be gods; Demigods are based on polytheistic accounts, but some may percieve themselves as angels - could their be some overlap or interact between the subgroups which adhere to a particular theology? Might they actually be the same kind of being on a some fundamental, but for some reason some become associated with the Divine Fire, while others grow associated with the Empyrean, the expression of human virtue and the opposite of the Inferno? If so, it might be possible for each to have a Z-type which represents evolution toward the other kind of being.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had been thinking about Irin when I was writing about this actually and I thought much the same about the whole 'polytheistic vs monotheistic' thing. One thing though, I only used 'Empyrean' in the title to refer to the 'heavenly' or 'divine' origins of demigods. Whether they are actually associated with the Empyrean as opposite the Inferno is neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856388#post856388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular, this group would be nice to combine with Leviathan, representing the type of supernatural (or one of the types) that empowers the Empyrean Theurgists. Halysis could be changed to distinguish it more from the Wake of Leviathans, for those who (like me) would like to play up the contrast between the two types of divinity. To contrast with the brainwashed cults created by the latter effect, I would reverse the effect of Halysis in part: instead of causing mortals to lose their own opinions and adopt those of the Demigod, mortals caught up in Halysis become <i>more</i> filled with their own ideals and virtues, but attribute these to the Demigod (As in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.religioustolerance.org/god_pra6.htm#sum&amp;quot;]this</a> study [/URL]from the Ontario Consultants for Religious Tolerance: attempts to assess divine will almost invariably confirmed the worshipper's own beliefs). Naturally, this will make creating a stable cult very difficult, since the tendency will be for any such organization to fracture into warring groups (each using the same Demigod as a figurehead) based on the true beliefs of the members. The Disciple merit would represent the humility to look past one's own beliefs and towards what the Demigod is actually saying. For mortals that are effected, it might be interesting to encourage a more frenzied pursuit of preexisting virtues mechanically. Maybe they can now indulge virtues more frequently for the full willpower benefit, but automatically lose a few points of Willpower each day, which becomes free-floating faith either consumed by the Demigod or influencing the environment/other people in strange ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the ideas and I was a little worried about Halysis being too close to the Wake. One theme I'd very much like to get in this is responsibility for subordinates. Perhaps we could make it so that Halysis causes people to see the demigod as an exemplar of their virtue? Disciples would be people with the clarity to see the truth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856388#post856388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Erinyes sound as if they might be the Demigods' interpretation of the new Paragon fangroup that is being developed on this same forum. It isn't automatically clear the themes overlap quite yet, but both have a CoD take on mythology, which could be the basis for interesting crossover as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've not come across the Paragons. Do you suppose you could give me a link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:34:13-07:00","id":856431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856388#post856388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In particular, this group would be nice to combine with Leviathan, representing the type of supernatural (or one of the types) that empowers the Empyrean Theurgists. Halysis could be changed to distinguish it more from the Wake of Leviathans, for those who (like me) would like to play up the contrast between the two types of divinity. To contrast with the brainwashed cults created by the latter effect, I would reverse the effect of Halysis in part: instead of causing mortals to lose their own opinions and adopt those of the Demigod, mortals caught up in Halysis become <i>more</i> filled with their own ideals and virtues, but attribute these to the Demigod (As in <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.religioustolerance.org/god_pra6.htm#sum&amp;quot;]this</a> study [/URL]from the Ontario Consultants for Religious Tolerance: attempts to assess divine will almost invariably confirmed the worshipper's own beliefs). Naturally, this will make creating a stable cult very difficult, since the tendency will be for any such organization to fracture into warring groups (each using the same Demigod as a figurehead) based on the true beliefs of the members. The Disciple merit would represent the humility to look past one's own beliefs and towards what the Demigod is actually saying. For mortals that are effected, it might be interesting to encourage a more frenzied pursuit of preexisting virtues mechanically. Maybe they can now indulge virtues more frequently for the full willpower benefit, but automatically lose a few points of Willpower each day, which becomes free-floating faith either consumed by the Demigod or influencing the environment/other people in strange ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps Halysis could make people more and more convinced that their view on the world is right, as evidenced by the demigod and their 'patronage' of the person? With the demigod becoming something of an archetypal figure of virtue in their eyes, no matter what he actually does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-31-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:43:22-07:00","id":856432,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda that weird person who specializes in antagonist plot hooks, so...<br /> <br /> I'm guessing freed hosts of the Gigantes who have already mutated are the ghoul-equivalent? Sort of like the Enkidu to their Gilgamesh (Enkidu's elevation from a two-legged animal to shepherd is even something of the prototypical story, though in this case Shamhat's lovemaking didn't so much give the wild man civilization so much as chased the animal lurking in his skin back to Drasil). They're also creatures like Cerberus and Landon, monsters who serve the divine and moral order of the world.<br /> <br /> Mutual dependency-obviously, the &quot;Enkidus&quot; depend on their demigods for something resembling a new life after the Gigante ruined it, and the demigods on them for...something. Hm, maybe they're actually a little better at understanding the Drasil than demigods are, part of them having been born there?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, thought of a common role in myth: Guardians and enforcers (the demigods provide authority, the [lesser template] adjudicates it). This fits with divine monsters being living punishments for breaking moral law and protecting that which the divine rules over. In practical terms, the [lesser template] deals with things the demigod doesn't have the resources or interest in managing-and more importantly, they don't radiate Halyasis, allowing people under the Empyrean's gaze to remain people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 03-31-2016, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:59:30-07:00","id":856445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856432#post856432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm kinda that weird person who specializes in antagonist plot hooks, so...<br /> <br /> I'm guessing freed hosts of the Gigantes who have already mutated are the ghoul-equivalent? Sort of like the Enkidu to their Gilgamesh (Enkidu's elevation from a two-legged animal to shepherd is even something of the prototypical story, though in this case Shamhat's lovemaking didn't so much give the wild man civilization so much as chased the animal lurking in his skin back to Drasil). They're also creatures like Cerberus and Landon, monsters who serve the divine and moral order of the world.<br /> <br /> Mutual dependency-obviously, the &amp;quot;Enkidus&amp;quot; depend on their demigods for something resembling a new life after the Gigante ruined it, and the demigods on them for...something. Hm, maybe they're actually a little better at understanding the Drasil than demigods are, part of them having been born there?</div> </div> </div> </div>I...hadn't actually thought about that. I think they probably would be the 'Enkidu' figure and yes, they would be the minor splat. As for what demigods would get out of the relationship, I think it would be a combination of a powerful subordinate, someone to talk to who isn't affected by Halysis and that idea with the better navigation is an interesting one. Perhaps ex-gigantes could enter the Drasil anywhere as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:03:18-07:00","id":856447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856445#post856445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I...hadn't actually thought about that. I think they probably would be the 'Enkidu' figure and yes, they would be the minor splat. As for what demigods would get out of the relationship, I think it would be a combination of a powerful subordinate, someone to talk to who isn't affected by Halysis and that idea with the better navigation is an interesting one. Perhaps ex-gigantes could enter the Drasil anywhere as well?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. I also threw out something I thought of in the edit-monsters aligned with the divine are generally the iron fist of the gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T07:27:03-07:00","id":856459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856416#post856416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not come across the Paragons. Do you suppose you could give me a link.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536449-homebrew-template-paragon\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536449-homebrew-template-paragon\"> Homebrew Template: Paragon - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536449-homebrew-template-paragon\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536449-homebrew-template-paragon </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The short and skinny of this template is that it's a minor template applied to the children of people Claimed by spirits, with notes for variants including Sin-eater children and children of those Claimed by Angels and Qashmallim. Link here. (https://docs.google.com/document/d/155yUKQHVETKzIkQOmyXhpYaPqnddhg </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:41:39-07:00","id":856500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856459#post856459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/536449-homebrew-template-paragon\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...mplate-paragon</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. I've had a look and it's certainly something I can use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:44:22-07:00","id":856503,"title":"","content":"I think what i'm going to be working on next is the mechanics for Faith, followed by rules for Gigantes and Enkidu (thanks to Leliel for the name).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T09:52:49-07:00","id":856549,"title":"","content":"If someone would be kind enough to do some work on Merits, that would be greatly appreciated and you would get a mention in the credits. For the Temple Merit, I was thinking something much like the leviathan Temple merit, although some of the amenities might be different. Cults would probably be smaller and less extreme, more along the lines of the Cult Merit from DtD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-31-2016, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T10:20:30-07:00","id":856572,"title":"","content":"The document on Faith is up in the GDrive folder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:54:04-07:00","id":856700,"title":"","content":"The document for Gigantes is up in the GDrive folder.<br /> <br /> The Enkidu are coming next, followed by some more detailed info on the Drasil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T04:30:53-07:00","id":857052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=856431#post856431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps Halysis could make people more and more convinced that their view on the world is right, as evidenced by the demigod and their 'patronage' of the person? With the demigod becoming something of an archetypal figure of virtue in their eyes, no matter what he actually does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly.<br /> <br /> As to how to combine this with this the theme of responsibility for one's subordinates, that could be tricky, since although the mortals in question would believe they're acting according to the Demigod's wishes, they're effectively loose canons insofar as the Demigod is able to actually control them. On the other hand, that can be true in many leadership situations. Maybe the moral is to choose your followers carefully, since starting with people who actually do share your ideals might mitigate some of the disadvantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:07:30-07:00","id":857065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=857052#post857052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, exactly.<br /> <br /> As to how to combine this with this the theme of responsibility for one's subordinates, that could be tricky, since although the mortals in question would believe they're acting according to the Demigod's wishes, they're effectively loose canons insofar as the Demigod is able to actually control them. On the other hand, that can be true in many leadership situations. Maybe the moral is to choose your followers carefully, since starting with people who actually do share your ideals might mitigate some of the disadvantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the responsibility thing would fit reasonably well with this, both for the reasons you mentioned and because if you let them run around on your own once they're exposed to Halysis, it's going to be difficult to moderate them without exposing them further. This is where the intermediaries, high priests and Enkidu come in. They're liasons with the rest of the world. If you want to maintain a vaguely-controllable cult, you're going to need those intermediaries, with yourself only appearing on occasion to keep them 'in the fold' as it were. There's the other theme, the division between divine and mundane. I think that would work. I'll have a go at writing it.<br /> <br /> If you get any more insights, feel free to say!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:11:08-07:00","id":857066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=857052#post857052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, exactly.<br /> <br /> As to how to combine this with this the theme of responsibility for one's subordinates, that could be tricky, since although the mortals in question would believe they're acting according to the Demigod's wishes, they're effectively loose canons insofar as the Demigod is able to actually control them. On the other hand, that can be true in many leadership situations. Maybe the moral is to choose your followers carefully, since starting with people who actually do share your ideals might mitigate some of the disadvantages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You've got to be responsible for them otherwise all their views and opinions will be 'vindicated' in their mind by your 'patronage' of them. A person who's been brought up in a wealthy neighbourhood and who harbours a slight prejudice against black people, connecting them with crime, becomes more and more bigoted, believing that their beliefs are valued and supported by their god until they end up as the worst of racists. And if the demigod says to stop, weell, he's too merciful to these...things. They don't deserve it. And so it becomes worse.<br /> <br /> That's something that could be used to make the players squirm a little I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-01-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:30:08-07:00","id":857822,"title":"","content":"By the way, I'll be off the grid from Sunday to Wednesday. I'll try to keep up with any posts but i won't be able to post anything new. Just so you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:00:53-07:00","id":857974,"title":"","content":"By the way, the Paragon fansplat that was referred to earlier was not the one linked, it was instead one of my own threads:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab\"> Heroic Fansplat Community Collab - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> As suggested in threads like this one (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero) and this </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All right, as per requested, I'll take a look at the Gigantes.<br /> <br /> Looks good, though I think you might want to &quot;spice up&quot; the resistance roll. Instead of Resolve + Composure, why not Resolve + Integrity? This means that the more damaged a mortal's soul is, the more of the supernatural it has witnessed, the easier it is for Gigantes to possess them.<br /> <br /> Enkidu look interesting, I look forward to reading about their more unique mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T16:46:47-07:00","id":858007,"title":"","content":"This is sounding very promising! Have a Like, ajf115. Making the World-Tree one of the central Mysteries is only fitting, as Norse mythology is a goldmine for this subject.<br /> <br /> In terms of powers, I suggest you take a look at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/742772-i-ve-got-nobilis-3e-on-my-mind\"><b>Amechra's Nobilis-Like Influences</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/673743-irin-the-announced\"><b>Arcanist's &quot;Irin: The Announced&quot;</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\"><b>Almarck's &quot;Monarch: The Endless&quot;</b></a>. I would be more specific, but since this is <i>your</i> vision of Demigods in the CoD, it's better if you mix-and-match according to <i>your</i> preferences. Besides, I'm not very good with crunch.<br /> <br /> I'm slightly bothered by the way you wrote the title, but it's really a nitpick. You don't play as a Geist in Geist: The Sin-Eaters, but it's no big deal.<br /> <br /> Any ideas for a Z-splat? Something like the Entitlements from Changeling would be interesting. There's even one called &quot;The Lost Pantheon&quot; (Lords Of Summer, page 151) whose changelings seek to become Old Gods in the New World.<br /> <br /> How do the Empyreans typically interact with the fansplats? I imagine that Geniuses would be stumped on how to model such beings. They might try to explain Empyreans as &quot;super-Manes&quot;, or a side-effect of Mania Storms caused by Man redefining his relationship with the Divine. They might hypothesize that the Drasil is a one-of-a-kind Bardo. If that's true, how is it getting Mania to sustain itself? The Empyreans might have once been Manes sent to harvest Mania, but they grew too close to Man. They somehow mutated into a more stable form instead of succumbing to Havoc.<br /> <br /> I haven't read Leviathan or Princess, so I can't speak for those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:50:18-07:00","id":858068,"title":"","content":"Dragon: the Inheritance would probably find them intriguing and terrifying in equal measure. These are gods of their successors.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling that a lot of Demigods would consider Beasts just another form of Gigantes, at least at first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T00:54:10-07:00","id":858202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=858068#post858068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling that a lot of Demigods would consider Beasts just another form of Gigantes, at least at first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably. I deliberately designed the Gigantes to be similar to Unfettered and Horrors, but there's a distinction. Horrors are embodiments of the fear of a thing. Gigantes are the embodiments of a thing that is feared. For example, the Great Drake is an embodiment of Destructive Greed, not of the fear of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T01:06:36-07:00","id":858207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=858007#post858007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is sounding very promising! Have a Like, ajf115. Making the World-Tree one of the central Mysteries is only fitting, as Norse mythology is a goldmine for this subject.<br /> <br /> In terms of powers, I suggest you take a look at <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/742772-i-ve-got-nobilis-3e-on-my-mind\"><b>Amechra's Nobilis-Like Influences</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/673743-irin-the-announced\"><b>Arcanist's &quot;Irin: The Announced&quot;</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\"><b>Almarck's &quot;Monarch: The Endless&quot;</b></a>. I would be more specific, but since this is <i>your</i> vision of Demigods in the CoD, it's better if you mix-and-match according to <i>your</i> preferences. Besides, I'm not very good with crunch.<br /> <br /> I'm slightly bothered by the way you wrote the title, but it's really a nitpick. You don't play as a Geist in Geist: The Sin-Eaters, but it's no big deal.<br /> <br /> Any ideas for a Z-splat? Something like the Entitlements from Changeling would be interesting. There's even one called &quot;The Lost Pantheon&quot; (Lords Of Summer, page 151) whose changelings seek to become Old Gods in the New World.<br /> <br /> How do the Empyreans typically interact with the fansplats? I imagine that Geniuses would be stumped on how to model such beings. They might try to explain Empyreans as &quot;super-Manes&quot;, or a side-effect of Mania Storms caused by Man redefining his relationship with the Divine. They might hypothesize that the Drasil is a one-of-a-kind Bardo. If that's true, how is it getting Mania to sustain itself? The Empyreans might have once been Manes sent to harvest Mania, but they grew too close to Man. They somehow mutated into a more stable form instead of succumbing to Havoc.<br /> <br /> I haven't read Leviathan or Princess, so I can't speak for those.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the advice. I've had a look at Monarch and Irin but the Influences thing will be very useful as well.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean in the title is just because I looked up synonyms for 'heavenly' or 'divine' and it came up.<br /> <br /> Z-Splats? I haven't really been thinking those so far. I've been concentrating on the more 'central' stuff. I imagine that the Z Splat would be something like a solidification of the character's place in the divine, like taking on a specific aspect and immersing himself in it, gaining advantages and drawbacks.<br /> <br /> As for the fansplats, I've not put a great deal of thought into that but I'll give it a go:<br /> <br /> Leviathan: I would imagine that Demigods see leviathans as a twisted mockery of what they are while leviathans are fascinated by the way that Halysis doesn't directly drive people mad like the Wake. That would be a point of extreme interest for them I think.<br /> <br /> Princess: No idea. I've not really read princess but my best guess would be a kind of wary respect. they both seem to be deeply connected with humanity and the way that they think, as well as having a mutual connection with virtue. The problem is that demigods all too often focus on the glory of that virtue, not the nice parts.<br /> <br /> Genius: I suppose that Genii would most likely believe that demigods are either some kind of mutated Mane like you said or that demigods are beings akin to Genii, save that where genii are powered by the insane force of human creativity, demigods draw strength from the power of human belief. The way that genii in the past often set themselves up as gods might lend more credence to this theory of kinship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T01:08:55-07:00","id":858209,"title":"","content":"I'm putting up a doc in the GDrive folder for Merits and another for Form Traits that will be open for editing. If anyone has any ideas, even note-form, feel free to jot them down. If fully written-up versions are put in, I will be eternally grateful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:47:45-07:00","id":858261,"title":"","content":"Idle musing here on my end, but I was wondering how Demigods could be regarded by members of this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/852386-minor-template-striders\">minor template</a> I'm working on. A part of me is debating whether they'd be hunted by a separate lineage, or counted among the favored enemies of those who hunt the likes of Beasts and Heroes.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T04:23:37-07:00","id":860219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=858261#post858261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle musing here on my end, but I was wondering how Demigods could be regarded by members of this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/852386-minor-template-striders\">minor template</a> I'm working on. A part of me is debating whether they'd be hunted by a separate lineage, or counted among the favored enemies of those who hunt the likes of Beasts and Heroes.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that they would be all by themselves, since in every case so far you've grouped at least a few different creatures together. Dreamborn looks like the closest fit on your list, but maybe they should be part of a larger group that hasn't been created yet. Even though ajf115 has stated that the Empyrean connection may or may not exist, there is enough commonality that Demigods might be in a group with the inhabitants of that realm (in which case Gigantes might be added to some other group, since they don't share the same common ground). Also, if you're going to add additional fan groups one of those might have more in common with Demigods than Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T04:30:36-07:00","id":860224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=860219#post860219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that they would be all by themselves, since in every case so far you've grouped at least a few different creatures together. Dreamborn looks like the closest fit on your list, but maybe they should be part of a larger group that hasn't been created yet. Even though ajf115 has stated that the Empyrean connection may or may not exist, there is enough commonality that Demigods might be in a group with the inhabitants of that realm (in which case Gigantes might be added to some other group, since they don't share the same common ground). Also, if you're going to add additional fan groups one of those might have more in common with Demigods than Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either Dreamborn or as part of another group, eh? Well, seeing as I read up on all the recent material here, I think that warrants further pondering. Still, having a supernatural type that falls outside the purview of their known favored enemies could make for some interesting story hooks.<br /> <br /> On the subject of fan splats, the only one I've ever read in detail were the Leviathans. I kinda doubt there's any possibility of a Strider legacy developed against them, especially when you factor in the Ahabs and Beloved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:00:52-07:00","id":860236,"title":"","content":"I've come up with some preliminary ideas for merits. Feel free to modify or disregard them as you see fit.<br /> <br /> <b>* Anthropsychic</b> Some say that mortals were created in the image of the gods, others that humanity creates its gods in its own image. In either case, many Demigods remain closer to human nature than most other supernaturals can match. A Demigod with this merit is treated as having a Virtue and Vice in any situation in which it is relevant, including as a prerequisite for additional merits (usually Myth is treated as Virtue and Impulse as Vice, but it could be the reverse under certain circumstances).<br /> <br /> <b>** Secondhand Glory</b> Part of the Demigod's divine presence rubs off on his closest allies. At the cost of a point of Faith (<i>or Willpower?</i>), the Demigod can designate one person as a boon companion, worthy of respect through his or her closeness to the divine. For the remainder of the scene, anyone effected by the Demigod's halysis will view this person in the same favorable, if inaccurate light as they do the Demigod her/himself.<br /> <br /> <b>***** Halo Effect</b> Those who follow the Demigod do not question each other's integrity, for all are touched by the same glory. All those effected by the Demigod's halysis treat each other as if under the influence of Secondhand Glory. They continue to pursue their own goals, but assume that the others are somehow working towards the same objectives, even if their actions show the exact opposite. This makes it possible for them to belong to a single organization, although it will behave so erratically that it almost might as well be several different groups.<br /> <br /> <b>0 - **** Religious Affiliation</b> The Demigod has accepted a particular faith in her or his very essence. The Demigod no longer risks receiving &quot;tainted&quot; faith on a failed roll to draw faith from a person or Temple associated with this particular faith. However, this comes at the cost of being further from other religions. Attempts to draw faith from a person or Temple associated with other religions are reduced to a chance die. The cost of this merit is based on how narrowly the Demigod defines his or her religious tradition, and how prevalent it is.<br /> <br /> 0 - A tiny sect: there might be two congregations in the immediate area. The Demigod is unlikely ever to find any others without personally recruiting new adherents. At this point drawbacks balance benefits, so this does not cost any merit dots.<br /> * - A small niche religion, small denomination, or sub-group of a larger denomination (e.g. Conservative Southern Baptists)<br /> ** - A large denomination or equivalently large religion (e.g. Catholics)<br /> *** - A major world religion (e.g. Judaism, Islam, Hinduism)<br /> **** - An entire family of religions (e.g. Abrahamic religions)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T05:18:38-07:00","id":860241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=860236#post860236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've come up with some preliminary ideas for merits. Feel free to modify or disregard them as you see fit.<br /> <br /> <b>* Anthropsychic</b> Some say that mortals were created in the image of the gods, others that humanity creates its gods in its own image. In either case, many Demigods remain closer to human nature than most other supernaturals can match. A Demigod with this merit is treated as having a Virtue and Vice in any situation in which it is relevant, including as a prerequisite for additional merits (usually Myth is treated as Virtue and Impulse as Vice, but it could be the reverse under certain circumstances).<br /> <br /> <b>** Secondhand Glory</b> Part of the Demigod's divine presence rubs off on his closest allies. At the cost of a point of Faith (<i>or Willpower?</i>), the Demigod can designate one person as a boon companion, worthy of respect through his or her closeness to the divine. For the remainder of the scene, anyone effected by the Demigod's halysis will view this person in the same favorable, if inaccurate light as they do the Demigod her/himself.<br /> <br /> <b>***** Halo Effect</b> Those who follow the Demigod do not question each other's integrity, for all are touched by the same glory. All those effected by the Demigod's halysis treat each other as if under the influence of Secondhand Glory. They continue to pursue their own goals, but assume that the others are somehow working towards the same objectives, even if their actions show the exact opposite. This makes it possible for them to belong to a single organization, although it will behave so erratically that it almost might as well be several different groups.<br /> <br /> <b>0 - **** Religious Affiliation</b> The Demigod has accepted a particular faith in her or his very essence. The Demigod no longer risks receiving &amp;quot;tainted&amp;quot; faith on a failed roll to draw faith from a person or Temple associated with this particular faith. However, this comes at the cost of being further from other religions. Attempts to draw faith from a person or Temple associated with other religions are reduced to a chance die. The cost of this merit is based on how narrowly the Demigod defines his or her religious tradition, and how prevalent it is.<br /> <br /> 0 - A tiny sect: there might be two congregations in the immediate area. The Demigod is unlikely ever to find any others without personally recruiting new adherents. At this point drawbacks balance benefits, so this does not cost any merit dots.<br /> * - A small niche religion, small denomination, or sub-group of a larger denomination (e.g. Conservative Southern Baptists)<br /> ** - A large denomination or equivalently large religion (e.g. Catholics)<br /> *** - A major world religion (e.g. Judaism, Islam, Hinduism)<br /> **** - An entire family of religions (e.g. Abrahamic religions)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks so much for the help and a lot of the merits look very good, but the stuff for Religious Affiliation was going to come under the Z splat, which I've been pondering up here in Wales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T12:54:35-07:00","id":860497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=858261#post858261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle musing here on my end, but I was wondering how Demigods could be regarded by members of this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/852386-minor-template-striders\">minor template</a> I'm working on. A part of me is debating whether they'd be hunted by a separate lineage, or counted among the favored enemies of those who hunt the likes of Beasts and Heroes.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably their own lineage, although they might get involved with the ones who hunt Beasts as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T13:05:37-07:00","id":860512,"title":"","content":"And anyway: I'm Baaaaack!<br /> <br /> I'm not going to be doing anything tonight but I intend to finish up the Enkidu tomorrow, as well as getting onto the Drasil in more detail.<br /> <br /> Now, and I feel like I'm copping out when I say this, but could somebody please find it in themselves (and their schedule) to write up the new version of Halysis? I'll do it if no one can but this'll be playable that much faster if I don't have to do it alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:37:34-07:00","id":860942,"title":"","content":"the Enkidu are up and finished, apart from a sample character. Any feedback would be more than welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T05:05:05-07:00","id":860965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=860497#post860497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably their own lineage, although they might get involved with the ones who hunt Beasts as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might make more sense. Especially if said line also counted Gigantes and Enkidus as favored enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:38:39-07:00","id":861682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=860965#post860965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That might make more sense. Especially if said line also counted Gigantes and Enkidus as favored enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would think so, seeing as the stuff from the Demigod line doesn't actually come from the Astral like Beasts and Heroes do. They bear similarity but they're not the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T05:06:22-07:00","id":861750,"title":"","content":"The document on the Drasil is still a work in progress but it has at least some usable info. More is coming soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T08:47:30-07:00","id":862593,"title":"","content":"has anyone got any ideas for a name for the inhabitants of the Drasil that are neither Demigod nor Gigante. Beings analogous to Circe, the Moirai, the Norns, the myriad Yokai and demon-spirits, Kitsune and so on; beings neither god nor monster nor mortal but something in between. These would be the seers and magicians and other weird things that you find in myths. I'm considering making Erinyes a part of this, although I'm not sure on that front.<br /> <br /> I'm roughly working off of the lesser immortals from Scion but there's only so far I can stretch that. I'm thinking it's a minor template but not a full-on splat. They would be physical beings (Strength, Intelligence, Presence instead of Power etc) but they would still have access to Essence. They would probably only use it for powers analogous to Numina, with each of them having more or less 'unique' powers(although similar beings would probably still have similar powers (Kitsune are shapeshifters and illusionists etc).<br /> <br /> Does that sound OK or is it overpopulating the thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:03:24-07:00","id":862823,"title":"","content":"How courteous do you want to be towards other fansplats? Because the creatures you want to name are sort of the focus of another fansplat currently being developed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T22:19:44-07:00","id":863021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\