"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T01:33:54-07:00","id":863073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=863070#post863070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I shall have a peek. D'you mean the Heroic Fansplat thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T02:08:57-07:00","id":863081,"title":"","content":"Ah. I see your point with the lesser immortals stuff. I might add in a sidebar talking about adapting Horrors (the kind from Hunter) to act as these but I think I'll leave it at that.<br /> <br /> On another note, here's a new idea for an Idigam-equivalent: the Foris (latin for Outsiders).<br /> Ahem. <br /> <br /> The Foris are a mystery to the Empyrean. They are creatures of someplace <i>other</i>, beings which come from the outer darkness beyond the light of the Tree. They come with chaos for a sword and oblivion on their breath. They come to destroy, to render all of existence down into the inchoate darkness that was before, to destroy the hateful light that imposes its form and structure upon them. They are Apep, Erebus, Primordials, Ymir and Tiamat. They are things from before there was such a thing as 'being' and they come to burn and freeze and consume. We know nothing beyond this. Fear them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T02:13:48-07:00","id":863084,"title":"","content":"The Foris would be rare, perhaps 2 or 3 appear in a century, but they are <i>very</i> powerful, on the level of the Idigam and beyond. They appear in the Tree, seemingly walking (or flying or swimming or riding or whatever they appear to do) in from the starless night beyond the tree. They usually appear towards the middle of the tree and begin to consume it from there, releasing armies of minions into the Branches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T17:43:44-07:00","id":863401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=863021#post863021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my suspicion on what splat that is, but would you care to link here?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab\"> Heroic Fansplat Community Collab - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/823793-heroic-fansplat-community-collab </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> As suggested in threads like this one (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822143-ever-getting-a-hero) and this </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Done!<br /> <br /> So yes, the Erinyes, the Norns, the Moirai, the Valkyries and the Keres are all the focus of the Paragon fansplat. It's basically &quot;what if the supporting cast had to step in and become heroic?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Fated don't overlap much with the Empyrean, since, from what I can tell, the Empyrean are all about embracing their divine nature, while Paragons are themed as reluctant heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T02:38:31-07:00","id":863540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=863401#post863401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fated don't overlap much with the Empyrean, since, from what I can tell, the Empyrean are all about embracing their divine nature, while Paragons are themed as reluctant heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that.<br /> <br /> One thing I am intending to get in (and this'll be in some of the flavour text in the GDrive folder when I get around to writing it) is that being a demigod means becoming estranged from the normal world. You don't <i>feel </i> the same way you did before. Everything is more intense, bigger in a way. Feelings are <i>mythic </i> now. You feel hate and love and pain and pleasure more than you did before and it's genuinely hard to feel gentle, subtle things like the pleasure of just sitting and having bit of peace and quiet. Love is epic and powerful. It's never just a crush, never just a momentary 'oh, she looks nice'. You <i>have </i> to have her and there's that little voice in your head that says 'You're half <i>god</i> now. How dare she dismiss you! You can just <i>make </i>her love you, can't you?'. You don't just get irritated or a little annoyed. You <b>hate </b>the guy who got promoted instead of you and again there's that little voice that says 'You could burn him you know. Set a fire in his bones and watch him <i>writhe</i>.'. You're not human any more. You're something beyond that and it's scary. I'm actually considering putting in a penalty in the Avatar chart, similar to Jabir from Genius, to rolls where you try to conceal your emotions.<br /> <br /> I know that I haven't got this across really, I have a tendency to come up with ideas in my head and then because I know what I'm talking about I kind of expect other people to too. Sorry about that. I'll keep an eye on the Paragon thread to make sure I'm not treading on any toes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T02:48:35-07:00","id":863543,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the consideration! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the bit about penalties, you could have a scaling set of penalties (from -1 at 1 dot to -5 at 10 dots, perhaps) to Composure rolls meant to control or conceal strong emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T03:10:32-07:00","id":863548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=863543#post863543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the consideration! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the bit about penalties, you could have a scaling set of penalties (from -1 at 1 dot to -5 at 10 dots, perhaps) to Composure rolls meant to control or conceal strong emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. Also, I've started writing up the new version of Halysis. I just need to get to work on the specific effects of the different levels of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T11:34:54-07:00","id":866463,"title":"","content":"Have you consided &quot;non-dice&quot; penalties as part of Attachment? <br /> <br /> Perhaps something similar to what Werewolves have for when manifesting Numinous form. At lower levels, you occassionally risk sliding into it, and higher levels, you're too human to trigger it without lots of &quot;clear you head&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T11:51:04-07:00","id":866471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=866463#post866463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you consided &amp;quot;non-dice&amp;quot; penalties as part of Attachment? <br /> <br /> Perhaps something similar to what Werewolves have for when manifesting Numinous form. At lower levels, you occassionally risk sliding into it, and higher levels, you're too human to trigger it without lots of &amp;quot;clear you head&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I might put something like that in. It probably wouldn't be a mechanical effect. It'll be in the proper write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T12:37:02-07:00","id":866491,"title":"","content":"When using Numinous form, how exactly does the rule set work. How do you do actions here? Dice wise?<br /> <br /> Also how do you regard changing technology to &quot;forge&quot; instead? <br /> Technology atleast what we consider technology is not a classic domain.... but it'd be part of the much larger creation crafting portfolio.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is Ascent to Godhood going to be a thing?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also Monarch - Demigod interactons? How do you seeing that going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T12:53:13-07:00","id":866498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=866491#post866491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When using Numinous form, how exactly does the rule set work. How do you do actions here? Dice wise?<br /> <br /> Also how do you regard changing technology to &amp;quot;forge&amp;quot; instead? <br /> Technology atleast what we consider technology is not a classic domain.... but it'd be part of the much larger creation crafting portfolio.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is Ascent to Godhood going to be a thing?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also Monarch - Demigod interactons? How do you seeing that going.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Still working on that. For the most part, it's like going into Demonic form for a demon, except they use the simplified attributes instead. Form Traits can alter things, but for the most part they work similarly to normal human bodies.<br /> <br /> 2) Technology is basically a placeholder name. The domain is basically over all technology, as defined as 'an object or thing which has been created or altered to accomplish a specific purpose'. Computer programs, swords, cars and sticks you've pulled the leaves off of to make a club all count as technology.<br /> <br /> 3) By design, the Second Ascension is very, very mysterious. Demigods haven't the faintest clue what happens to those who undergo it. It's a leap of faith, rather appropriately. There won't be mechanics for it, as an Ascended Demigod would be in the same league as Rank 6+ entities. To misquote Demon the Fallen, &quot;Apotheosis and obliteration look a great deal alike from the outside&quot;. It's like when a Changeling becomes one of the Gentry, except more ambiguous.<br /> <br /> 4) I've no idea, frankly. I might elaborate on this at a later date, but for the moment I haven't a clue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T12:39:22-07:00","id":866995,"title":"","content":"I have a request to make. If anyone is interested and has the time, could someone (or several someones) write down a few ideas for Followings, under the following format:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Name</u><br /> <br /> Short Description<br /> <br /> Summary of Organisation<br /> <br /> Sample Numinous Form</b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:08:41-07:00","id":869404,"title":"","content":"I finally finished up the mechanics for Halysis and intend to finish up the rules for a demigod's Cult, followed by the Temple Merit. After that's I'm going to be working on writing up Attachment and Avatar fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T13:22:11-07:00","id":869602,"title":"","content":"Faith has been changed to Potentia, as I felt like I was mooching off of Demon: the Return. Furthermore, I have begun on the Temple Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T13:57:04-07:00","id":869631,"title":"","content":"I have a problem here. In my opinion, the game is altogether too light on conflict. Some ideas for a more constant threat than the occasional Gigante or Foris incursion would be great.<br /> If anyone can help or has any ideas, I beg you, please, make yourself known! Give my poor, barren soul some inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T14:37:38-07:00","id":869667,"title":"","content":"Well, let's see here... Pagan demigods have a few natural enemies that come to mind;<br /> 1) Rival gods/demigods<br /> 2) Monotheism!<br /> 3) The Titans, et al.<br /> 4) Monsters. Hercules needs a Nemean Lion to slay, after all.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that's all I can think of. I know I'd run demigod's as antagonists to the Fallen in my Demon campaigns, since they both fight for cults and worship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T15:35:51-07:00","id":869714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=869667#post869667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, let's see here... Pagan demigods have a few natural enemies that come to mind;<br /> 1) Rival gods/demigods<br /> 2) Monotheism!<br /> 3) The Titans, et al.<br /> 4) Monsters. Hercules needs a Nemean Lion to slay, after all.<br /> <br /> Hmm, that's all I can think of. I know I'd run demigod's as antagonists to the Fallen in my Demon campaigns, since they both fight for cults and worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>HM. I think that my main problem at the moment is that I'm not really sure what it is exactly that demigods do. Werewolves deal with spirits, vampires have their Danse Macabre, Prometheans strive towards the New Dawn. The closest I can think for demigods is trying to understand their new state and what they should be. That's quite woolly though. It's not the best base to build a Chronicle off of. Some advice would be welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T20:56:26-07:00","id":869889,"title":"","content":"I say look to the old Scion for Inspiration. Perhaps, the Demigod's main thing to do is labor for more powers. Call it the Great Labor, and have them need to, well, quest to gain XP. They need to have plans, and do things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T02:55:26-07:00","id":870056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=869889#post869889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say look to the old Scion for Inspiration. Perhaps, the Demigod's main thing to do is labor for more powers. Call it the Great Labor, and have them need to, well, quest to gain XP. They need to have plans, and do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>hm. It still feels a little too hollow and a bit too close to endorsing power gaming to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've had a bit of a brainstorm about how I can rearrange their supernatural scene to give them a little more conflict other than on-off monsters. I've come up with a more solid cosmology in terms of the entities that populate it and a little bit of feedback would be nice. The following is a 'family tree' of sorts, showing the hierarchy of beings. bear in mind that the 'true divines' and the 'primordial divines' could be the Olympians and the Protogenoi respectively, or they might be the Archangels and the Unmoved Mover, or they might be Bodhisattvas and Devas.<br /> <br /> Primordial Divines &gt; Titans &gt; True Divines &gt; Demigods<br /> <br /> Titans &gt; Titan Shards &gt; Titanspawn<br /> <br /> Gigantes &gt; Enkidu<br /> <br /> Titan Shards are very powerful things and are the equivalent of Idigam. On the bright side, each Shard has its own prison within the Drasil, as a result being one of the losers in the War in Heaven, the eternal conflict between the True Divines and the Titans. On the other hand, Titanspawn are powerful entities, although they vary in power. Titanspawn are creatures created by the Titan Shards with work towards freeing their masters from their entrapment. Some are simple monsters, some are, to all appearances, human. Needless to say, they can cause quite a bit of trouble in both the Drasil and the Phenomenal world.<br /> <br /> Gigantes are now basically independent beings who do not necessarily hate demigods but covet many of the same things, such as Gardr and Temples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-21-2016, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T04:06:00-07:00","id":870077,"title":"","content":"It's not quite in the format you wanted, and it hasn't been aligned with the latest revisions, but here are my ideas for the followings: <b>Following of Vassals (nickname: Lackeys)</b><br /> This following believes that Demigods have been selected by the True God (or the True Goddess, or True Gods, plural) to be their servants on Earth. Unfortunately for them, they don't have much more insight into what their gods may want than mortals do, so they tend either to become scrupulous interpreters of holy texts, or to wander other worlds looking for beings who fit the description they have in mind (popular choices have been powerful spirits, Astral versions of various gods, and the Divine Fire - the God-Machine has been less popular, as it usually grinds Demigods who offer to serve it into raw material for new angels). This latter option makes them the following which interacts most frequently with other supernaturals, although not always in a positive way.<br /> A majority of their members are of the monotheistic faiths, but there are also some who believe themselves to be servants of polytheistic deities. Their Cults and Temples almost invariably mirror their chosen faith, though there is something of a split between Vassals who found or latch onto relatively orthodox groups and those who start idiosyncratic sects who see a given Vassal as their primary<br /> Opinions on Second Ascension are also divided: most believe it to be the final reward for their service, with the polytheists among them believing that the True Gods promote worthy Demigods to their own ranks. However, a few believe that Second Ascension actually represents damnation or some form of demotion, and point to the fact that it is the Demigods who became most distant from humanity - and thus most distracted from their mission among humans - who are most likely to ascend again.<br /> Wings are the most common element tying together the numinous forms of this following, symbolizing their role as go between for the higher heavens and the mundane world.<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\"> </span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Following of Sparks (nickname: Fragments)</b></span><br /> This following believes that there is only one thing which is truly divine, faith itself. Demigods are the result when humans have a great concentration of Faith.<br /> Members of this following tend to collect faith from members of all religions equally, seeing each as a similar means for faith to express itself in the world. They seldom belong to an organized mortal religion themselves, but some may believe that the worldwide sea of Faith is itself conscious and thus be able to reconcile it with some form of monotheism or pantheism (there are virtually no polytheists among them - the Sparks believe that polytheistic religions originally followed Demigods who have long since Ascended for the second time and thus no longer have individual consciousness). The Following of Sparks is itself more like a religion than most of the other Followings: unlike the following of Reincarnates, they believe in a higher power which should be served, and unlike the Following of Vassals, they have reached an agreement on roughly what this power is and what it wants. Simply put, it wants more of itself to be spread throughout the world. Sparks accomplish this mission by spreading new Cults and founding new Temples, which tends to make them popular with other followings even if their reasons for doing so do not, for they create far more of these resources than they use themselves and are often willing to share.<br /> Sparks believe that Second Ascension is the process of becoming one with Faith again, and they see it not only the pinnacle and goal of their own existence, but of everyone else's as well.<br /> The numinous forms in this following tend to be fiery or to radiate some other form of energy, reflecting the belief among followers that they are filled with the energy of faith.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Following of Reincarnates</b></span><br /> This following believes that each Demigod is the reincarnated form of some known deity from a known religion. What pantheon they believe themselves to hail from varies from Demigod to Demigod, but they have established techniques which they claim can verify a Demigod's original divine identity. Whether this actually works or not is of course a matter of faith, but true or not, the rites involved have led to this group's explosive growth over the past few decades, now that they have been freed from the embarrassment of having dozens of &quot;Thors&quot; and &quot;Dagdas&quot; at the same time, which once opened them to all manner of mockery. (Note: If there is eventually going to be a form of Rote for miracles, then I think it would be a good idea to give some to each Following to further distinguish them, and this would be one that pertains to the Reincarnates.)<br /> Reincarnates usually establish Temples and Cults based on the original religions of the gods they believe themselves to be, although they seldom place much emphasis on doing things exactly the same way as the ancients did. They consider themselves the ultimate authority within their own cults, and typically feel free to change things not only century to century but day to day as the mood strikes them. Occasionally a group of Reincarnates who believe themselves to hail from the same pantheon will create Cults and Temples which they share amongst themselves, in which case they tend to default more to the ancient example (as they understand it) as a compromise. Even more rarely, some Reincarnates may give space in their Cults/Temples to allies of their mythical persona whose reincarnation they've never met or who are believed to still enjoy True Godhood.<br /> Reincarnates are split on the issue of Second Ascension. Many believe that Demigods who vanish in this manner have returned to their otherworldly thrones, but others believe that Demigods who supposedly ascend for the second time actually find themselves starting over in a new mortal body. The rite of identity supports both theories: some of the ascended deities are replaced almost immediately, while other names never reappear.<br /> The numinous forms in this following are the most varied, since each Demigod comes to resemble the god they believe themselves to be rather than any unified template. Common elements are a basically humanlike form, and signature weapons. Perhaps because it is a religion which already admits the possibility of reincarnation, Hindu deities are particularly likely to be claimed by reincarnates, so blue skin and multiple arms are frequent as well<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:28px\"> </span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Following of Heirs</b></span><br /> This following believes that the gods worshipped by previous religions either never existed or have died, and that Demigods are the creation of humankind's collective soul to fill the void. Some believe that Demigodhood is the eventual destiny of every human being, while others merely consider themselves shepherds of humanity's aspirations, a role they try to fulfill in different ways.<br /> They tend to be the most modern in their outlook of all the followings, and often dismiss older religions as steps (or even wrong turns) on the path that lead to the current generation of Demigods.They have no qualms about taking faith from worshippers or temples of other religions, but their own Temples and Cults are usually started in their own names or that of their personal ideals, and incorporate all of the improvements which a particular Heir sees in society since the major world religions were founded.<br /> Unlike the other followings, the Heirs are almost unanimous in seeing Second Ascension as a bad thing. They believe themselves to be empowered directly by the aspirations of humanity, and so deduce that losing Attachment would completely destroy those who have become more faith than human themselves.<br /> Numinous forms in this following are among the least flashy, since the Heirs see themselves more as &quot;Humanity+&quot; than as something dramatically different. Increased size, astonishing beauty, or unearthly grace are often the only things which distinguish their numinous forms from their regular ones.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T04:10:13-07:00","id":870079,"title":"","content":"As for bringing in more conflict, we could try inventing one or more antagonistic factions (no ideas immediately come to mind), come up with new Hunter groups that might seek to strike against Demigods (or use existing ones), or give the PC factions reasons to fight against each other.<br /> <br /> Based on your theme of being responsible for ones subordinates, it might be good to create some way for Demigods to be led into conflict by their own Cults or even to have their Cults attack other Demigods without the Demigods leading them ever becoming aware of it. It might annoy players if their Cults have too much life of their own, though, and one would think that <i>halysis</i> would keep mortals from being much of a long-term direct threat. Maybe looking at the latest revision will spark some more ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=869404#post869404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finally finished up the mechanics for Halysis and intend to finish up the rules for a demigod's Cult, followed by the Temple Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see the rules for the revised <i>halysis</i> on Google Drive. Are they up yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","user":"Alastor","date":". 04-21-2016, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T05:10:47-07:00","id":870097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=870079#post870079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't see the rules for the revised <i>halysis</i> on Google Drive. Are they up yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry for the confusion, they're in the first post on the thread. I haven't got around to putting it up in its own doc. It's under Inherent Powers.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much for the stuff about Followings. I haven't had the chance to read them thoroughly yet but I'm going to find a time when I can read them over in detail and give some opinions. From what I've seen so far, they look to be right on the money.<br /> <br /> For the stuff about cults getting out of hand, due to the powerful effects that Halysis engenders other than obedience and reverence, that's actually quite common. One of the statistics for Cults is Doctrine, which deals with how much you've got your Cult under control and how much you can curb their excesses with holy laws and commandments. If a cult begins to think that their god is being to merciful to that other god, they'll probably come to the conclusion that He wants them to act on their own (when of course the other demigod might actually be more powerful than the one with the cult) and get the demigod into quite a bit of trouble.<br /> <br /> I don't think that there'll be direct 'Miracle Rotes', but I was considering 'specialties' of a sort that the Following grants. They would be to Domains what Specialties are to skills. They might be bit more important though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-21-2016, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T05:40:49-07:00","id":870109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=869889#post869889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say look to the old Scion for Inspiration. Perhaps, the Demigod's main thing to do is labor for more powers. Call it the Great Labor, and have them need to, well, quest to gain XP. They need to have plans, and do things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to be said that I don't particularly like the idea of demigods having 'seeking power' as their central thing. They have power and can obtain it easily. What they lack is understanding. They know almost nothing about themselves. They might have faith that they are a particular thing, but they have no solid proof. For all their power, they cannot find a meaning to their own existence, other than to demand worship. For all they know, they might simply be puppets of higher powers, dancing on strings for their amusement. That's not a comfortable thing to feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:18:50-07:00","id":870129,"title":"","content":"Not that I disagree with you, but a quest doesn't mean goign for power, that could be the impetus, but ultimately be about gaining wisdom. It's an old tale. However, I like what you've wrote so far, good ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T04:16:08-07:00","id":875480,"title":"","content":"The major thing which comes to mind to create more conflict between Demigods would be to make Potentia more difficult to harvest, forcing them to fight over it. As it stands, it looks as if there is no limit to the number of different Demigods who can take Potentia from the same Temple. If we limit the number of times a Temple can provide resources based on its rating, it would incentivize more fighting over them, as well as making Gigantes more of a threat, assuming the Essence they draw from Temples counts against the same limit.<br /> Since the power provided by Temples now comes from a root of the Drasil rather than directly from the worship that takes place there, I suggest that drawing on more than the limit be possible, but risks killing the root providing the Temple's value, which most Demigods would be reluctant to do. This would open the possibility of a group that kills these roots deliberately, trying to sever the world from the Drasil. It would be interesting if such a group didn't even see Demigods as much of a threat to be opposed - they just want to stop the Gigantes (and Titanspawn?) who occasionally invade the mundane world, and see inconveniencing Demigods as an acceptable loss. It would be unlikely ever to happen, but it they ever succeeded well enough at their goal to kill all the roots leading to the regular world, it might hurt the tree itself, with possible far-reaching results which no one would be able to predict. Something I like about this possible group is that it represents one of your themes - separation between the mortal and the divine.<br /> Another group that could play with this theme is one that seeks to enforce the Masquerade as it pertains to Demigods. Their reasoning would be that mortals for some reason need to be free to doubt, and that by their presence and open activity by Demigods tend to stunt the ability of humans to develop faith on their own, without evidence.<br /> <br /> P.S. Thank you for directing me to the correct location for the new <i>halysis</i>. I like the way it looks from the Demigod standpoint: the mechanical aspect is simple and the description provides clear guidelines for how mortals influenced by it may act while still leaving room for variety. It would be nice to have it written as a series of conditions so that it would be easier to use if Demigod NPCs are encountered in Mortal or Hunter game, but for Demigod itself that isn't really necessary.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:11:21-07:00","id":875545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=875480#post875480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The major thing which comes to mind to create more conflict between Demigods would be to make Potentia more difficult to harvest, forcing them to fight over it. As it stands, it looks as if there is no limit to the number of different Demigods who can take Potentia from the same Temple. If we limit the number of times a Temple can provide resources based on its rating, it would incentivize more fighting over them, as well as making Gigantes more of a threat, assuming the Essence they draw from Temples counts against the same limit.<br /> Since the power provided by Temples now comes from a root of the Drasil rather than directly from the worship that takes place there, I suggest that drawing on more than the limit be possible, but risks killing the root providing the Temple's value, which most Demigods would be reluctant to do. This would open the possibility of a group that kills these roots deliberately, trying to sever the world from the Drasil. It would be interesting if such a group didn't even see Demigods as much of a threat to be opposed - they just want to stop the Gigantes (and Titanspawn?) who occasionally invade the mundane world, and see inconveniencing Demigods as an acceptable loss. It would be unlikely ever to happen, but it they ever succeeded well enough at their goal to kill all the roots leading to the regular world, it might hurt the tree itself, with possible far-reaching results which no one would be able to predict. Something I like about this possible group is that it represents one of your themes - separation between the mortal and the divine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent idea and one which I have a couple of ideas for enforcing. Perhaps a Temple gathers 1 point of Potentia every ((6 - Potency)*2) hours and can hold a number of points equal to (Potency*2). If you try to gather Potentia while the thing is empty, it temporarily reduces the Temple's Potency. If the Potency is reduced to 0, the Temple loses its power, although it might regain it in the future. Sound good? It would make Temples quite fragile edifices. Much like faith, in fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=875480#post875480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another group that could play with this theme is one that seeks to enforce the Masquerade as it pertains to Demigods. Their reasoning would be that mortals for some reason need to be free to doubt, and that by their presence and open activity by Demigods tend to stunt the ability of humans to develop faith on their own, without evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I might build on that. They probably wouldn't be a direct antagonist group, but they could certainly interfere with the PCs business.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=875480#post875480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S. Thank you for directing me to the correct location for the new <i>halysis</i>. I like the way it looks from the Demigod standpoint: the mechanical aspect is simple and the description provides clear guidelines for how mortals influenced by it may act while still leaving room for variety. It would be nice to have it written as a series of conditions so that it would be easier to use if Demigod NPCs are encountered in Mortal or Hunter game, but for Demigod itself that isn't really necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'm quite up to codifying it as a series of Conditions at the moment, but I might get around to doing that eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T06:51:39-07:00","id":884585,"title":"","content":"If it's fine for me to say, I love how this fansplat is turning out. But if I may ask, has there been any ideas for Z Splats? I have one if there isn't any prior ones.<br /> <br /> Pretty much, some gods can lord over certain concepts that are really specific or cross into other Supernatural Territory. For example, Hecate is the Goddess of Witchcraft, Selene is a Goddess of the Moon, Melinoe is a Goddess of Undeath, so on and so forth. What I was thinking was the idea that the Z Splat could cover these really specific functions, being able to use special Domains that cross over into other supernatural thresholds and holding power there as well. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T12:57:46-07:00","id":884835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=884585#post884585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's fine for me to say, I love how this fansplat is turning out. But if I may ask, has there been any ideas for Z Splats? I have one if there isn't any prior ones.<br /> <br /> Pretty much, some gods can lord over certain concepts that are really specific or cross into other Supernatural Territory. For example, Hecate is the Goddess of Witchcraft, Selene is a Goddess of the Moon, Melinoe is a Goddess of Undeath, so on and so forth. What I was thinking was the idea that the Z Splat could cover these really specific functions, being able to use special Domains that cross over into other supernatural thresholds and holding power there as well. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have... Ideas for the Z splat. I was thinking that it would effectively be a kind of solidification of the Empyrean's place in the divine, a kind of personal thing that allows the demigod almost truly divine power over a select purview, a kind of dominion-within-dominion. I was thinking that this might be where the 'rote' Miracles might come in, allowing the Demigod to draw on his power independent of the faith of mortals. These 'rotes' would all have to be within a reasonably small purview, smaller than a Dominion. Is that about what you were thinking?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't really have any ideas for the name of the Z Splat. Any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T13:58:00-07:00","id":884886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=884835#post884835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have... Ideas for the Z splat. I was thinking that it would effectively be a kind of solidification of the Empyrean's place in the divine, a kind of personal thing that allows the demigod almost truly divine power over a select purview, a kind of dominion-within-dominion. I was thinking that this might be where the 'rote' Miracles might come in, allowing the Demigod to draw on his power independent of the faith of mortals. These 'rotes' would all have to be within a reasonably small purview, smaller than a Dominion. Is that about what you were thinking?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't really have any ideas for the name of the Z Splat. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. It was kinda, to be honest I'm abit underread on this project so I don't have any further ideas. &gt;&lt;&quot; But yes, the ideas you brought up sound good. How does &quot;Creed&quot; sound as a name?<br /> <br /> As well, I was hoping to suggest two dominions if they're applicable: Time and Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T22:24:58-07:00","id":885166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=884886#post884886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. It was kinda, to be honest I'm abit underread on this project so I don't have any further ideas. &gt;&lt;&amp;quot; But yes, the ideas you brought up sound good. How does &amp;quot;Creed&amp;quot; sound as a name?<br /> <br /> As well, I was hoping to suggest two dominions if they're applicable: Time and Space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about Creed as a name, but Time and Space are certainly valid Domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T13:57:55-07:00","id":890776,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's the followings I've got so far (with help from the ever-wonderful <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"858\" data-vbnamecard=\"858\">Alastor</a>):<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of Reincarnates</b><br /> Believe that they are the reincarnations of ancient deities.<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of Heirs</b><br /> Believe that they are the creations of mankind's soul in order to fill the void of the either absent or nonexistent gods.<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of Sparks</b><br /> Believe that they are the creations of mankind's collective faith<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of Vassals</b><br /> Believe that they are the servants of a higher being (aka God/ess) on earth<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of Descendants</b><br /> Believe that they are heirs to a literal bloodline of divine beings from ages past (or more recent liaisons).<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of the Morningstar</b><br /> Believe that they are beings which fled a 'higher authority', be that God, the Demiurge or some kind of 'divine dictator' to Earth, encasing themselves in mortal flesh and suppressing their memories.<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of Embodiments</b><br /> Believe that demigods are a physical embodiment of their Purview, in a way similar to Spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>The Following of Ascendants</b><br /> Believe that demigods are the next step in humanity's journey towards a perfect being <br /> <br /> <b>The Following of the Nine Circles</b><br /> Believe that demigods are demons who have escaped Hell at the price of the majority of their identity and now have a chance to live free<br /> <br /> Any other ideas would be appreciated, particularly for more 'scientific' Followings.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:06:27-07:00","id":891540,"title":"","content":"I wasn't sure how to write the Summary Of Organisation, so I left that part out. I imagine that they are similar to the Union and the Night Watch at the local level, and more like the Barrett Commission and Utopia Now in the grand scale. <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Following Of Banners</u><br /> <br /> Short Description: </b>To be a God is to choose your People. They shall not be your enemies or slaves: they are your Family, and with your power and guidance, they will become the greatest of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Numinous Form: </b>Symbols of leadership and power are common, such as crowns, staffs and swords. Natural elements include flashy ones like fire and lightning, but also ones that represent abundance and wealth, like crystalline water, precious ores/gems and fruit-bearing plants. Imagine the Nimbus of an Obrimos or the Mien of a Fairest. When they are low on Potentia and/or the support of mortals, their symbols lose their spark. Swords become dull and rusty, fruits rot and attract flies, and their booming voices falter and stutter.<br /> <br /> <b>Common Domains:</b> Protection, Armaments, Conflict, Strategy, Loyalty, Technology, Fate, Fear","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T22:45:27-07:00","id":891591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891540#post891540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't sure how to write the Summary Of Organisation, so I left that part out. I imagine that they are similar to the Union and the Night Watch at the local level, and more like the Barrett Commission and Utopia Now in the grand scale. <br /> <br /> <b><u>The Following Of Banners</u><br /> <br /> Short Description: </b>To be a God is to choose your People. They shall not be your enemies or slaves: they are your Family, and with your power and guidance, they will become the greatest of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Numinous Form: </b>Symbols of leadership and power are common, such as crowns, staffs and swords. Natural elements include flashy ones like fire and lightning, but also ones that represent abundance and wealth, like crystalline water, precious ores/gems and fruit-bearing plants. Imagine the Nimbus of an Obrimos or the Mien of a Fairest. When they are low on Potentia and/or the support of mortals, their symbols lose their spark. Swords become dull and rusty, fruits rot and attract flies, and their booming voices falter and stutter.<br /> <br /> <b>Common Domains:</b> Protection, Armaments, Conflict, Strategy, Loyalty, Technology, Fate, Fear</div> </div> </div> </div>So - and forgive me if I've got the wrong end of the stick here - the Following of Banners believes that a demigod's power is rooted in humanity and that a demigod's duty is to lead humanity into a better world?<br /> <br /> For the summary of organization thing, I was just thinking stuff like do they have a hierarchy within the following? Is that hierarchy a feudal one, a theocracy or are they ruled by some kind of council? Do they actively attempt to cultivate cults (I'm thinking yes in this case) or do they attempt to withdraw from the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T23:53:51-07:00","id":891601,"title":"","content":"I had an idea: that as they grow in power, a demigod's Numinous Form becomes more and more like a true Ephemeral's. Mechanically, the Numinous Form would have a'default' Manifestation based on the demigod's Avatar. For lower levels (1-3), they would just have Materialized, for the middle ranges(4-7) they would be in Twilight Form but with Image active and in the higher levels (8-10) they have a full Twilight Form. In the Drasil , they would all be permanently Materialized.<br /> That way, you both reinforce the theme of the separation of the mundane and divine, make high-level demigod's cults all the more like real religions (you can't see your god, except when He lets you...) and solve the problem of why those gigantic god-monsters wandering around aren't noticed by (most) people.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that Demigods ought to have an honorary Rank, but I'm not quite sure how it would work.<br /> <br /> Finally, do you think there should be an upper limit on the number of Domains a demigod should have? It's just because I don't like the idea of a demigod having Water and Fire and Technology and War and a dozen other unconnected Domains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T04:20:34-07:00","id":891666,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Demigods evolving to become more like Ephemerals over time - it reinforces the idea of their distance from humanity. Maybe manifesting in the mundane world would be more difficult for Demigods with lower Attachment?<br /> <br /> I don't think that there should be a hard limit on the number of Domains a Demigod should be able to purchase. If you look at deities as they were worshipped historically, many of them have portfolios that are wide ranging &amp; conceptually diverse. Demigods should have the option to be the same way if they are willing to spend the requisite experience. Your recent idea for a Z type suggested that the Demigod becomes particularly specialized, with more control over one small sub-domain. Perhaps you could make the cost of such specialization a loss of the ability to branch into Domains which are unrelated to this focus. So a Demigod who is focused on Seaweed (just as an example) might have Domain points in Water or Plants, but they wouldn't be able to learn Leadership, at least not unless they come up with a convincing reason why this would relate back to Seaweed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T05:27:12-07:00","id":891676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891666#post891666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Demigods evolving to become more like Ephemerals over time - it reinforces the idea of their distance from humanity. Maybe manifesting in the mundane world would be more difficult for Demigods with lower Attachment?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I was going to do it was to have the Numinous Form have specific Manifestations which are always active. The Manifestations depend on your Avatar and, barring Miracles, <i>those are the Manifestations you get</i>. A demigod with Avatar 9 <i>will</i> have Twilight Form, not Image, not Possess, Twilight Form. If the Demigod has the Light Domain, he could create an illusion of himself that people can see, but it's a Miracle, not a Manifestation.<br /> An effect which I'm looking to add onto Attachment is how well a Demigod can control their impulses and emotions, with high attachment allowing more control, more human-ness, while low Attachment lets the demigod detach themselves better and act more as a divine being (although there's no guarantee that they'll be a nice one).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891666#post891666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that there should be a hard limit on the number of Domains a Demigod should be able to purchase. If you look at deities as they were worshipped historically, many of them have portfolios that are wide ranging &amp; conceptually diverse. Demigods should have the option to be the same way if they are willing to spend the requisite experience. Your recent idea for a Z type suggested that the Demigod becomes particularly specialized, with more control over one small sub-domain. Perhaps you could make the cost of such specialization a loss of the ability to branch into Domains which are unrelated to this focus. So a Demigod who is focused on Seaweed (just as an example) might have Domain points in Water or Plants, but they wouldn't be able to learn Leadership, at least not unless they come up with a convincing reason why this would relate back to Seaweed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I thought. The Domains will be quite expensive experience-wise anyway, so it shouldn't be too much of a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T10:33:33-07:00","id":891850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891591#post891591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So - and forgive me if I've got the wrong end of the stick here - the Following of Banners believes that a demigod's power is rooted in humanity and that a demigod's duty is to lead humanity into a better world?<br /> <br /> For the summary of organization thing, I was just thinking stuff like do they have a hierarchy within the following? Is that hierarchy a feudal one, a theocracy or are they ruled by some kind of council? Do they actively attempt to cultivate cults (I'm thinking yes in this case) or do they attempt to withdraw from the world?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, they know that they depend on humanity for more than just Potentia. The relationship can be pragmatic just as easily as passionate. Some go as far as to say that they are the best line of defense against any <b><a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaos_(cosmogony)\" target=\"_blank\">Chaoskampf</a></b> deities.<br /> <br /> They aren't a single group with a centralized leadership. It's a catch-all term. The Empyreans of this Following can be CEOs and mafia bosses as well as freedom fighters and civil rights activists. They tend toward high Attachment, of course, and they learn to use their powers strategically out of necessity. It should be noted that they are not immune to internal conflict or bad decisions, despite Halysis. I think there should be a Merit that lets you both gain and lose followers more quickly. This Following would let you buy that Merit at a reduced cost, or it might even come as a freebie.<br /> <br /> Don't feel restricted by the sample Numinous Forms and Domains. An Empyrean of Banners leading espionage missions against a dictatorship or hostile corporate takeover might look more like a Darkling or the Horror of an Ugallu/Eshmaki, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:24:08-07:00","id":891880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891850#post891850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This Following would let you buy that Merit at a reduced cost, or it might even come as a freebie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering having Followings grant things like this in a way similar to Hunter's Endowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:37:50-07:00","id":891888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891880#post891880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was considering having Followings grant things like this in a way similar to Hunter's Endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. However, I would not make any such Merits exclusive to a single Following, unless the Merit in question really clashed with the ideas of the other Followings. For the most part, I would give discounts and/or additional effects for the resonant Followings, in the style of Contracts in Changeling 2ED.<br /> <br /> As for the powers of the Numinous Form, I have to admit that the Demonic Forms and Atavisms already offer an excellent list of options. If we tried making a bunch of Empyrean ones, they would end up resembling the aforementioned powers. Korogra also wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities\"><b>a bunch of Angelic Form abilities.</b></a> We can also borrow Dread Powers and Cryptid Adaptations. We might need to do some re-fluffing and adjust the crunch, but that's it. No need to reinvent the wheel.<br /> <br /> Of note is how Atavisms work. Beasts have a smaller pool of Fuel points, so 1 Satiety might be worth 2 or 3 Potentia. What could be the &quot;Low Satiety&quot; equivalent of Empyreans? Or would they count as &quot;Low Satiety&quot; by default?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T11:46:51-07:00","id":891898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891888#post891888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the powers of the Numinous Form, I have to admit that the Demonic Forms and Atavisms already offer an excellent list of options. If we tried making a bunch of Empyrean ones, they would end up resembling the aforementioned powers. Korogra also wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities\"><b>a bunch of Angelic Form abilities.</b></a> We can also borrow Dread Powers and Cryptid Adaptations. We might need to do some re-fluffing and adjust the crunch, but that's it. No need to reinvent the wheel.<br /> <br /> Of note is how Atavisms work. Beasts have a smaller pool of Fuel points, so 1 Satiety might be worth 2 or 3 Potentia. What could be the &quot;Low Satiety&quot; equivalent of Empyreans? Or would they count as &quot;Low Satiety&quot; by default?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For the Numinous Form powers, I was just going to effectively do them as Dread Powers, with each having a 'dot rating'. Demigods have a pool of point determined by their Avatar which they can use to buy form traits and I was going to make it so that once bought, they can't usually be changed unless the demigod undergoes a profound change in the way they see the world (or raises or lowers their Avatar). The powers would probably do much of the same things as Atavisms, Demonic Form abilities and so on. One thing I was going to have, though, was that it is quite rare to have to spend Potentia to activate Numinous Form traits. They're kind of an integral part of the demigod, in much the same way as Atavisms don't require Satiety to be spent for most of their uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:09:58-07:00","id":891908,"title":"","content":"Has anyone got any ideas for breaking points on Attachment? Here's a short thing about them.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Falling Upwards</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breaking points towards humanity are usually actions which neglect the demigod\u2019s power and responsibilities for the sake of human concerns or companionship. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Leaving Mortality Behind</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breaking points towards the divine are usually caused by using divine power needlessly or the dismissal of consequences for the use of divine power. </span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:33:35-07:00","id":891925,"title":"","content":"I've (finally) added a few Numinous Form powers to the doc in the folder, as well as adding some stuff to Attachment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T12:54:04-07:00","id":891943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891908#post891908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone got any ideas for breaking points on Attachment? Here's a short thing about them.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Falling Upwards</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breaking points towards humanity are usually actions which neglect the demigod\u2019s power and responsibilities for the sake of human concerns or companionship. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Leaving Mortality Behind</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Breaking points towards the divine are usually caused by using divine power needlessly or the dismissal of consequences for the use of divine power. </span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div> It depends on how much you want to borrow from 2ED Harmony. In any case, Towards Mortal shouldn't be the same as &quot;good&quot; and Toward Godhood shouldn't be the same as &quot;evil&quot; (or vice-versa). There should be custom triggers in addition to a few baseline ones. Perhaps high Attachment requires you to spend Potentia for Numinous Form powers that are normally free?<br /> <br /> As a side note, what do Empyreans have in terms of magic items? Just about every god has an iconic object, from Zeus' thunderbolts to Thor's Mjolnir. In fact, Empyreans might have an inherent power like the Token Master and Token Maker Merits from Changeling 1ED. When they Ascend, an object dear to them takes on aspects of their Purview and Myth. As their Avatar increases, they can invest more objects with divine power. I'd say that the methods used in crafting these items should be closer to Hedgespinning than Gadget Installation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T13:07:19-07:00","id":891951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891943#post891943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It depends on how much you want to borrow from 2ED Harmony. In any case, Towards Mortal shouldn't be the same as &quot;good&quot; and Toward Godhood shouldn't be the same as &quot;evil&quot; (or vice-versa). There should be custom triggers in addition to a few baseline ones. Perhaps high Attachment requires you to spend Potentia for Numinous Form powers that are normally free?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean to put it like that, sorry. My intention was that breaking points towards humanity were essentially irresponsibility, acting in a way which rejects the divine half of the demigod while those towards the divine are acting in a way like the gods of myth, using your powers frivolously. that might not work, but oh well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=891943#post891943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, what do Empyreans have in terms of magic items? Just about every god has an iconic object, from Zeus' thunderbolts to Thor's Mjolnir. In fact, Empyreans might have an inherent power like the Token Master and Token Maker Merits from Changeling 1ED. When they Ascend, an object dear to them takes on aspects of their Purview and Myth. As their Avatar increases, they can invest more objects with divine power. I'd say that the methods used in crafting these items should be closer to Hedgespinning than Gadget Installation.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for this, one of the Numinous Form powers that I've written basically makes it so that when a demigod enters Numinous Form a magical item materialises which is imbued with Miraculous effects (the more dots you invest into an Icon, the more power(s) you can put in it). It can be stolen or given away though and others (even mortals can use it if they pay Willpower to do so. It might be better to make that a separate system like you suggested. I have to say that it would work rather well for a 'Miraculous Rotes' system. I'll consider that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 05-16-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:13:13-07:00","id":893460,"title":"","content":"Having considered it, Icons are now an individual subsystem to be fleshed out as soon as possible. the number of icons a demigod can possess as well as the dots of Miracles that can be imbued into them are under Avatar in the first post.<br /> <br /> Continuing this, how do you think the imbued Miracles should work? Should the demigod be able to change them easily, should it be an hour-long-ritual-per-dot-to-be-changed thing or should they be set in stone? BTW, the items which become Icons upon a demigod gaining extra Avatar would be in the control of the Storyteller. The first Icon is chosen by the player (although not the character).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:30:49-07:00","id":900206,"title":"","content":"An idea, which I want to make very clear is up for debate: How to cheat death as a demigod.<br /> <br /> My idea was that if a demigod dies, their primary Icon (the one with the most dots of Miracles imbued in it) becomes a vessel, of sorts, for their spirit (which may or may not be a conscious or semi-conscious entity, I've not decided yet) for a time (the time in question based upon how many dots of Miracles are in the Icon). It retains all other properties that it had before, including the ability to project the demigod's Halysis around it and perform Miracles, making it quite an attractive object in its own right.<br /> <br /> Basically, my idea was that if a person takes up the Icon, the further they get pulled into Halysis, the more the demigod's spirit becomes aware again and it slowly becomes able to influence the unfortunate who is in possession of the Icon. This process would be modelled with ephemeral Manifestations, at least partially. I'm thinking Urged at Halysis 3, temporary Possession at Halysis 4. Once the wielder reaches Halysis 5, the demigod becomes able to quasi-Claim them, taking over their body and warping it into the demigod's previous form. Doing this would be a <i>serious </i> breaking point towards low Attachment.<br /> <br /> A demigod can choose to pass on and not take another's life in place of their own, but they do have that option. As well as quite possibly a cult of people willing to become the demigod's 'avatar'.<br /> <br /> Anyway, does this sound like a thing that could work? Or not? Any thoughts? Advice? Denunciations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:34:50-07:00","id":900212,"title":"","content":"Maybe make that the &quot;easy&quot; way to resurrect, with a less immoral but much more costly &quot;hard option&quot;, like maybe destroying the primary Icon to create a body? Not sure if it's a good idea or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:47:26-07:00","id":900227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=900212#post900212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make that the &quot;easy&quot; way to resurrect, with a less immoral but much more costly &quot;hard option&quot;, like maybe destroying the primary Icon to create a body? Not sure if it's a good idea or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not destroying the primary Icon, but making it inoperable for an extended period of time? Like, a few weeks or longer, depending on the demigod's power (the higher, the longer)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:18:13-07:00","id":900295,"title":"","content":"Thre's been some significant additions to the Icons document. I haven't written up any of the rules for being 'reborn' through them, because I thought that some more discussion on that would be a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:43:10-07:00","id":900955,"title":"","content":"Icon's look pretty cool. :3 If I may ask, what do you mean by being &quot;reborn&quot; through them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:55:06-07:00","id":901034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=900955#post900955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Icon's look pretty cool. :3 If I may ask, what do you mean by being &quot;reborn&quot; through them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll quote myself here:<br /> <br /> My idea was that if a demigod dies, their primary Icon (the one with the most dots of Miracles imbued in it) becomes a vessel, of sorts, for their spirit (which may or may not be a conscious or semi-conscious entity, I've not decided yet) for a time (the time in question based upon how many dots of Miracles are in the Icon). It retains all other properties that it had before, including the ability to project the demigod's Halysis around it and perform Miracles, making it quite an attractive object in its own right.<br /> <br /> Basically, my idea was that if a person takes up the Icon, the further they get pulled into Halysis, the more the demigod's spirit becomes aware again and it slowly becomes able to influence the unfortunate who is in possession of the Icon. This process would be modelled with ephemeral Manifestations, at least partially. I'm thinking Urged at Halysis 3, temporary Possession at Halysis 4. Once the wielder reaches Halysis 5, the demigod becomes able to quasi-Claim them, taking over their body and warping it into the demigod's previous form. Doing this would be a <i>serious </i>breaking point towards low Attachment.<br /> <br /> A demigod can choose to pass on and not take another's life in place of their own, but they do have that option. As well as quite possibly a cult of people willing to become the demigod's 'avatar'.<br /> <br /> <br /> This has been partially revised, so that this is one way in which a demigod may reanimate. The others are to sacrifice their primary Icon (meaning that they have to make a new one, which is a difficult and costly process) or to give up all but 1 of their Avatar (this option is not open to demigods with Avatar 1). In order to take any course, the bearer of your primary Icon must reach at lest Halysis stage 3, as it is at that point where the demigod's 'spirit' becomes aware enough to make such decisions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:20:29-07:00","id":901123,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. I like how the &quot;Gods Need Prayer Badly&quot; is played out here. <br /> <br /> If I may suggest another way for Demigods to come back from the dead, I have an idea. What if they simply reincarnate themselves? Not as in &quot;start completely from scratch&quot;, but more that the Demigod retains all of their miracles, their Avatar rating (they might need to give up a point of Avatar to do this upon dying) and their mental and social skills and merits, but they lose all physical skills and merits? <br /> <br /> The reasoning for this idea is that there's many stories where a god incarnates themselves within a mortal (Jesus and Vishnu being two prominent examples) and retain their power and mental faculties. I think it's more prominent for Vishnu though.<br /> <br /> When it comes to being reborn through their Icon though, I like the idea. If I may suggest an idea that Touhou's used (Which also plays abit on &quot;Gods need prayer badly&quot;, at least in the cases of Kanako, Suwako and Sanae) three chars used a special sort of reanimation where they set an object (they used a vase, a plate and a sword respectively) to &quot;die&quot; in their place and they'd be reborn as immortals. It took more than a few centuries for reanimation to take place due to the ritual being messed with, and the ritual can be disrupted by destroying the object they set to die in their place. After returning to life, their dead body became the object they used, and the object they used became their new body.<br /> <br /> I don't know how this idea can be used or explained in mechanics, but I hope it could work for inspiration? Not to mention it adds in a small danger to the method. Hunters trying to stop a Demigod from coming back would need to keep an eye out for everything they could've stashed away in case if they died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:30:31-07:00","id":901137,"title":"","content":"&lt;removed by me&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T10:31:09-07:00","id":901140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=901123#post901123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see. I like how the &quot;Gods Need Prayer Badly&quot; is played out here.<br /> <br /> If I may suggest another way for Demigods to come back from the dead, I have an idea. What if they simply reincarnate themselves? Not as in &quot;start completely from scratch&quot;, but more that the Demigod retains all of their miracles, their Avatar rating (they might need to give up a point of Avatar to do this upon dying) and their mental and social skills and merits, but they lose all physical skills and merits?<br /> <br /> The reasoning for this idea is that there's many stories where a god incarnates themselves within a mortal (Jesus and Vishnu being two prominent examples) and retain their power and mental faculties. I think it's more prominent for Vishnu though.<br /> <br /> When it comes to being reborn through their Icon though, I like the idea. If I may suggest an idea that Touhou's used (Which also plays abit on &quot;Gods need prayer badly&quot;, at least in the cases of Kanako, Suwako and Sanae) three chars used a special sort of reanimation where they set an object (they used a vase, a plate and a sword respectively) to &quot;die&quot; in their place and they'd be reborn as immortals. It took more than a few centuries for reanimation to take place due to the ritual being messed with, and the ritual can be disrupted by destroying the object they set to die in their place. After returning to life, their dead body became the object they used, and the object they used became their new body.<br /> <br /> I don't know how this idea can be used or explained in mechanics, but I hope it could work for inspiration? Not to mention it adds in a small danger to the method. Hunters trying to stop a Demigod from coming back would need to keep an eye out for everything they could've stashed away in case if they died.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did consider that when a demigod comes back through someone else, they essentially replace the personality in that body while the body remains unchanged. So you would effectively be permanently possessing the new body, using its physical Attributes while keeping everything else. Would that work do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T11:12:12-07:00","id":901177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=901140#post901140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did consider that when a demigod comes back through someone else, they essentially replace the personality in that body while the body remains unchanged. So you would effectively be permanently possessing the new body, using its physical Attributes while keeping everything else. Would that work do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that'd work. <br /> <br /> Although I realize I misspoke. When I said &quot;reincarnate within a mortal&quot; I meant something more like &quot;Be reborn within a human female&quot; or something kinda of like the Virgin Mary. Pardon that. &gt;&gt;&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:24:46-07:00","id":902172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=901177#post901177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that'd work.<br /> <br /> Although I realize I misspoke. When I said &quot;reincarnate within a mortal&quot; I meant something more like &quot;Be reborn within a human female&quot; or something kinda of like the Virgin Mary. Pardon that. &gt;&gt;&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>With you having said that, I think that that might be what happens when a demigod uses a point of Avatar to reincarnate. Like, their Icon-bearer's next copulation will lead to a pregnancy which the demigod's consciousness occupies. The only problem with that is that it would take the demigod out of action for years on end unless they grow up unnaturally fast.<br /> <br /> On another note, I've been considering Purview and I think it might need to be retooled into something more specific and meaningful. As much as I like the idea of the X splat being what the demigod is a god of, the way it's done at the moment cheapens and trivialises it compared to other splats. At the moment it's little more than what kind of Miracles you're best at. What I'm thinking is keeping the name and using fairly wide concepts which Domains could be subsets of. A given Domain would almost certainly be featured in at least two Purviews. Here's the ones I've thought of so far as well as which Domains could be subordinate to them:<br /> <br /> <b>Creation -</b> Light, Fate, Animals, Plants, Emotions, Health, Water, Inspiration, Knowledge<br /> <br /> <b>Chaos -</b> Fire, War, Conflict, Deception, Air, Emotions, Darkness, Inspiration, Disease<br /> <br /> <b>Destruction -</b> Death, Cold, Darkness, Conflict, Water, Inspiration, Rot, Disease, Fate<br /> <br /> <b>Order -</b> Technology, Fate, Earth, Metal, Death, Cold, Knowledge, Light, Water, Health","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:27:15-07:00","id":902174,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that none of these would be 'evil' or 'good'. You could just as easily create a hurricane as bestow a blessing on someone and I think that you might be somewhat more thanked for destroying a malicious ghost or spirit than imposing a clockwork order onto others. <br /> <br /> P.S. Anyone else see the Order guys getting involved with the G-M?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:40:19-07:00","id":902183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902172#post902172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With you having said that, I think that that might be what happens when a demigod uses a point of Avatar to reincarnate. Like, their Icon-bearer's next copulation will lead to a pregnancy which the demigod's consciousness occupies. The only problem with that is that it would take the demigod out of action for years on end unless they grow up unnaturally fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even at a young age, the avatars of some things still had great wisdom or the like. I was thinking that in reincarnating, the Demigod regains all of their memories from the moment they're born.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902172#post902172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, I've been considering Purview and I think it might need to be retooled into something more specific and meaningful. As much as I like the idea of the X splat being what the demigod is a god of, the way it's done at the moment cheapens and trivialises it compared to other splats. At the moment it's little more than what kind of Miracles you're best at. What I'm thinking is keeping the name and using fairly wide concepts which Domains could be subsets of. A given Domain would almost certainly be featured in at least two Purviews. Here's the ones I've thought of so far as well as which Domains could be subordinate to them:<br /> <br /> <b>Creation -</b> Light, Fate, Animals, Plants, Emotions, Health, Water, Inspiration, Knowledge<br /> <br /> <b>Chaos -</b> Fire, War, Conflict, Deception, Air, Emotions, Darkness, Inspiration, Disease<br /> <br /> <b>Destruction -</b> Death, Cold, Darkness, Conflict, Water, Inspiration, Rot, Disease, Fate<br /> <br /> <b>Order -</b> Technology, Fate, Earth, Metal, Death, Cold, Knowledge, Light, Water, Health</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, this looks well done. I must say though that there's a couple of things I find weird, if only in placement of Purview. It seems that a few Domains are listed in the same Purviews. Is this intentional? Otherwise, I like the idea for these Purviews. :3<br /> <br /> If it's not minded, I think Time and Space were fitting for Domains? Would they fit in Order and Creation (Time) and Chaos and Destruction (Space) respectively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:47:37-07:00","id":902187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902183#post902183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even at a young age, the avatars of some things still had great wisdom or the like. I was thinking that in reincarnating, the Demigod regains all of their memories from the moment they're born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, i was thinking that too (otherwise it wouldn't be much of a reincarnation) but they're still stuck in a baby-body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902183#post902183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, this looks well done. I must say though that there's a couple of things I find weird, if only in placement of Purview. It seems that a few Domains are listed in the same Purviews. Is this intentional? Otherwise, I like the idea for these Purviews. :3<br /> <br /> If it's not minded, I think Time and Space were fitting for Domains? Would they fit in Order and Creation (Time) and Chaos and Destruction (Space) respectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, some Domains were intended to be in more than one Purview. As for the Time and Space, I would have put Time in Order and Destruction (for time marching ever onwards and old age respectively) and put Space in Order and Chaos (the former for the sensible-ness and the latter for the chaos messing with it would cause). I've probably done my thing where I think something and assume I've said it, but I was thinking of having Domains as being much like Influences in that you can essentially make them up, provided the Storyteller says they're OK. I'll ahve to go back and edit the first post to put that in, if I don't get any cries of &quot;No, how could you?!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T12:10:01-07:00","id":902207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902187#post902187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, i was thinking that too (otherwise it wouldn't be much of a reincarnation) but they're still stuck in a baby-body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing a Miracle of Life or using a Domain to fashion a body to act for you can't fix? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902187#post902187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, some Domains were intended to be in more than one Purview. As for the Time and Space, I would have put Time in Order and Destruction (for time marching ever onwards and old age respectively) and put Space in Order and Chaos (the former for the sensible-ness and the latter for the chaos messing with it would cause). I've probably done my thing where I think something and assume I've said it, but I was thinking of having Domains as being much like Influences in that you can essentially make them up, provided the Storyteller says they're OK. I'll ahve to go back and edit the first post to put that in, if I don't get any cries of &quot;No, how could you?!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, that sounds fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T14:13:41-07:00","id":902281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902207#post902207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing a Miracle of Life or using a Domain to fashion a body to act for you can't fix? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just prefer to have it as one self-contained system. Sin-Eaters don't have to use a special Ceremony to reanimate. On the other hand, it would be reasonably in-theme to have them just grow up really quickly. In a lot of the 'avatar' myths, the hero often grows to maturity or at least an age at which he can fight extremely quickly, most notably in some Aztec and Greek myths. Maybe demigods who 'reincarnate' age to maturity at about 3-4 times as fast? Although I have to say that the idea of despotic child-gods reminds me a great deal of teh Goa'uld from Stargate, who, incidentally, are excellent examples of demigods gone bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=902207#post902207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, that sounds fitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll have a go at the first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:35:30-07:00","id":903984,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a>: I like that you're trying to give more depth to the Purviews. Perhaps you could draw inspiration from Jungian Archetypes and Tarot? Or would that step too much into Mage territory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:51:28-07:00","id":903993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=903984#post903984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>: I like that you're trying to give more depth to the Purviews. Perhaps you could draw inspiration from Jungian Archetypes and Tarot? Or would that step too much into Mage territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Tarot would, but oblique references to the Jungian archetypes would certainly work, I think. I'm thinking of putting them in a bit like Mage does with its necromancers and theurgists and Enchanters and so on. What archetypes would work for each, do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T23:57:03-07:00","id":903998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=903993#post903993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that the Tarot would, but oblique references to the Jungian archetypes would certainly work, I think. I'm thinking of putting them in a bit like Mage does with its necromancers and theurgists and Enchanters and so on. What archetypes would work for each, do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div> There should be one for Tricksters and Fools, that's for sure. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T00:17:01-07:00","id":904004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=903998#post903998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There should be one for Tricksters and Fools, that's for sure. </div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos would definitely be the Trickster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T00:21:47-07:00","id":904006,"title":"","content":"Creation might be the Mother, the Father or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T01:25:15-07:00","id":906280,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about it and I think that Avatar is the wrong name for the power stat. It doesn't work like all the others, where you can say a mage's Gnosis or a Promethean's Azoth. It has to be an Avatar <i>rating </i> and that doesn't sit right with me. Besides that, it doesn't capture the image I was after for the essence of a demigod.<br /> <br /> The idea was that their power stat represents what was once their soul, now transformed into a gateway through which the divine essence flows to permeate the body and mind. Ultimately, demigods are just as inhuman as Beasts when it comes to their soul. Beasts have a nightmare Horror and its Lair while demigods have a luminous hole, a gateway to the center of everything, where possibility lives and through which that possibility can shine out into the world.<br /> <br /> They feel it like a cold star in their chests, a fire that does not burn pouring the white light of divinity into their hearts and minds. As Attachment lowers, the star burns brighter and brighter, its light eclipsing the rest of the world. As Attachment grows, the light lessens, the base matter of the world dimming it until it seems to gutter out entirely (at Attachment 10).<br /> <br /> I thought that maybe Transcendence or Luminance could work, but I'd welcome any suggestions that people have.<br /> <br /> On another note, I'm working on collating 'Avatar', Attachment, Potentia, Icon and integral powers into one document on the GDrive page, named 'Special Systems. It's still very much a work in progress though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T01:44:50-07:00","id":906283,"title":"","content":"Divinum - Meaning both Divinity and Offering in Latin? Perhaps Caelum, the latin derivative of Celestial? Mind, couldn't find any good english words better than what you have there but these things have a nice sound to them IMO (course, my sound for them is probably not how they are pronounced given I never studied latin, but hey what can you do? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> Astra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T02:01:02-07:00","id":906287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=906283#post906283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divinum - Meaning both Divinity and Offering in Latin? Perhaps Caelum, the latin derivative of Celestial? Mind, couldn't find any good english words better than what you have there but these things have a nice sound to them IMO (course, my sound for them is probably not how they are pronounced given I never studied latin, but hey what can you do? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> Astra?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Caelum and Astra are both nice. Latin is always good when you're dealing with stuff like this. Gives it a nice magic-ey feeling. Thanks for helping. Ahhhhhhh! Decisions, decisions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T04:04:56-07:00","id":906310,"title":"","content":"If anyone would like to chip in, some examples for Miracles would be welcome. Pick whatever Domain you like and have some fun! If there are any problems in the rules or if you're not sure whether a given Miracle would be of this tier or another, just ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T04:07:50-07:00","id":906313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=906283#post906283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divinum - Meaning both Divinity and Offering in Latin? Perhaps Caelum, the latin derivative of Celestial? Mind, couldn't find any good english words better than what you have there but these things have a nice sound to them IMO (course, my sound for them is probably not how they are pronounced given I never studied latin, but hey what can you do? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> Astra?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In relation to this, I found something that might work. Adstrum is Latin for constellation, glory, immortality, star and heaven sounds bout right to me. I admit, though, that this is running off of Google Translate and I'm no Latin-speaker. If anyone is and could set me right on this or if I'm doing something completely screwy or weird with the language, just tell me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T05:59:36-07:00","id":907581,"title":"","content":"OK, random antagonist/possible ally/wibbly thing. <br /> <br /> As I was looking up a bunch of occult stuff to do with temples, cults, orders and so on, I came across a concept called an 'egregore' or 'egregor', meaning 'watcher' in greek. The idea is that the collective will and being of a group can manifest and become a being in its own right, a being that watches over its creators. In the CoD, these egregores exist as beings of ephemera. For the most part, they sleep, much like an unawakened spirit with the exception that not all unawakened egregore are weak like Muthrum. In order to awaken and become more than just the feeling you get when you enter a corporate building or a slogan, meme or symbol, to become a being in their own right, a touch of the divine is needed, and provided in the form of Temples. <br /> <br /> If an egregore can feed off of the Potentia that leaks into Temples from the Drasil, it can become a true being, able to think, reason and, to an extent, act. An awakened egregore would be modelled with the ephemeral beings rules but in comparison to other ephemerals such as angels, ghosts or spirits, has little direct power. All egregore can only use whatever powers they might have upon one who lets them in by acknowledging and believing in them or what they stand for. An egregore born from the collective identity of a small town's churchgoers can only use its Influences or Numina upon its parishioners. They would have little in the way of direct Manifestations either, the closest they would likely get to a Materialisation would likely be Image. They would probably be able to Possess or Claim those under their aegis, though. they would have quite a lot of indirect power, most likely more Influences than other beings, comparatively.<br /> <br /> I thought the concept would make an interesting counterpoint to the way that demigods create cults, as opposed to egregores being created by their cults. Beyond that, they would give a Storyteller more to work with in the way of antagonists in the phenomenal world. Plus, they'd naturally be really quite good at opposing demigod cults through their subordinates.<br /> <br /> On another note, I've been considering removing Gigantes and Enkidu,as they don't really seem to fit in their current form. I'm not sure about this, but I know that I don't like them as they are at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":