onto yourself while they yet live?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:42:51-07:00","id":915851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=915845#post915845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only complaint with the movie (from what I've seen) is that none of the actors look Egyptian. &gt;x3<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, it could work. Although would you be able to graft another god's powers onto yourself while they yet live?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not their powers as such, but you could certainly use their Icons and the Miracles imbued therein. If Horus' eyes were Icons (which could work), Set could steal them and use their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:57:16-07:00","id":915861,"title":"","content":"Because of the way that (I think) Icons are going to work, they are at once a great strength and an equally great weakness. You can use Imbued Miracles much more easily and cheaply than doing it without, but it also presents a vulnerability, in that Icons can be stolen and used by others. If you go and put a really powerful Miracle into an Icon and show it off, be prepared for people to try and pinch it. Even mortals can use Icons, to an extent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T11:37:46-07:00","id":916343,"title":"","content":"I've added a new type of Miracles, Incarnation Miracles. These allow the demigod to transform themselves, becoming a part of their Domain. For example, a demigod with the Animal domain could turn into an animal, while one with the Domain of Water could melt into a river and emerge elsewhere along its course or simply remain within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T03:26:07-07:00","id":916755,"title":"","content":"Here's a new and improved Antagonists section, which has been added to the first post as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Gigantes</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Gigantes are those demigods who have lost all connection to the mortal world and, having no human nature to shield them from the demands of their Aspect, have become its avatars, acting out its agenda in the world with no regard for the wants or lives of others. They are powerful and unpredictable beings, the only certainty in their behaviour is that they are always working towards their Aspect. Destroyers destroy, creators create, chaotes bring chaos and the lords of order seek to build monuments to their glory and make the world a clockwork paradise.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Typhons</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Should a demigod become too attached to his human life, however, his two natures will find themselves unable to reconcile in any fashion and will tear a \u2018rift\u2019 of sorts within the demigod\u2019s mind and Luminance. Not unlike multiple personality disorder, becoming a Typhon splits the personality of a demigod, often into three parts. One personality is, to all intents and purposes, mortal, having no supernatural abilities or memories of his activities as a demigod. Another is a \u2018pure\u2019 demigod, not unlike a Gigante and holds the demigod\u2019s Luminance and powers.<br /> The last one seems to be an entirely new personality, created at the moment of the split. To those who can perceive auras, it is obvious when this personality is in control, as instead of the blinding radiance of a demigod\u2019s aura or the human aura of the mortal personality, the aura of the aptly-named \u2018Hollow\u2019 personality is like a black hole, consuming any supernatural energies near it, especially Potentia. It can leech the magical fuel straight from the bodies of demigods, Teras, or even creatures like werewolves or mages and has its own powers based on the rejection of reality and the nihilistic urges to which the Hollow is slaved.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <b>Teras or Titanspawn</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> Populating the Drasil are countless outlandish creatures, seemingly sprang straight from myth and legend, from chimeras to dragons to dwarves to evil spirits. While not all are malicious, many are and take great delight in making mischief for Empyrean visitors. Many claim Gardr of their won and a few have even set up their own petty kingdoms in the branches of the Great Tree, populated with human slaves taken from the phenomenal world or by lesser races such as dwarves or gremlins.<br /> While few Teras have the ability to enter the phenomenal world, those who can are greatly valued and are often vicious creatures more than capable of creating havoc in the phenomenal world for the short duration of their stay. Fortunately for the mortals populating the physical world, no Teras can regain Essence to sustain themselves there with ease, being forced to steal it from others or from demigods.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Titans</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> In the branches of the Great Tree, hidden away in dark corners and upon the furthest reaches, sometimes one can find what seem to be cages or prisons grown out of the Tree itself, the bars (or ropes or chains) so numerous and close together that one can scarcely see between them. Should you try, though, you might catch a glimpse of something inside, writhing and beating at the walls of its prison or perhaps attempting to wrench its way out of its mummifying chains.<br /> These are the so-called Titans, fragments of primordial gods who were defeated and shattered by the first gods of humanity. Or so some say. Others say that these \u2018shards\u2019 are in fact the gods birthed by the hopes and fears of Neanderthals and early humanity, thus explaining why they seem to have, for all their power, so little understanding of the world around them.<br /> When a rare Titan manages to escape its bonds, they bring ruin with them. Each Titan embodies a single thing, whether water or storms or fire or fury or war and possesses and aura of sorts which imposes its nature on the world around it. Where a Titan of storms walks, hurricanes and tornadoes follow. When a Titan of fire is abroad, the world burns. They have almost absolute control over their purview and, perhaps most terrifyingly of all, can enter the mortal world, should they think to attempt it. One thing common to all Titans is that they are almost childlike, with an enormous curiosity for the world around them. Many simply wish to see and experience what is, but bring destruction by their presence. Few understand that they are actually hurting people or things with their strange Miracles. Some demigods even say that they try to help people, not comprehending that burning or drowning hem harms them.<br /> In a way, Titans are pitiable, but that does not make them any less powerful or dangerous. Even the greatest of demigods would have little chance to defeat a Titan on their own, let alone kill one. In fact, no method has been discovered to permanently destroy them. If their bodies are killed, they simply reform in their prisons.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <b>Egregores</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <br /> In the study of the occult, an egregore is a thoughtform, a \u2018being\u2019 of sorts created from the will and collective identity of a group. In fact, it would not be incorrect to say that it <i>is </i>the will of a group, in the same way that if a country was attacked, it would be the will of the country to retaliate.<br /> In the World of Darkness, these strange quasi-beings do exist, but for the most part are \u2018asleep\u2019, so to speak, inseparable from the will that spawned them. Should a nascent egregore find itself able to feed upon the Potentia that gathers in Temples, though, they can become something more. They awake and become able to think, reason, consider and, to an extent, act. An awakened egregore is, in a way, similar to other ephemeral beings such as angels, ghosts or spirits, but has little direct power. What power they have can only be used upon those who acknowledge or are a part of the group which spawned the egregore. An egregore born from the collective identity of a small town's churchgoers can only use its Influences or Numina upon its parishioners. They would have little in the way of direct Manifestations either, with the closest they would likely get to a Materialisation being the Image Manifestation. They are able to Possess or Claim those under their aegis and many are more than cunning enough to use the powers they have to strengthen their organisation and therefore increase their influence and power.<br /> The interests of egregore and demigods align as much as they are at odds depending on the organisations that the egregore is the patron for. An egregore of a demigod\u2019s own cult is significantly more likely to work with him than that of an opposing cult or a major corporation. One perennial source of conflict is over the Temples that both egregore and demigods covet; as it is rare that both can draw from a single source without quickly damaging or destroying it.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <b>Other Demigods</b><br /> <br /> <b>Hunters</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T14:56:46-07:00","id":916993,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on the revised antagonists? I think that the titans will need to be revised somewhat to make them more universally useful for story construction. Do you think that Typhons are OK? I might alter the demigod personality so that it's closer to how the demigod was before. That way you can have a demigod go quietly mad and spring the Hollow, psychotic personality on the players to give it more of an impact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:54:54-07:00","id":918230,"title":"","content":"Here's a new Following for you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Following of the Annunaki</u></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adherents to this Following believes that demigods are the heirs to an ancient bloodline or psychic inheritance implanted in humanity in the ancient past by some race of higher beings. The exact nature of these beings varies from demigod to demigod. Some believe that they were a hyper-advanced race of aliens, others that they were angels or some other kind of divine being, but the core tenet of the Following is that demigodhood is not natural but rather an engineered state, in some way. What demigods do with this belief is also extremely varied. Some seek to propagate this \u2018bloodline\u2019 physically, often making use of their cults to do so, while others believe that the conditions which allow Ascension are instead mental and seek to spread this through teaching. Some believe that the \u2018bloodline\u2019 was a failed experiment or perhaps a deliberate curse upon humanity, given the drawbacks of the Empyrean state. These often try to prevent the spread of what they see as a plague or destructive meme. More intellectually minded Followers often try to isolate the specific causes of Ascension, whether that be a gene, metaphysical markers, or a psychological state.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a consequence of their divided opinions, the Following of the Annunaki is at once organised and fractious. Groups of adherents often form cliques and factions based on their personal positions, gathering like-minded individuals and conflicting with those who oppose their views, sometimes with direct violence, sometimes in debate. These organisations vary in their structure according to their tenets as well, with those who strongly believe that Ascension is a blessing or curse often forming cultlike institutions dedicated to propagating or stymieing it, while those who wish to investigate it tend towards the more scientific structures, where each demigod investigates a different facet of the conundrum.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In their Numinous Forms, the Followers of the Annunaki tend towards the enormous shapes purported to have been worn by the ancient beings which their revere or despise. They often bear little in the way of flashy magical accoutrements and lean towards the physical, expressing their might with wings, claws and bulging muscles while their minds are augmented by elongated craniums and oversized brains.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Domains, the Followers of the Annunaki often rule over similar concepts to those which their legendary \u2018ancestors\u2019 taught to early humankind, such as Law, Civilisation, Craftsmanship and Stone. Occasionally they command physical forces of nature such as the seas or the skies, but rarely do they hold power over ephemeral concepts such as death or life. This Following is profoundly rooted in the physical.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T04:56:54-07:00","id":934998,"title":"","content":"The most recent changes look pretty good for the most part. I like the rules for Icons (although I'm not entirely sure how crafting new ones is supposed to work).<br /> <br /> Since the rules for Miracles are based on Influence, do you think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> 's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/742772-i-ve-got-nobilis-3e-on-my-mind\">Dharmas and Influences</a> (which I know of thanks to the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages\">Influenced-based mages</a>&quot; thread) might have some useful ideas to appropriate? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8802-new-system-organization-rules-cults-conspiracies-orders-and-covenants\">Organization Rules </a> also has a few elements that might combine well with the Cult system you're using.<br /> <br /> Since the X-types are now Creator, Destroyer, Chaotes, and Lords of Order and the Z-types are associations with particular areas of influence, where does alliegance to a particular religious tradition come in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T05:36:06-07:00","id":935007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=934998#post934998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most recent changes look pretty good for the most part. I like the rules for Icons (although I'm not entirely sure how crafting new ones is supposed to work).<br /> <br /> Since the rules for Miracles are based on Influence, do you think <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> 's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/742772-i-ve-got-nobilis-3e-on-my-mind&amp;quot;]Dharmas</a> and Influences[/URL] (which I know of thanks to the &amp;quot;<a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/916338-minor-template-influence-based-mages&amp;quot;]Influenced-based</a> mages[/URL]&amp;quot; thread) might have some useful ideas to appropriate? <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8802-new-system-organization-rules-cults-conspiracies-orders-and-covenants&amp;quot;]Organization</a> Rules [/URL] also has a few elements that might combine well with the Cult system you're using.<br /> <br /> Since the X-types are now Creator, Destroyer, Chaotes, and Lords of Order and the Z-types are associations with particular areas of influence, where does alliegance to a particular religious tradition come in?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the crafting icons thing, I'm not entirely sure myself. I like the idea of some kind of ritual or something, requiring an investiture of potentia and a dot of Willpower at least.<br /> <br /> For the 'religious traditions thing, that's what a Following is and has always been. If you're talking about an attachment to particular mortal faiths, that's a personal, non-mechanical thing, except for the purposes of harvesting Potentia from Temples that you haven't spent merit dots on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T08:53:18-07:00","id":935088,"title":"","content":"I must admit, I like how the antagonists are coming out. Good job. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:44:16-07:00","id":935102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935088#post935088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit, I like how the antagonists are coming out. Good job. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Any areas where you think they could be improved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T10:04:36-07:00","id":935111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935102#post935102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. Any areas where you think they could be improved?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. :3 I can't think of any improvements, but I was sort of wondering in the case of Teras/Titanspawn, given that they feed off of essence. Would it perhaps be possible for a Demigod to potentially feed one Potentia and potentially befriend it, kind of like how a person tries to get a pet? That's just an idea that popped up in my head that I personally find interesting.<br /> <br /> I also wonder about Titans, how were they all tied up in the first place? <br /> <br /> Perhaps as a final thought on my end, I sorta noticed that Enkidus are in the Obselete folder in the Google Drive. Are they being taken out of the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:23:19-07:00","id":935154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935111#post935111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're welcome. :3 I can't think of any improvements, but I was sort of wondering in the case of Teras/Titanspawn, given that they feed off of essence. Would it perhaps be possible for a Demigod to potentially feed one Potentia and potentially befriend it, kind of like how a person tries to get a pet? That's just an idea that popped up in my head that I personally find interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. There's going to be a Merit for that, kind of like a Hedgebeast from Changeling. However, you're going to need to feed it regularly or it'll most likely take what it wants. Also, Teras have a... compulsion, I guess, to obey Titans, although it can be resisted. It's not quite a Ban, but its similar. It takes a great deal of loyalty, willpower and/or love to counteract that. Also, bear in mind that many Titanspawn are as sentient and unique as you or I. There are brutish monsters, but more than a few are just people, created slaves to the Titans who must feed on potentia. That's not to say that they're all 'just misunderstood' (a lot of them really <i>are</i> monsters which delight in suffering). I'm thinking about making them a full minor splat. Maybe even playable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935111#post935111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder about Titans, how were they all tied up in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>That, along with what/who they are, where they come from, the origins of the Drasil and the power of demigods, is one of the big mysteries of Demigod, and the answer (or at least <i>my </i>answer) will be put up in a Deep Meta document. That kind of question is of the same order as 'what makes a vampire a vampire?' and 'what was Father/Mother Wolf?'. So no offense, ut i'll be keeping that particular card to my chest for a while longer. Suffice to say that their 'imprisonment' is not as it seems to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935111#post935111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps as a final thought on my end, I sorta noticed that Enkidus are in the Obselete folder in the Google Drive. Are they being taken out of the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they are. Seeing as Gigantes, Teras and Titanspawn have all been greatly changed, the Enkidu didn't seem to work very well with them. If you can see a way to integrate them or an edited version of them, feel free but I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T12:10:55-07:00","id":935183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935154#post935154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. There's going to be a Merit for that, kind of like a Hedgebeast from Changeling. However, you're going to need to feed it regularly or it'll most likely take what it wants. Also, Teras have a... compulsion, I guess, to obey Titans, although it can be resisted. It's not quite a Ban, but its similar. It takes a great deal of loyalty, willpower and/or love to counteract that. Also, bear in mind that many Titanspawn are as sentient and unique as you or I. There are brutish monsters, but more than a few are just people, created slaves to the Titans who must feed on potentia. That's not to say that they're all 'just misunderstood' (a lot of them really <i>are</i> monsters which delight in suffering). I'm thinking about making them a full minor splat. Maybe even playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That's pretty cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When I was making the post, I was kinda focusing more on the &quot;mythical animal monster&quot; than anything else, but I do understand that they can be sapient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935154#post935154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, along with what/who they are, where they come from, the origins of the Drasil and the power of demigods, is one of the big mysteries of Demigod, and the answer (or at least <i>my </i>answer) will be put up in a Deep Meta document. That kind of question is of the same order as 'what makes a vampire a vampire?' and 'what was Father/Mother Wolf?'. So no offense, ut i'll be keeping that particular card to my chest for a while longer. Suffice to say that their 'imprisonment' is not as it seems to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>None taken, I don't mind the secrets. :3 <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935154#post935154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they are. Seeing as Gigantes, Teras and Titanspawn have all been greatly changed, the Enkidu didn't seem to work very well with them. If you can see a way to integrate them or an edited version of them, feel free but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. I was kind of thinking of how most splats have a sort of sub-splat special to them, such as Ghouls for Vampires, Sleepwalkers/Proximi for Mages, Wolf-Blooded for Werewolves etc, I saw how Demigods seem to lack that, and was thinking of how Enkidu sounds like a good idea for a Demigod Subsplat. The reasoning for this is (how I see it if it's not correct) how most subsplats can be used as a link to humanity, as potential helpers in things and the like, and the naming being based off of the man who was able to make a jerkass demigod back into a good person again. <br /> <br /> I was just thinking given the relationship between Gilgamesh and Enkidu, if we replace &quot;Gilgamesh&quot; with &quot;Demigod&quot;, I think that Enkidus could potentially be a good idea for a subsplat. Although it might require some changes on them, most likely by making a Demigod be able to make someone have a piece of Potentia and perhaps be deeply connected to the Demigod too. What do you think on these ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:11:35-07:00","id":935222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935183#post935183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. I was kind of thinking of how most splats have a sort of sub-splat special to them, such as Ghouls for Vampires, Sleepwalkers/Proximi for Mages, Wolf-Blooded for Werewolves etc, I saw how Demigods seem to lack that, and was thinking of how Enkidu sounds like a good idea for a Demigod Subsplat. The reasoning for this is (how I see it if it's not correct) how most subsplats can be used as a link to humanity, as potential helpers in things and the like, and the naming being based off of the man who was able to make a jerkass demigod back into a good person again.<br /> <br /> I was just thinking given the relationship between Gilgamesh and Enkidu, if we replace &quot;Gilgamesh&quot; with &quot;Demigod&quot;, I think that Enkidus could potentially be a good idea for a subsplat. Although it might require some changes on them, most likely by making a Demigod be able to make someone have a piece of Potentia and perhaps be deeply connected to the Demigod too. What do you think on these ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the ideas are really good. I'm just not sure how to implement them. I think that the Enkidu - how you're suggesting them - would make an excellent anchor and would help me counteract one of the problems I always seem to have in writing: losing sight of the people for the cool powers. It''s the problem i had with Dragon: the Hunted. The dragons became so disconnected from people and humans that they just wouldn't be an interesting thing to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:40:38-07:00","id":935268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935222#post935222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the ideas are really good. I'm just not sure how to implement them. I think that the Enkidu - how you're suggesting them - would make an excellent anchor and would help me counteract one of the problems I always seem to have in writing: losing sight of the people for the cool powers. It''s the problem i had with Dragon: the Hunted. The dragons became so disconnected from people and humans that they just wouldn't be an interesting thing to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like them. :3 I'm not sure on implementation either, but I have some other ideas that I hope helps bring something to mind. All in all, my ideas so far are the idea of making Enkidu's an almost living humanizing aspect for the Demigods that keep them grounded. From what I'm reading on Attachment, Enkidus could help keep a Demigod at Attachment 4-6. Losing an Enkidu is prolly definitely a Breaking Point, hence making them both a boon and weakness to a Demigod. I also imagine that any attempt for a Demigod to use a Miracle that would damage their Enkidu would automatically fail. If they have anything they're fighting over, they're practically forced to do it mundanely.<br /> <br /> I'm also imagining in terms of meta, an Enkidu and Demigod are connected at the soul. <br /> <br /> Basing off of the Epic of Gilgamesh abit more, the only ideas I have on Enkidus is that they have enough power to match a Demigod (at least the one they're linked to in the first place, just to fit how Gil and Enkidu were able to kick the crap out of each other and it ended with a draw). They aren't capable of using Miracles on their own, but they are capable of acting as a Secondary Actor to the Demigod for doing Miracles or in some way boosting their rolls. I imagine they could use Icons as easily as the Demigod they belong to and may spend Potentia for them. <br /> <br /> When it comes to Luminance or Potentia, let's say Enkidus either have Luminance equal to the Demigod they're connected to and may use Potentia for Eternal Flesh. They only face penalties for spending Potentia if the Demigod they're connected to suffers from it, but it is possible for the Enkidu to pay the Potentia upkeep. Although this idea might be complicated, since it means that the Demigod and Enkidu share the Luminance as a Supernatural Advantage (on the Enkidu's end it's more limited) but it also means the Demigod and Enkidu have their own Potentia pools.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? I hope I'm not being too complicated in ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T14:47:47-07:00","id":935273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935268#post935268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad you like them. :3 I'm not sure on implementation either, but I have some other ideas that I hope helps bring something to mind. All in all, my ideas so far are the idea of making Enkidu's an almost living humanizing aspect for the Demigods that keep them grounded. From what I'm reading on Attachment, Enkidus could help keep a Demigod at Attachment 4-6. Losing an Enkidu is prolly definitely a Breaking Point, hence making them both a boon and weakness to a Demigod. I also imagine that any attempt for a Demigod to use a Miracle that would damage their Enkidu would automatically fail. If they have anything they're fighting over, they're practically forced to do it mundanely.<br /> <br /> I'm also imagining in terms of meta, an Enkidu and Demigod are connected at the soul. <br /> <br /> Basing off of the Epic of Gilgamesh abit more, the only ideas I have on Enkidus is that they have enough power to match a Demigod (at least the one they're linked to in the first place, just to fit how Gil and Enkidu were able to kick the crap out of each other and it ended with a draw). They aren't capable of using Miracles on their own, but they are capable of acting as a Secondary Actor to the Demigod for doing Miracles or in some way boosting their rolls. I imagine they could use Icons as easily as the Demigod they belong to and may spend Potentia for them. <br /> <br /> When it comes to Luminance or Potentia, let's say Enkidus either have Luminance equal to the Demigod they're connected to and may use Potentia for Eternal Flesh. They only face penalties for spending Potentia if the Demigod they're connected to suffers from it, but it is possible for the Enkidu to pay the Potentia upkeep. Although this idea might be complicated, since it means that the Demigod and Enkidu share the Luminance as a Supernatural Advantage (on the Enkidu's end it's more limited) but it also means the Demigod and Enkidu have their own Potentia pools.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts? I hope I'm not being too complicated in ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, most of it sounds quite good. Perhaps Enkidu cannot use Miracles save through Icons but have a kind of quasi Numinous Form? The Second Actor thing would definitely be an interesting idea. Perhaps Enkidu can 'channel' a demigod's Miracles? Or sort of 'hijack' them? I don't know.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've added a new thing on the first post: Demigod Images. It's full of links to pictures and stuff that I think fit. If anyone has any suggestions, post a link here and I'll see about putting it there as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:26:54-07:00","id":935344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=935273#post935273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, most of it sounds quite good. Perhaps Enkidu cannot use Miracles save through Icons but have a kind of quasi Numinous Form? The Second Actor thing would definitely be an interesting idea. Perhaps Enkidu can 'channel' a demigod's Miracles? Or sort of 'hijack' them? I don't know.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've added a new thing on the first post: Demigod Images. It's full of links to pictures and stuff that I think fit. If anyone has any suggestions, post a link here and I'll see about putting it there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Perhaps an Enkidu's Numinous Form....hrm, I want to say that their Numinous form depends on the Demigod's. But I also feel like it should be equal/almost equal in strength to a Demigod. <br /> <br /> If we do more of a &quot;linked&quot; idea, what if the Demigod and Enkidu maintain a near permanent link, kind of like how a Mage has to a familiar? They can read each other's emotional states, potentially be able to have telepathic communication or the like. An Enkidu can wield a Miracle so long as they have permission from a Demigod first?<br /> <br /> I somewhat fear if Enkidus, as they are now, are perhaps abit more powerful compared to other Subsplats. But I imagine given how harm coming to an Enkidu can hurt a Demigod in terms of Attachment (at least in my ideas), I can only imagine one massive limitation to them that is special for them. A Demigod may only ever have one Enkidu at a time. An Enkidu cannot exist without a Demigod, and they are attached to one by default. <br /> <br /> As for the pictures, I like them and think they're good. But you might wanna check a few of the Titan ones and the Icon picture, the link says the page doesn't exist. :c","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T02:27:44-07:00","id":936468,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm working on clearing up the images. I don't know what made them do that, though. Anyway, here's what I've got for the Enkidu so far. Any other ideas or opinions on what's already there would be welcome.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Ideas</u></span></span><ul><li>Cannot be targeted by Miracles</li> <li>Are connected to a given demigod, soul-bond?</li> <li>Have some kind of Numinous Form that is equivalent to their bonded demigod\u2019s?</li> <li>Can channel Miracles?</li> <li>(Instead of Numinous Form idea) Are physically more powerful than demigods in human form? (see Discipline idea)</li> <li>Capable of using Icons as demigods do</li> <li>Discipline-esque channels for Potentia? (Potency, Celerity, Fortitude etc?)</li> <li>Can act as an Icon of sorts, with certain specific Miracles \u2018inbuilt\u2019?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T05:00:46-07:00","id":936494,"title":"","content":"Also, has anyone got any ideas for Conditions imposed by Halysis. Like, one per threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T14:54:52-07:00","id":936731,"title":"","content":"Well, I dunno if it needs repeating, but from how we have it, I feel like Enkidus could potentially be one of the strongest sub-splats around, so I still kinda hold to the idea that a Demigod may only have one Enkidu. <br /> <br /> Which also makes me think. What power or the like makes a normal human into an Enkidu? I don't think it's something so easily defined like how other supernaturals make their subsplats. The idea I have at the moment is that the potential Enkidu (or the Demigod) should have the True Friend merit in regards to the Demigod (or vice versa). Being as close as they are, the Demigod may choose at any time to spend a <i>dot </i>of Luminance. This dot latches toward the potential Enkidu and makes them into a full fledged Enkidu. It also plays on the friendship theme of Gilgamesh and Enkidu. <br /> <br /> As for being unable to be targeted for Miracles, I think the original idea was to make them immune to their Demigod's Miracles, but I'm somewhat fine with extending this immunity to any Demigod's Miracles. I prolly shouldn't say immunity, indirect sources of harm caused by Miracles (let's say flooding or fire storm) should still cause harm.<br /> <br /> As for the Numinous form, physically more powerful and/or channeled powers not like Domains idea, the only idea I have is how Enkidu was a being made of mud, once wild and beastial. To tie into this, maybe we should say that Enkidus are beings tied to the physical world? But I also feel the need that Enkidus should also be able to play the role as &quot;partner&quot; to demigods and go wherever Demigods can, which should include the Drasil...<br /> <br /> I feel the Miracles and &quot;Can act as an Icon of sorts&quot; should be mixed into one thing. How does this sound: Enkidus can make use of Domains, but they may only ever use Domains that is covered by their Demigod's Aspect. This means that an Enkidu to a Demigod with the Chaos Aspect can only ever make use of Chaos Aspected Domains on their own. They can still use other Domains they can't use through Icons though. <br /> <br /> As for Conditions, here's the ideas I have for them at each stage. :3 I also noticed, Halysis as it's written has ways to go up to new thresholds, but there's nothing listing how it goes down. Shouldn't there be a way to make it for mortals to lose Halysis? Perhaps they can lose one level of Halysis per Luminance Days?<br /> <br /> <b>Seeing is Believing (Paragon Threshold)</b><br /> Your character has been in the presence of a Demigod and failed to withstand his glory, giving the impression that the Demigod is someone to look up to. However, the character also sees the Demigod as an excuse to lash out with their predjudices. Your character automatically gains a good impression in the case of the Demigod, and wherever it would be appropriate to lash out with the character's predjudices, the character must roll Resolve + Composure and succeed not to do so.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a Beat every time your character fails to withhold their prejudice due to this condition.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>The character gains enough Halysis to reach this threshold.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition: </b>The Character moves up to the Hero threshold. <br /> <br /> <b>Hero Worshipper (Hero Threshold)</b><br /> Your character has spent more time in the presence of a Demigod, and now is laid low by their awe towards the Demigod. They see him as someone to be respected and every request fulfilled. Your character loses a Door in Social Maneuvering with the Demigod opening them, and your character does not get 10 Again in any rolls that would go against the Demigod. Their prejudices also become more justified by their faith, your character is considered to fail any roll where they would resist acting on their prejudice unless it would cause a Breaking Point.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a beat when your character suffers a hardship due to their prejudice caused by this condition.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>The character gains enough Halysis to reach this threshold.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition: </b>The Character moves up to the Archetype Threshold.<br /> <br /> <b>The Yes Man (Archetype Threshold)</b><br /> Your character has spent so much time in the Demigod's presence that he's basically basking in it whenever the Demigod is known. To them, the Demigod is without reproach, every act is done for the greater good. Your character loses 3 Doors when engaging in Social Maneuvering with the Demigod, and the Demigod gains 9 Again in speaking with them. Also, your character no longer has the restraint in their opinions, making them able to commit Breaking Points so long as they will not be discovered. Any attempt to restrain themselves from acting on their opinions or prejudices where they can commit a Breaking Point and get away with it automatically fails.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a Beat when your character commits a breaking point in the name of their own opinions or prejudices.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a Beat whenever your character suffers a hardship at the Demigod's request or as a result of their requests.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>The Character gains enough Halysis to reach this Threshold.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition: </b>The character moves up to the Symbol Threshold.<br /> <br /> <b>The Butt Kisser (Symbol Threshold)</b><br /> Your character barely even resists the Demigod's glory, such that it flows into him and makes him more willing to act in favor of that glory. Perhaps by serving him, the Demigod may be pleased to give some of that glory to the servant...? Your character loses 5 doors when engaging in Social Maneuvering with the Demigod, and the Demigod gains 8 Again against your character. Your character also loses regard of other people's opinions, adding a penalty of half the Demigod's Luminance to all rolls any other character would try to reason with them. <br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a Beat when your character suffers a significant hardship due to their prejudices. <br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a Beat whenever your character suffers a significant hardship due to the Demigod's request or as a result of their requests.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>Your character gains enough Halysis to reach this Threshold.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition: </b>The Character moves up to the God Threshold.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sycophantic Servant (God Threshold)</b><br /> Your character is now fully open to the awe of a Demigod, worshipping them as the god they are and losing what little restraint they had left against acting on their prejudices and opinions. The only restraint that remains is perhaps the Demigod's own demands. Your character loses 7 Doors when engaging in Social Maneuvering with the Demigod, and the Demigod gains Rote Quality in their rolls of Social Maneuvering against your character. Your character also doesn't care about committing Breaking points in the name of the Demigod, being fanatical as they are. However, the word of the Demigod is law, and if the Demigod forbids your characters actions, then they will not act upon it. This doesn't mean your character can't think of ways to get around it or act in other ways of course.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a beat whenever your character suffers a Breaking Point in the name of their Demigod.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Take a beat whenever your character acts out in favor of the Demigod at a cost to themselves.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>Your Character gains enough Halysis to reach this Threshold. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T04:40:52-07:00","id":937005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=936731#post936731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I dunno if it needs repeating, but from how we have it, I feel like Enkidus could potentially be one of the strongest sub-splats around, so I still kinda hold to the idea that a Demigod may only have one Enkidu.<br /> <br /> Which also makes me think. What power or the like makes a normal human into an Enkidu? I don't think it's something so easily defined like how other supernaturals make their subsplats. The idea I have at the moment is that the potential Enkidu (or the Demigod) should have the True Friend merit in regards to the Demigod (or vice versa). Being as close as they are, the Demigod may choose at any time to spend a <i>dot </i>of Luminance. This dot latches toward the potential Enkidu and makes them into a full fledged Enkidu. It also plays on the friendship theme of Gilgamesh and Enkidu.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of an Enkidu being linked to a specific Demigod who as a close companion, but at the same time it would be nice to keep the option of having them as independent antagonists. Even the usually-obedient ghouls have the occasional Ambrogio Baudolino.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the True Friend merit is necessary to <i>safely</i> become an Enkidu, but an irresponsible Demigod can sacrifice a dot of Luminance to empower someone to whom they are not so close. The resulting character would be trapped in their Numinous Form and at risk of insanity (paralleling Enkidu's bestial appearance and behavior at the start of the epic) unless they find a Demigod to adopt and befriend them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T05:54:01-07:00","id":937022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937005#post937005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the idea of an Enkidu being linked to a specific Demigod who as a close companion, but at the same time it would be nice to keep the option of having them as independent antagonists. Even the usually-obedient ghouls have the occasional Ambrogio Baudolino.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the True Friend merit is necessary to <i>safely</i> become an Enkidu, but an irresponsible Demigod can sacrifice a dot of Luminance to empower someone to whom they are not so close. The resulting character would be trapped in their Numinous Form and at risk of insanity (paralleling Enkidu's bestial appearance and behavior at the start of the epic) unless they find a Demigod to adopt and befriend them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is definitely a good idea, but I'm not sure I like the idea of that being the only way to create an Enkidu. Perhaps a demigod can create Enkidu connected to other demigods. For example, a powerful Empyrean might do so to create a counterbalance to a younger, uncontrolled demigod (perhaps that's what actually happened in the myth). Also, I can't help but feel that having them be trapped in Numinous Form limits story ideas. The risk of insanity thing works, I think, but I kind of like the idea of having a 'free' Enkidu as a rogue element in demigodly politics. A spy, informant or perhaps even assassin who cannot simply be vaporised with a Miracle. I think that 'free' Enkidu would not be able to use Miracles as a bonded one might. Also, perhaps bonded Enkidu have their partner's immortality while free Enkidu do not (or only have longevity)?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and when I say immunity to Miracles, I mean immunity to their direct effects. So they wouldn't drown in conjured water or be vaporised directly, but the air around them could be heated up to the point when their lungs are cooked from inhaling it or water could be summoned from a river or a pipeline or something and that would drown them. Demigods can still fight them with miracles, they just need to be a little more clever about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 07-25-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T05:58:40-07:00","id":937027,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a>, I hope you don't mind if I use those Conditions, do you? I might change a couple of the names (Butt-Kisser for one) but other than that, I'll probably just Copy-Paste. Is that OK?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T07:45:56-07:00","id":937085,"title":"","content":"Random idea, but should we make it so that a demigod must spend Potentia in order to remain in Numinous Form (not just to transform into it)? Except in the Drasil, where they're always in N.F.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T08:13:14-07:00","id":937096,"title":"","content":"Any ideas for sub-merits to Temple? Off the top of my head I can think of something like a weapons arsenal, something that makes it easier to access the Drasil, something that makes it cheaper to enter Numinous Form and one that represents the Temple being shrouded in secrecy (that one would impose a cap on Potency, though, unless the Temple is owned by the demigod's Cult).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T10:34:16-07:00","id":937165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937027#post937027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a>, I hope you don't mind if I use those Conditions, do you? I might change a couple of the names (Butt-Kisser for one) but other than that, I'll probably just Copy-Paste. Is that OK?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind, these conditions were specifically made for this game. So they're yours to make use for whatever you like. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937085#post937085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random idea, but should we make it so that a demigod must spend Potentia in order to remain in Numinous Form (not just to transform into it)? Except in the Drasil, where they're always in N.F.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be an odd idea, but what if Demigods could suffer Essence (or in this case, Potentia) Bleed while in Numinous Form? I haven't read up on Spirit Rules for the GMC/ChoD, but I remember in the 1E version that a Spirit or Ghost would need to be anchored/fettered to something and be around it in order to not suffer Essence Bleed. For Demigods, their Anchor/Fetter is their Temple meaning having one allows a Demigod to stay in Numinous Form indefinitely so long as they own the Temple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937096#post937096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas for sub-merits to Temple? Off the top of my head I can think of something like a weapons arsenal, something that makes it easier to access the Drasil, something that makes it cheaper to enter Numinous Form and one that represents the Temple being shrouded in secrecy (that one would impose a cap on Potency, though, unless the Temple is owned by the demigod's Cult).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Secrecy for a Temple. If I may also add, how about a merit to represent the Demigod's cult as accepted in mainstream society? I don't have the thing on me right now, but I know that there was something on these forums that covered the idea of a Cult becoming an official religion. Of course, if it's someone else's idea we should ask them permission first.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a Demigod, Cult or Temple being able to have an ordained priest for the job. This could be a merit?<br /> <br /> Also, I have a small idea for a merit for Demigods.<br /> <br /> <b>Obscurity (1 to 3 Dots)</b><br /> Prerequisite: Cannot have Fame<br /> Not all gods are recognized as such. Some have merely faded into the background of their own myths and stories, from the public eye. Some aren't even remembered today, lost to the mists of time. But regardless, these gods have once existed, and some Demigods find they take some of those same traits. Obscure Demigods are people who are barely on the corners of the public eye, and tend to be forgotten by mundane sources. Records get lost, authorities forget they have warrants to arrest a Demigod for a time, even mundane neighbors can forget the Demigod lives next door. Obscurity however gives supernatural protection too. For each dot in Obscurity, a power that would harm the Demigod takes an equivalent penalty.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback: </i>Obscure Gods don't recieve much worship, and tend to be forgotten on top of that. When attempting to harvest Potentia, the Demigod takes an equivalent penalty to all rolls to harvest it unless it's from a person acting out of faith for the Demigod themselves, or it's from the Demigod's own Cult. Not to mention, a Demigod who becomes well known cannot maintain this merit. They must cultivate to keep this merit. They can lose this merit temporarily if they become well known for a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T11:21:10-07:00","id":937183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937165#post937165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't mind, these conditions were specifically made for this game. So they're yours to make use for whatever you like. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937165#post937165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be an odd idea, but what if Demigods could suffer Essence (or in this case, Potentia) Bleed while in Numinous Form? I haven't read up on Spirit Rules for the GMC/ChoD, but I remember in the 1E version that a Spirit or Ghost would need to be anchored/fettered to something and be around it in order to not suffer Essence Bleed. For Demigods, their Anchor/Fetter is their Temple meaning having one allows a Demigod to stay in Numinous Form indefinitely so long as they own the Temple.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would work very well, I think. One thing I've been trying to get in is that Numinous Form, especially those of more powerful demigods, is very similar to an ephemeral being. I'll have to check up on the rules too. I don't think they'd suffer the Potentia Bleed in the Drasil either, but that might have been implied in your post and I missed it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937165#post937165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Secrecy for a Temple. If I may also add, how about a merit to represent the Demigod's cult as accepted in mainstream society? I don't have the thing on me right now, but I know that there was something on these forums that covered the idea of a Cult becoming an official religion. Of course, if it's someone else's idea we should ask them permission first.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a thread where someone made up full rules for cults, organisations and stuff. I'll probably be using a lot of them. I asked a while back if I could use them and got a yes, although I'll probably be tweaking some stuff to fit better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937165#post937165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like the idea of a Demigod, Cult or Temple being able to have an ordained priest for the job. This could be a merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good idea. I'm not sure how it would work though. Perhaps it allows the demigod to treat the priest as a Temple for the purposes of harvesting Potentia, because that faith is being focused through them? It might play in well to a rough idea I've been pondering on, of having a kind of magic-ish thing that only mortals can do with the help of a demigod that allows them to create relatively weak quasi-Icons. I'll probably model it off of the Enchanting part of my Primordial Sorcery project. Perhaps the priest might provide a bonus to that? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937165#post937165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I have a small idea for a merit for Demigods.<br /> <br /> <b>Obscurity (1 to 3 Dots)</b><br /> Prerequisite: Cannot have Fame<br /> Not all gods are recognized as such. Some have merely faded into the background of their own myths and stories, from the public eye. Some aren't even remembered today, lost to the mists of time. But regardless, these gods have once existed, and some Demigods find they take some of those same traits. Obscure Demigods are people who are barely on the corners of the public eye, and tend to be forgotten by mundane sources. Records get lost, authorities forget they have warrants to arrest a Demigod for a time, even mundane neighbors can forget the Demigod lives next door. Obscurity however gives supernatural protection too. For each dot in Obscurity, a power that would harm the Demigod takes an equivalent penalty.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback: </i>Obscure Gods don't recieve much worship, and tend to be forgotten on top of that. When attempting to harvest Potentia, the Demigod takes an equivalent penalty to all rolls to harvest it unless it's from a person acting out of faith for the Demigod themselves, or it's from the Demigod's own Cult. Not to mention, a Demigod who becomes well known cannot maintain this merit. They must cultivate to keep this merit. They can lose this merit temporarily if they become well known for a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T11:57:26-07:00","id":937197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937183#post937183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937183#post937183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would work very well, I think. One thing I've been trying to get in is that Numinous Form, especially those of more powerful demigods, is very similar to an ephemeral being. I'll have to check up on the rules too. I don't think they'd suffer the Potentia Bleed in the Drasil either, but that might have been implied in your post and I missed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean for them to suffer it, especially with how 1 point of Potentia is gained for day in the Drasil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937183#post937183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a thread where someone made up full rules for cults, organisations and stuff. I'll probably be using a lot of them. I asked a while back if I could use them and got a yes, although I'll probably be tweaking some stuff to fit better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, that'll be nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937183#post937183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a good idea. I'm not sure how it would work though. Perhaps it allows the demigod to treat the priest as a Temple for the purposes of harvesting Potentia, because that faith is being focused through them? It might play in well to a rough idea I've been pondering on, of having a kind of magic-ish thing that only mortals can do with the help of a demigod that allows them to create relatively weak quasi-Icons. I'll probably model it off of the Enchanting part of my Primordial Sorcery project. Perhaps the priest might provide a bonus to that?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps, what I was thinking when it came to Priests was the idea of how some splats have two subsplats. For example:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Ghouls and Blood dolls<br /> Werewolves: Wolf-Blooded and Skinchangers<br /> Mages: Sleepwalkers and Thaumaturges<br /> <br /> GRANTED, this doesn't exactly work out for every splat. But I was thinking that it could work for Demigods. Enkidu being their sidekicks and helpers, and Priests being able to take care of their cults or the like. <br /> <br /> I also forgot to mention, but I have an idea for a pre-requisite for becoming a Priest. Namely, the person in question needs to be at least in the Symbol or God Threshold of Halysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937183#post937183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:43:39-07:00","id":937228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937197#post937197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't mean for them to suffer it, especially with how 1 point of Potentia is gained for day in the Drasil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per hour, I thought. Anyway, moving on...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937197#post937197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alrighties, that'll be nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can give you a link if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937197#post937197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps, what I was thinking when it came to Priests was the idea of how some splats have two subsplats. For example:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Ghouls and Blood dolls<br /> Werewolves: Wolf-Blooded and Skinchangers<br /> Mages: Sleepwalkers and Thaumaturges<br /> <br /> GRANTED, this doesn't exactly work out for every splat. But I was thinking that it could work for Demigods. Enkidu being their sidekicks and helpers, and Priests being able to take care of their cults or the like.<br /> <br /> I also forgot to mention, but I have an idea for a pre-requisite for becoming a Priest. Namely, the person in question needs to be at least in the Symbol or God Threshold of Halysis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that working. So, they'd basically be demigod-powered thaumaturges? Kinda. Is that sort of what you meant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:33:52-07:00","id":937256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937228#post937228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see that working. So, they'd basically be demigod-powered thaumaturges? Kinda. Is that sort of what you meant?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of Priests being more like Blood Dolls, where a Demigod could get Potentia from better than anyone else. <br /> <br /> I could also imagine, given the idea for requiring to be at God threshold, that they could make for some interesting stories. Possibly misinterpreting the Demigod's commands, trying to spread them throughout more people, doing things behind the Demigod's back. Sure, they may be a hassle, but I feel like it could play with the theme of &quot;responsibility for lessers&quot; abit more. <br /> <br /> Let's just say my current thoughts on the matter for Priests are something like the Vigil of Stendarr in Skyrim. &quot;Walk always in the Light, or we will drag you into it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T13:58:55-07:00","id":937270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937256#post937256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking of Priests being more like Blood Dolls, where a Demigod could get Potentia from better than anyone else. <br /> <br /> I could also imagine, given the idea for requiring to be at God threshold, that they could make for some interesting stories. Possibly misinterpreting the Demigod's commands, trying to spread them throughout more people, doing things behind the Demigod's back. Sure, they may be a hassle, but I feel like it could play with the theme of &amp;quot;responsibility for lessers&amp;quot; abit more. <br /> <br /> Let's just say my current thoughts on the matter for Priests are something like the Vigil of Stendarr in Skyrim. &amp;quot;Walk always in the Light, or we will drag you into it&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Perhaps they could have some basic cantrip-like powers, as a 'gift from our lord'? How do you think it could be done mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T14:09:14-07:00","id":937276,"title":"","content":"And for the powers, I don't mean anything remotely powerful. Perhaps a bonus to Abjuration, Warding and Binding, as well as some basic tricks dependant on their demigod's Domains. So a Priest of a demigod with the domain of war could inspire warriors in battle or one bound to a demigod of fire cannot be harmed by fire (and only fire, so molten metal or something would still hurt them). Just to make them a little more interesting than 'you can get more power from these guys'. Also sp they can unintentionally mess with the demigod's plans even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T17:02:07-07:00","id":937376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937276#post937276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for the powers, I don't mean anything remotely powerful. Perhaps a bonus to Abjuration, Warding and Binding, as well as some basic tricks dependant on their demigod's Domains. So a Priest of a demigod with the domain of war could inspire warriors in battle or one bound to a demigod of fire cannot be harmed by fire (and only fire, so molten metal or something would still hurt them). Just to make them a little more interesting than 'you can get more power from these guys'. Also sp they can unintentionally mess with the demigod's plans even more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good enough. Perhaps they receive half the Demigod's Luminance as a bonus to attempts to Abjurate, Ward or Bind? As far as the blessings go, I think they should mainly stick with the Demigod's original Domain. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T07:03:43-07:00","id":937580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937376#post937376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sounds good enough. Perhaps they receive half the Demigod's Luminance as a bonus to attempts to Abjurate, Ward or Bind? As far as the blessings go, I think they should mainly stick with the Demigod's original Domain. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right. I could see it maybe granting appropriate Supernatural Merits or something. What would a demigod have to pay to make a Priest, though? (Other than EXP). Would there be a price?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T11:56:09-07:00","id":937714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937580#post937580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds about right. I could see it maybe granting appropriate Supernatural Merits or something. What would a demigod have to pay to make a Priest, though? (Other than EXP). Would there be a price?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say at least a point of Potentia per day? Just to give the feel of Divine Patronage or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T13:06:03-07:00","id":937734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937714#post937714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say at least a point of Potentia per day? Just to give the feel of Divine Patronage or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't particularly like the idea of a constant bit of bookkeeping like that, and that would kind of make creating the Priest in the first place a bit redundant. Perhaps they could have something like a cost in Potentia (and EXP) to create them in the first place, buying them as a kind of 'Retainer', but they lose the template if they fall below the Symbol threshold, so they require 'upkeep' in the form of constant attention. Perhaps a Potentia every ((Luminance - Number of Priests)*2) days or something? The thing is, Potentia is meant to be fairly scarce, or at least rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T16:17:53-07:00","id":937823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937734#post937734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't particularly like the idea of a constant bit of bookkeeping like that, and that would kind of make creating the Priest in the first place a bit redundant. Perhaps they could have something like a cost in Potentia (and EXP) to create them in the first place, buying them as a kind of 'Retainer', but they lose the template if they fall below the Symbol threshold, so they require 'upkeep' in the form of constant attention. Perhaps a Potentia every ((Luminance - Number of Priests)*2) days or something? The thing is, Potentia is meant to be fairly scarce, or at least rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't think it'd be a major cost in Potentia. Priests are meant to make it easier to gain Potentia, but I do understand how it can be a headache in micromanaging. Constant attention then is prolly good enough.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can see as an idea (I think I may be getting complicated by now) is that Priests are capable of having a Potentia Pool of their own that the Demigod they're dedicated to can pull from at any time. The Priests cannot spend this pool for any reason save for whatever &quot;blessings&quot; they have in mind, the Priest may gain Potentia only through acts of faith to their Demigod (so basically how Demigods witness acts of faith, but the Priest must pull it off themselves). Given that they have no Luminance, they're only capable of holding Potential equal to their Willpower (or we say they have a base pool of 10).<br /> <br /> Ack, sorry if I'm getting out of hand on ideas. ^^&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T00:26:03-07:00","id":937976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937823#post937823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i don't think it'd be a major cost in Potentia. Priests are meant to make it easier to gain Potentia, but I do understand how it can be a headache in micromanaging. Constant attention then is prolly good enough.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can see as an idea (I think I may be getting complicated by now) is that Priests are capable of having a Potentia Pool of their own that the Demigod they're dedicated to can pull from at any time. The Priests cannot spend this pool for any reason save for whatever &quot;blessings&quot; they have in mind, the Priest may gain Potentia only through acts of faith to their Demigod (so basically how Demigods witness acts of faith, but the Priest must pull it off themselves). Given that they have no Luminance, they're only capable of holding Potential equal to their Willpower (or we say they have a base pool of 10).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, that seems like quite an elegant solution. Perhaps what they can do is hold Potentia <i>instead</i> of Willpower, as in each point of Potentia that the Priest has 'locks up' one slot for Willpower. MAybe we could extend that, making it so that they can spend that Potentia like Willpower (to gain +3 dice to something) but the way it helps is not so much 'you're putting your all into this' and more 'you change the world to help you'. If you know Nobilis, it would be like the difference between Bonds and Afflictions. So if you spend a Potentia to help you defeat an enemy in melee combat and the Priest serves a demigod with the primary Domain of Fire, he might ignite his hands and use them to fight with. Maybe it could also allow the Priest to roll for things that he usually couldn't, like, &quot;I want to walk through that fire without being hurt. I spend 2 Potentia and therefore roll 6 dice. On a success, I walk right through that fire. On a failure I still get burned.&quot; Or something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=937823#post937823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ack, sorry if I'm getting out of hand on ideas. ^^&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as too many ideas. Bad ideas are better than no ideas and your ideas are by no means bad. Please continue! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T05:47:08-07:00","id":938045,"title":"","content":"Random bit of fluff, but how does it sound if upon his Ascension and as he grows in power, the qualities of a demigod's mortal form become exaggerated somewhat? For example, someone who is handsome beforehand becomes more so while an old lady's wrinkles deepen, although they make her look more 'wizened' than decrepit. It's another expression of the hyperbole inherent in legend and myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:11:08-07:00","id":938162,"title":"","content":"Here's my attempt at mechanics for Priests. Feel free to comment, review, flame etc.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Priests</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For all their power, demigods are not omnipotent and one of the greatest checks on their power is the fact that in order to exercise it, both in Numinous Form and in Miracles, requires Potentia, the divine energy of the Drasil. Potentia can be harvested from cults, Temples and the Drasil itself but all of these come with drawbacks and risks. Cults can be destroyed or can lose their faith, Temples are inherently fragile structures and are never far away from the possibility of destruction and access to the Drasil requires a Temple.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Therefore, many demigods seek to create more reliable sources of Potentia and to that end, many create 'Priests', mortals endowed with the ability to use and, more importantly, collect Potentia independently of the demigod as well as acting as a kind of repository that the demigod can draw upon, should the need arise.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>To Be Ordained</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In game terms, creating a Priest is done by simply spending Experience on the Priest Merit and applying the Priest template to a suitable NPC. In character, however, the process is somewhat more involved. In order to become a Priest, a mortal (hereafter referred to as the Acolyte) must be under the effects of the Symbol or God Thresholds of Halysis. In addition, they must know that the demigod is supernatural in some way \u2013 although their belief need not be </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>accurate</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u2013 and the demigod must offer them Priesthood verbally and in person. They need not explain all the mechanics of the position but they must make it clear that the position grants the Acolyte power at the price of service to the demigod. The Acolyte must then accept the position, willingly and under no compulsion, supernatural or otherwise, excepting that imposed by Halysis. The demigod cannot word this as a command, it must be an offer which the Acolyte is free to decline (not that he is likely to do so, given his adoration of the demigod, but it is possible.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Having done this, the demigod spends a point of Potentia and presses a hand to the Acolyte's skin, in some location. Where the hand touches, a mark not unlike a brand or tattoo is burned onto the Acolyte's skin. This mark is unique to each demigod and is usually representative of that demigod's Domains, Aspect or Following. A demigod may not attempt to imitate the Mark of another. This Mark cannot be removed by mundane means, although the Priest may spend a point of Willpower to cause it to disappear for a scene.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Fall From Grace</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are four ways in which a Priest may lose his power and position.</span></span><ul><li>If the demigod which Ordained him dies but still endures (by incarnating in his Icon, for example), the Priest temporarily loses the template and his Mark fades to something not unlike a scar or a birthmark. The template is re-applied upon the demigod's resurrection.</li> <li>If the demigod which Ordained him dies permanently, the Priest loses the template and the Mark burns itself off. If the demigod is later resurrected by some arcane means, the template does not return.</li> <li>The demigod who Ordained a Priest can strip them of their position with a touch and another point of Potentia. If this is done, the Priest immediately loses all Willpower and Potentia (see below) and has the Stunned Tilt for the rest of the scene, as well as the Soul-Shocked Condition for the next week. He also immediately falls a THreshold of Halysis, as his faith is shaken by the demigod\u2019s dismissal of his service.</li> <li>If the Priest ever falls below the Symbol Halysis Threshold, he loses the Priest template until that Threshold is regained. He also gains the Shaken Condition, which is only resolved when the former Priest either falls another Threshold of Halysis or returns to the Symbol Threshold.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Gifts of the Divine</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Priest template grants the following abilities:</span></span><ul><li>Priests are immune to the Rapture, although not to the effects of Halysis. They are also immune to Breaking Points due to witnessing the supernatural.</li> <li>A Priest has an extra Virtue, entitled 'Serving My God', which is fulfilled whenever the Priest significantly inconveniences himself to do something for the demigod. Whether or not this is what the demigod actually <i>wants</i> is a moot point.</li> <li>Whenever the Priest would regain Willpower, he may instead elect to roll (Resolve + Composure) and gain Potentia equal to successes rolled. This Potentia can be stored in place of Willpower. For each point gathered, mark a horizontal line through a Willpower box (which may be used or not). That point of Willpower may not be spent while the Potentia is there. If this roll is made, the Priest gains no Willpower, no matter how many (or few) successes are rolled.</li> <li>A Priest may spend Potentia in place of Willpower, gaining +3 dice to a single roll. However, he may also choose to spend Potentia in order to attempt to work a miracle (although not a capital \u2018M\u2019 Miracle), using only the dice gained from the Potentia spent. This allows Priests to channel some of the power of their patron into superhuman and magical feats. A Priest may attempt to use these minor miracles to affect anything which relates to one of their demigod's Domains, although they can never create any effect beyond that of a 1-dot Miracle, can only affect the Priest and those he is touching and cannot last any longer than 1 round per success.<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willpower cannot be spent to augment this roll.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Example: The Priest Martin Goldman, serving a demigod with the Domains of </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Fire, Conflict and Earth, is trapped in a burning building. Conflict is little help here, and the power of a miracle of Earth necessary to allow him to sink through the floor is beyond the skill of a Priest, but he can use a miracle of protection to keep himself safe</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>from the heat of the flames. He spends 2 of his 4 Potentia, giving him a dice pool of 6. He rolls, and comes up with 3, 4, 9, 3, 10 and 6. He rolls another dice for the 10 and comes up with a 9. He has a</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>total of 3 successes, enough for approximately 12 seconds of fire </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>protection. He'd better hurry!</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Later </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>on, the same Priest is called by his demigod to command a party of </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>cultists in defending their Temple from a rival Cult. In the fight, </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Martin's group is affected by a fear-causing Miracle from an Icon wielded by an enemy Cultist which inflicts the Beaten Down Tilt on a </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>number of Martin's war party. Seeing this, he spends another Potentia, this time using the Domain of Conflict to fuel a Miracle to inspire his followers. He rolls one success on his three dice and roars in defiance at his enemy, letting out a fierce battle cry, rallying his comrades and removing the Tilt. Because the enemy </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Miracle is an Instant effect which simply imposes the Tilt, not an ongoing one which keeps it there, the Priest's miracle need only act for one</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>turn to remove it. It does nothing to protect the cultists from the Icon's Miracle being used again.</i></span></span></i></span></span></span></span><ul><li>A Priest may spend their stored Potentia in order to make use of Miracles imbued into Icons, spending 1 Potentia for 1- and 2-dot Miracles, 2 for 3- and 4-dot Miracles and 3 for 5-dot Miracles. He may still elect to spend Willpower as if he were a normal mortal if he wishes to do so.</li> <li>A Priest's demigod patron can, in any scene that he can directly see (not through cameras, although lenses or binoculars work fine) or touch the Priest, roll Resolve + Composure + Luminance and drain a number of points of Potentia from the Priest equal to successes rolled.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 07-27-2016, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T10:06:43-07:00","id":938183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=938045#post938045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random bit of fluff, but how does it sound if upon his Ascension and as he grows in power, the qualities of a demigod's mortal form become exaggerated somewhat? For example, someone who is handsome beforehand becomes more so while an old lady's wrinkles deepen, although they make her look more 'wizened' than decrepit. It's another expression of the hyperbole inherent in legend and myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. The Priest template also looks good. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:08:01-07:00","id":940562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=938183#post938183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds good. The Priest template also looks good. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> Getting back to business, a while back there was a suggestion that perhaps Followings should give a 'Specialty' of sorts for the use of Miracles and I think this would be a good idea to develop a little more. Do you think there should be only one specialty granted or several (three maybe)? Any ideas for a particular name, to distinguish them from skill specialties? Some rationale for them being there? My immediate thought on that front is that the combined 'pressure' of the belief and will of the Following upon its own members 'moulds' them somewhat, making subtle changes to their human form (nudging it towards the ideal of that Following), more overt ones to the Numinous Form, given its malleability, and upon the manifestation of their Miracles, making it easier for them to work them in some ways. Should there be some kind of 'anti-specialty' for Miracles which work against the Follwoing's ethos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T04:19:23-07:00","id":940564,"title":"","content":"BTW, the post above was addressed to anyone who cares to give an answer, although <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a> is more than welcome to as well, seeing as he's (she's?) been a great help in the last couple of weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T07:25:54-07:00","id":940616,"title":"","content":"I've been considering, and I think that it might be a better idea to remove the parts of Luminance that affect the Size and Manifestation Condition of the Numinous Form, as the former makes it unnecessarily difficult to use it and the latter makes it so that Numinous Form is effectively useless in the physical world at high Luminance, its only purpose being to empower Miracles.<br /> <br /> This is not what I am <i>going</i> to do, though. It's just a thought that I had and one which I thought I'd run by you guys. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T11:21:21-07:00","id":940711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940562#post940562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back to business, a while back there was a suggestion that perhaps Followings should give a 'Specialty' of sorts for the use of Miracles and I think this would be a good idea to develop a little more. Do you think there should be only one specialty granted or several (three maybe)? Any ideas for a particular name, to distinguish them from skill specialties? Some rationale for them being there? My immediate thought on that front is that the combined 'pressure' of the belief and will of the Following upon its own members 'moulds' them somewhat, making subtle changes to their human form (nudging it towards the ideal of that Following), more overt ones to the Numinous Form, given its malleability, and upon the manifestation of their Miracles, making it easier for them to work them in some ways. Should there be some kind of 'anti-specialty' for Miracles which work against the Follwoing's ethos?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that favoritism of certain Miracles would be fitting. Allowing to use them at lower costs and the like. Although it seems like there's loads of Followings.<br /> <br /> If I may suggest a small idea, what if Followings covered mainly the five aspects most WoD games follow? Leadership/Social, Warriors/Fighters, Lore and Secret Keepers, Tricksters and Spies, and finally those who follow human development and the like? I know it may be a little cliche, but most of the other gamelines seem to have the pattern for either X or Y splats. I can also admit Siren sort of does the same for the &quot;Good&quot; currents.<br /> <br /> <b>Ideas on this</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Leader/Social Following could be the somewhat blatant religion that you know from the old world. They take the forms of lost gods from dead religions, adopting the forms that people know of and can look up to. For example, in Scandanavia, most Leader Following Demigods could take the form of the Aesir or Vanir in Viking Mythology. I can see this being a mix of the Followings of Heirs and Sparks.<br /> <br /> The Warriors and Fighters are both the gods of conflict and war as much as harmony and peace. Their Following is perhaps the most involved in the human state of matters, as they're the ones who are most likely to try and keep the state of affairs of their cults to be peaceful and smiting down enemies to the cult with great prejudice. This could be a mix of the Following of Banners and Descendants.<br /> <br /> The Lore and Secret Keepers are the Gods you imagine when it comes to hierarchal societies. The Gods are always up top, and the members usually seek enlightenment through the god. Those with greater amounts of enlightenment tend to be amongst the Priests or greater levels of Halysis. However, their thirst for knowledge and enlightenment aren't quenchable and it always goes back up to the god up top too. In a sense, think of them like a less malignant Hermaus Mora from the Elder Scrolls. This could be a mix of the Followings of Vassals and Eidolon.<br /> <br /> The Trickster and spies are the Gods that you automatically think of when it comes to secret societies or cults. They're the gods who hold large amounts of influence and exert it on others.Another idea I had was that these kinds of gods do decieve and lie to their own followers, but those who manage to work their way past the lies and tricks the god puts up, they tend to be able to move up to greater levels of importance. They could be a mix of the Followings of the Morning-Star and Ascendants.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Human Development Gods. These gods tend to be less &quot;God&quot; and more like forces of nature, lines of psychology, they embody the way the human world tries to grasp on natural and unnatural phenomena, and trying to change themselves in turn to human development and belief of the phenomena. Heck, maybe even the Following tries to lead the development. Afterall, a man of science reads hundreds of books and believe that there's more to learn, which in turn can give more potentia to a Demigod. The ideas I have atm is that this could be a mix of the Followings of Annunaki and Embodiments.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course, these are just ideas, feel free to disregard them. I'm just stating some suggestions on the number of followings. If you do take these ideas into account though, perhaps some of the ideas for Followings could still be used for Z-Splats?<br /> <br /> Anyways, regarding the post itself. The one idea I have is using a Mage Rote Spell equivalent, except for Domains? It would allow a Demigod to use a Dicepool with their Domain larger than their normal pool and it wouldn't cause Revelation within mortals already affected by Halysis or connected to a Demigod, like an Enkidu or Priest? Maybe they could be called Liturgies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940564#post940564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, the post above was addressed to anyone who cares to give an answer, although <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a> is more than welcome to as well, seeing as he's (she's?) been a great help in the last couple of weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first time I've had gender confusion when I wasn't using a username of &quot;Sally&quot;. XD I don't mean any offense, it's just some stuff that's been going on about on other places (mainly about Steam) that never fails to amuse me. I'll note that I'm a male though. :3<br /> <br /> As for the final post, I suppose I need to ask a little on the Numinous Form. Would Size automatically be increased with higher Luminance? I can see how it'd be a problem then. And could you please explain the Manifestation Condition part? I take it that Materialized means they can fully interact with the mortal world, Image means they're more in twilight but can still interact reality, whereas Twilight Form completely forces them to stay in Twilight?<br /> <br /> I don't mind the idea of changing them if it makes it more efficient to be a demigod.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:18:29-07:00","id":940739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940711#post940711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that favoritism of certain Miracles would be fitting. Allowing to use them at lower costs and the like. Although it seems like there's loads of Followings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't thinking so much a cost reduction, but more like a bonus to the roll to invoke them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940711#post940711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may suggest a small idea, what if Followings covered mainly the five aspects most WoD games follow? Leadership/Social, Warriors/Fighters, Lore and Secret Keepers, Tricksters and Spies, and finally those who follow human development and the like? I know it may be a little cliche, but most of the other gamelines seem to have the pattern for either X or Y splats. I can also admit Siren sort of does the same for the &quot;Good&quot; currents.<br /> <br /> <b>Ideas on this</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Leader/Social Following could be the somewhat blatant religion that you know from the old world. They take the forms of lost gods from dead religions, adopting the forms that people know of and can look up to. For example, in Scandanavia, most Leader Following Demigods could take the form of the Aesir or Vanir in Viking Mythology. I can see this being a mix of the Followings of Heirs and Sparks.<br /> <br /> The Warriors and Fighters are both the gods of conflict and war as much as harmony and peace. Their Following is perhaps the most involved in the human state of matters, as they're the ones who are most likely to try and keep the state of affairs of their cults to be peaceful and smiting down enemies to the cult with great prejudice. This could be a mix of the Following of Banners and Descendants.<br /> <br /> The Lore and Secret Keepers are the Gods you imagine when it comes to hierarchal societies. The Gods are always up top, and the members usually seek enlightenment through the god. Those with greater amounts of enlightenment tend to be amongst the Priests or greater levels of Halysis. However, their thirst for knowledge and enlightenment aren't quenchable and it always goes back up to the god up top too. In a sense, think of them like a less malignant Hermaus Mora from the Elder Scrolls. This could be a mix of the Followings of Vassals and Eidolon.<br /> <br /> The Trickster and spies are the Gods that you automatically think of when it comes to secret societies or cults. They're the gods who hold large amounts of influence and exert it on others.Another idea I had was that these kinds of gods do decieve and lie to their own followers, but those who manage to work their way past the lies and tricks the god puts up, they tend to be able to move up to greater levels of importance. They could be a mix of the Followings of the Morning-Star and Ascendants.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Human Development Gods. These gods tend to be less &quot;God&quot; and more like forces of nature, lines of psychology, they embody the way the human world tries to grasp on natural and unnatural phenomena, and trying to change themselves in turn to human development and belief of the phenomena. Heck, maybe even the Following tries to lead the development. Afterall, a man of science reads hundreds of books and believe that there's more to learn, which in turn can give more potentia to a Demigod. The ideas I have atm is that this could be a mix of the Followings of Annunaki and Embodiments.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Of course, these are just ideas, feel free to disregard them. I'm just stating some suggestions on the number of followings. If you do take these ideas into account though, perhaps some of the ideas for Followings could still be used for Z-Splats?</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I like the stuff that you've said here (and I do, the religion/following ideas are great) I kind of want demigodly society to be among the most fractious of any supernaturals in the CoD. My vision of it is that they although they have these big, organised Followings, unlike Mage's Orders or Werewolf's Tribes, demigodly Followings fight against each other more than with each other. They really do launch crusades in the Drasil against other Followings to steal their Icons and Gardr because <i>each one believes that they are right to do so. </i>Even within FOllowings you get factions which declare other factions 'heretical' and try to wipe them out. That's not to say that there aren't demigods who object to that, but when faith and belief are such big things in your life that they <i>literally </i>empower you to work miracles, they become things that all too many demigods live by. Their faith is what keeps a lot of them going through the decades and possibly centuries, when all their power does nothing to help those around them and only indoctrinates mortals into their service, their faith is what they cling to, as people <i>do</i>. Their faith that <i>I will return to the service of God, I will become transcendent, I will be freed from my human failings. </i>(Those are the followings of Vassals, Ascendants and Embodiments respectively)<br /> <br /> As I say, I think that mood could definitely be <i>achieved </i>with fixed factions and then splinter-factions within them, but I'm not sure it would be so easy to get the 'warring religions' thing. I don't know. I'll consider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940711#post940711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, regarding the post itself. The one idea I have is using a Mage Rote Spell equivalent, except for Domains? It would allow a Demigod to use a Dicepool with their Domain larger than their normal pool and it wouldn't cause Revelation within mortals already affected by Halysis or connected to a Demigod, like an Enkidu or Priest? Maybe they could be called Liturgies?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was kind of thinking that this would kind of be what the imbued Miracles in Icons would stand in for (the whole Miracle-Rotes thing, I mean) and Enkidu and Priests are immune to teh Rapture anyway, but I see where you're coming from. I could see perhaps having Liturgies as Following-specific 'rotes', which you get with Status in the Following, or something like that. Like the seasonal mantles from Changeling 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940711#post940711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time I've had gender confusion when I wasn't using a username of &quot;Sally&quot;. XD I don't mean any offense, it's just some stuff that's been going on about on other places (mainly about Steam) that never fails to amuse me. I'll note that I'm a male though. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>I just didn't know. I'm glad to see I got it right the first time. And, as they say, Rule 30 is that 'There are no girls on the Internet'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940711#post940711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the final post, I suppose I need to ask a little on the Numinous Form. Would Size automatically be increased with higher Luminance? I can see how it'd be a problem then. And could you please explain the Manifestation Condition part? I take it that Materialized means they can fully interact with the mortal world, Image means they're more in twilight but can still interact reality, whereas Twilight Form completely forces them to stay in Twilight?<br /> <br /> I don't mind the idea of changing them if it makes it more efficient to be a demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Size does increase automatically with Luminance at the moment (which is kind of awkward, I think) and the Manifestation stuff is basically how you said, except Image means that the demigod can be seen in the real world but only really exists in Twilight. I'm just thinking that the whole thing is just a bit clunky and unnecessary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T12:58:30-07:00","id":940773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940739#post940739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't thinking so much a cost reduction, but more like a bonus to the roll to invoke them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Well, my only thought is perhaps being able to make certain applications of a Domain have a bonus? My ideas at the moment is that each Following has one Domain application that becomes Rote Quality when performed? The applications being Manipulation, Creation, Understanding, Protection, Animation and Incarnation. For example, the Following of Reincarnation could easily have Domain Applications of Incarnation gaining rote quality?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940739#post940739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like the stuff that you've said here (and I do, the religion/following ideas are great) I kind of want demigodly society to be among the most fractious of any supernaturals in the CoD. My vision of it is that they although they have these big, organised Followings, unlike Mage's Orders or Werewolf's Tribes, demigodly Followings fight against each other more than with each other. They really do launch crusades in the Drasil against other Followings to steal their Icons and Gardr because <i>each one believes that they are right to do so. </i>Even within FOllowings you get factions which declare other factions 'heretical' and try to wipe them out. That's not to say that there aren't demigods who object to that, but when faith and belief are such big things in your life that they <i>literally </i>empower you to work miracles, they become things that all too many demigods live by. Their faith is what keeps a lot of them going through the decades and possibly centuries, when all their power does nothing to help those around them and only indoctrinates mortals into their service, their faith is what they cling to, as people <i>do</i>. Their faith that <i>I will return to the service of God, I will become transcendent, I will be freed from my human failings. </i>(Those are the followings of Vassals, Ascendants and Embodiments respectively)<br /> <br /> As I say, I think that mood could definitely be <i>achieved </i>with fixed factions and then splinter-factions within them, but I'm not sure it would be so easy to get the 'warring religions' thing. I don't know. I'll consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. And I understand what you're going for. If nothing else, I do remember that Mage does have splinter factions within themselves. So it could be doable. But this is your gameline. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940739#post940739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was kind of thinking that this would kind of be what the imbued Miracles in Icons would stand in for (the whole Miracle-Rotes thing, I mean) and Enkidu and Priests are immune to teh Rapture anyway, but I see where you're coming from. I could see perhaps having Liturgies as Following-specific 'rotes', which you get with Status in the Following, or something like that. Like the seasonal mantles from Changeling 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Enkidus, I have one more idea of them. Shouldn't they get the immortality that Demigods have too? As in mainly Agelessness. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940739#post940739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just didn't know. I'm glad to see I got it right the first time. And, as they say, Rule 30 is that 'There are no girls on the Internet'</div> </div> </div> </div>On the internet, all girls are men and all kids are FBI agents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=940739#post940739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Size does increase automatically with Luminance at the moment (which is kind of awkward, I think) and the Manifestation stuff is basically how you said, except Image means that the demigod can be seen in the real world but only really exists in Twilight. I'm just thinking that the whole thing is just a bit clunky and unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about making Size as one of the Numinous Form upgrades? And as for Manifesting, how about the Demigod is automatically Manifested when within the Drasil or their Temple, and anywhere else they're in Twilight Form? However, adding in a possible way to spend Potentia (at least 1 Potentia) to be able to Manifest for the rest of the scene?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T06:44:29-07:00","id":941906,"title":"","content":"The Deep Meta document is up. Don't read it unless you're ready for some <i>serious </i>spoilers, including some possibly erroneous assumptions about preexisting elements of the setting <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> namely the Divine Fire</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T07:16:49-07:00","id":941922,"title":"","content":"The next thing to be done on Demigod is probably to finish off the Aspects, but frankly it's a bit much for me to do alone and so if anyone could (please) help, that would be absolutely wonderful (and I'll put you in the credits, along with the people who've helped out so far).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T03:17:49-07:00","id":943513,"title":"","content":"Here's the first finished Aspect: Creation. Any thoughs on it would be greatly appreciated. Don't hesitate to point out flaws if you see them though.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Creation</u></span></span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Aspect of the Mother</span></b></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Progenitors</span></b></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Builders</span></span></b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">[e.g. Gaea, Amun, Ra, Izanagi, Baldur, Tiamat, Odin, Pan Gu, Brahma]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Introduction</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Throughout history, every faith, mythology and religion has recognised the divinity of creation. All of them recognise the miracle of birth and every faith has some kind of creator god or fertility deity. Even the ancient animistic faiths had spirits which brought plenty and aided in childbirth. Creation is the greatest miracle allotted to all life: the ability to create more of its kind, to build something that will last beyond itself. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Other than birth, another creative event present in every mythology is the very creation of the world, almost always carried out by powerful and intelligent forces. Pan Gu, having hatched from his world-egg, held the sky and earth apart long enough for the heavy elements of earth and water to sink to form land and oceans and for the world to become stable enough to stand without him. Ra created himself from the primordial waters and, by will, raised the first mountain from the sea of chaos. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">That said, one need only look at Gaea in Greek mythology, Tiamat in the Mesopotamian tales or at the sacrifices and rites performed in honour of countless fertility gods to see that creation need not be a benevolent force. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Ascension</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Those who Ascend through the Aspect of Creation are most often artistic and driven souls beforehand, and the days and weeks leading up to their metamorphosis are almost always characterised by a lack of inspiration and success and a growing frustration with themselves and the world around them. Perhaps they are an artist who </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">find</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> that they can\u2019t come up with anything to paint. Maybe they\u2019re a businessman whose investments keep falling through. They might even be a highschooler whose significant other keeps standing them up. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">All this leads up to a breaking point, where the proto-demigod feels utterly crushed by his frustrations and failings. And then a light comes. They feel something ignite inside. Their will and resolve return and the lightning-fire of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Potentia</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> first burns through them, re-shaping their body even as inspiration strikes them. Their faith in themselves is re-kindled, but the world still remains flawed, to their sight. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Drive</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The drive of the Progenitors is to </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>create</i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">. They cannot help but see the world in terms of what could be made or built upon, beside or in place of that which already exists. Although they are inherently creative, they find it difficult to help but see the flaws in what </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>is </i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">and not think that they could build better, regardless of the truth of the matter (altogether too many Builders fancy themselves master architects when they are, at best, mediocre, if that). </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Progenitors are often found in positions where they can exercise their creative urges. Architecture and the arts are perennial favourites, but many take up careers in politics or business, where they can build the closest things to empires possible in this modern age. It is rare to find a Builder without means, as even those in professions which would normally see them living hand-to-mouth such as a commissions artist tend to prosper, using Miracles or the effects of Halysis to sell their work. In general, whether by innate talent or supernatural power, Progenitors tend to be trend-setters rather than followers and, like all demigods, chafe at working under others.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Some of the Aspect of Creation aim far higher than others, seeking to shape not only the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">present,</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> but the world for years, decades and centuries to come. Some </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">take up</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> causes which they believe in - perhaps animal welfare, perhaps humanitarian causes such as AquAid - and make themselves the face of them (or at least their local branch). They try to make sweeping changes, hoping to make the adjustments in the collective consciousness that are required for lasting change.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Not all Builders are so benevolent, though. In fact, they are the Aspect most likely to build Cults (although not necessarily under that name) in the open. More than a few third-world dictators have Ascended to this Aspect and it is rare to find a Builder without a powerful vision of how this world should be. And where such visions exist, it is all too common to find someone who is willing to go to extraordinary - and often monstrous - lengths to see them through. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Followings</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The chosen Followings of the Demigods of Creation are most often those which look towards the future and see the Empyrean state as being a blessing of some kind. Of the most common Followings, the Followings of Ascendants, Embodiments, Sparks, Banners and the Eidolon are the ones most often chosen, although a Progenitor following the creed of the Annunaki, the Vassals or the Heirs is rarely enough to raise eyebrows.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cults</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">The Cults of the Builders tend to be some of the largest, as it\u2019s far easier to convince someone that you are good when you are trying to build something great than when you are tearing down anything that you disagree with. The Builders often try to recruit from those who have (and can lend) the power to build something new. They often count business leaders, politicians and similar among their followings, or at least more so than the other Aspects. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Cults to the Aspect of Creation are often some of the most structured, as the demigod at their heart tries to build them as best they can. They often end up with complex hierarchies of rank and holiness, with equally complex games of power as cultists compete for the favour of the demigod. In this way, the cults of the Progenitors are at once both rigidly structured and chaotic, as cultists rise and fall.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">More commonly than in other cults (perhaps save those of the demigods of Order), the cults of the Builders tend to have rich and deep mythologies, in which the demigod is, if not the principal actor, then at least a major character. These are not necessarily traditional mythologies, as they are most often based on the demigod\u2019s Following and incorporate significant figures from its mythology, but they are universally compelling. Many Builder cults will gather on sacred holidays and recite tales of their deeds and those of their patron. More than a few archive these stories, turning them into a growing mythos of the God and his Blessed Followers.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">As the Builders themselves are - generally speaking - divided between those who hold dominion over nature and those who rule the creations of humankind, their cults tend to be similarly aligned. Many of the cults of the Progenitors revere the demigod as a manifestation of the power of nature, but just as many see him as something more approaching a messiah, come to deliver them and the rest of humanity from its own sin and evil and to create a better tomorrow. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Domains</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Perhaps unsurprisingly, the Builders typically manifest Domains which are creative in nature, with a not-insignificant number being patrons of the arts and sciences. However, there is a demographic split in the Aspect between the demigods who mostly hold Domains concerned with human endeavours and those who hold Domains over the growth and flourishing of nature and the natural world.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Common Domains include plants, animals, inspiration, light, health, earth, crafts, metal and water. Relatively few Builders manifest the powers of the ephemeral elements of fire and air and tend not to have power over the dead, although power over the denizens of the Shadow is not unheard of.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Concepts</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Charismatic cult leader, corporate empire-builder, master sculptor, visionary terrorist, eco-warrior, famous architect</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Stereotypes</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Destruction: </b>Our natural opposites, and yet how can one make art without a clean canvas?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Chaos:</b> A stagnant civilization is destined for destruction. That\u2019s what these guys are for.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Order: </b>Now these guys are like publishers. You need them to sort out your stuff but they always <i>edit</i>.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Vampires: </b>Not in my empire.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Werewolves:</b> These guys understand the importance of territory. And every king needs hunting dogs.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Mages: </b>Every emperor needs advisors and philosophers. Just make sure you know what they\u2019re up to behind your back.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Beasts:</b> Our opposite number, us gods to their monsters. It\u2019s always good to have a stick, though, for when the carrot isn\u2019t enough. They're good for that.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><b>Mummies:</b> Undead servants of dead gods, keeping alive the memory of a dead </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">empire,</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"> when they can. I wonder if mine will be remembered as long.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Mortals:</b> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">How can you stand living in something you didn\u2019t build with your own hands? I don\u2019t know how I ever managed.</span></span></span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-06-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:20:06-07:00","id":943533,"title":"","content":"The description of the Creators looks very good to me, and it will be much easier for anyone who wants to attempt to complete one of the other Aspects now that they have a finished example. In particular, I liked the split between the creation as the living growth of natural life vs. human creativity. Also, the descriptions of how the Builders' ethos influenced their interactions with the followings and their own cults both made sense and provides them with a distinct flavor without being restrictive.<br /> <br /> The only issue I see is with the Stereotypes: only the Destruction and Order aspects (and possibly Vampires) seem like comments that only a Builder would make. The other statements could make sense for any Demigod to say, and the Mummy Stereotype in particular seems inappropriate since it references using Mummies as a weapon when this aspect is all about creating new things rather than attacking what already exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","user":"Alastor","date":". 08-04-2016, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:36:58-07:00","id":943536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=943533#post943533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of the Creators looks very good to me, and it will be much easier for anyone who wants to attempt to complete one of the other Aspects now that they have a finished example. In particular, I liked the split between the creation as the living growth of natural life vs. human creativity. Also, the descriptions of how the Builders' ethos influenced their interactions with the followings and their own cults both made sense and provides them with a distinct flavor without being restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=943533#post943533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only issue I see is with the Stereotypes: only the Destruction and Order aspects (and possibly Vampires) seem like comments that only a Builder would make. The other statements could make sense for any Demigod to say, and the Mummy Stereotype in particular seems inappropriate since it references using Mummies as a weapon when this aspect is all about creating new things rather than attacking what already exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you mean. i'll have another look at those and see what i can do. I can't thank you enough for the feedback. It makes everything so much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T04:44:50-07:00","id":943541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=943533#post943533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only issue I see is with the Stereotypes: only the Destruction and Order aspects (and possibly Vampires) seem like comments that only a Builder would make. The other statements could make sense for any Demigod to say, and the Mummy Stereotype in particular seems inappropriate since it references using Mummies as a weapon when this aspect is all about creating new things rather than attacking what already exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's an updated version.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stereotypes</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Destruction:</b> Our natural opposites, and yet how can one make art without a clean canvas?</li> <li><b>Chaos: </b>A stagnant civilization is destined for destruction. That\u2019s what these guys are for.</li> <li><b>Order: </b>Now these guys are like publishers. You need them to sort out your stuff but they always <i>edit</i>.</li> <li><b>Vampires:</b> Not in my empire.</li> <li><b>Werewolves: </b>These guys understand the importance of territory. And every king needs hunting dogs.</li> <li><b>Mages:</b> Every emperor needs advisors and philosophers. Just make sure you know what they\u2019re up to behind your back.</li> <li><b>Beasts: </b>Our opposite number, us gods to their monsters. It\u2019s always good to have a stick, though, for when the carrot isn\u2019t enough. They're good for that.</li> <li><b>Mummies:</b> Undead servants of dead gods, keeping alive the memory of a dead empire, when they can. I wonder if mine will be remembered as long.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mortals:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How can you stand living in something you didn\u2019t build with your own hands? I don\u2019t know how I ever managed.</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T15:35:46-07:00","id":943941,"title":"","content":"I noticed your post in the Cults for Everyone thread and I figured it would be easier to respond here. Instead of using the old material, why not use the updated stuff I've come up with? Ignore the last two pages of the document, I'm still trying to toy with Totem mechanics to see if they would work just as well with other Ephemeral Beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_VOpIH9hXNwZkJwZzMwOXBNaEk/view\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_VOpIH9hXNwZkJwZzMwOXBNaEk/view\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_VOpIH9hXNwZkJwZzMwOXBNaEk/view\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_VOpIH9hXNwZkJwZzMwOXBNaEk/view </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T01:09:40-07:00","id":944186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=943941#post943941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed your post in the Cults for Everyone thread and I figured it would be easier to respond here. Instead of using the old material, why not use the updated stuff I've come up with? Ignore the last two pages of the document, I'm still trying to toy with Totem mechanics to see if they would work just as well with other Ephemeral Beings.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_VOpIH9hXNwZkJwZzMwOXBNaEk/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_V...MwOXBNaEk/view</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks very much! Do you mind if I just copy-paste it into the thing (with a few alterations so that it fits a little better)? <br /> <br /> Also, I don't suppose I could trouble you to have a quick look at the Creation Aspect above, could I?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:41:32-07:00","id":946325,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, the break from making things is done and I'm ready to post and help on this project as well. :3<br /> <br /> I like how the Creation Aspect looks perhaps my only criticism is the Stereotypes for Creators. They sound like they're more in line with the Order Aspect than with the Creation Aspect. If I may be so bold as to suggest alternative ones?<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires: </b>They bear no spark of creation, they are pitiful creatures who can only corrupt all they touch.<br /> <b>Werewolves: </b>Such base creatures who know only how to hunt and take away.<br /> <b>Mages: </b>If their magic could withstand the test of their mortal peers, perhaps they could nearly match us. I don't know whether that gives me awe or fear of their potential.<br /> <b>Beasts: </b>For all their claims of relationship, they only create fear. Perhaps what the monster creates, it may not take back?<br /> <b>Mummies:</b> *no change*<br /> <b>Mortals:</b> *no change*<br /> <br /> Although if I may suggest one fitting one for Creation to have. :3<br /> <br /> <b>Genius: </b>There is such a terrible beauty in what they do, one I understand very well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:01:36-07:00","id":946489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=946325#post946325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alrighties, the break from making things is done and I'm ready to post and help on this project as well. :3<br /> <br /> I like how the Creation Aspect looks perhaps my only criticism is the Stereotypes for Creators. They sound like they're more in line with the Order Aspect than with the Creation Aspect. If I may be so bold as to suggest alternative ones?<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires: </b>They bear no spark of creation, they are pitiful creatures who can only corrupt all they touch.<br /> <b>Werewolves: </b>Such base creatures who know only how to hunt and take away.<br /> <b>Mages: </b>If their magic could withstand the test of their mortal peers, perhaps they could nearly match us. I don't know whether that gives me awe or fear of their potential.<br /> <b>Beasts: </b>For all their claims of relationship, they only create fear. Perhaps what the monster creates, it may not take back?<br /> <b>Mummies:</b> *no change*<br /> <b>Mortals:</b> *no change*<br /> <br /> Although if I may suggest one fitting one for Creation to have. :3<br /> <br /> <b>Genius: </b>There is such a terrible beauty in what they do, one I understand very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice to see you back again!<br /> <br /> I can agree with you on the stereotypes. They were probably the thing I was least satisfied with, even the revised ones. I certainly like yours and to be honest, Genius had completely slipped my mind for some reason. I might put them here and move mummies over to order or destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:05:53-07:00","id":946495,"title":"","content":"Another idea for vampires:<br /> <br /> &quot;A race of immortals who craft nothing but lies. Creatures worthy only of pity and cleansing fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:34:16-07:00","id":946515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=946489#post946489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice to see you back again!<br /> <br /> I can agree with you on the stereotypes. They were probably the thing I was least satisfied with, even the revised ones. I certainly like yours and to be honest, Genius had completely slipped my mind for some reason. I might put them here and move mummies over to order or destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why thank you. :3 <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I mostly suggested Genius because their themes of Inspiration (and how horrible it can go) and creation of Wonders seems like something that the Creation Aspect would comment on.</span></span></span> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=946495#post946495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea for vampires:<br /> <br /> &quot;A race of immortals who craft nothing but lies. Creatures worthy only of pity and cleansing fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might sound better for Vampires. Since stereotypes are supposed to be a view from the outside and the factor that Vampires lack the spark of life is only well known to those who deal with vampires regularly.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm ready to begin trying my hand on an aspect. Would it be fine if I began on Chaos? I don't know why, I've just always had a liking for the kinds of gods in mythology listen under them (Set, Susano-oo, Loki, etc :3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T15:47:11-07:00","id":946522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=946515#post946515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why thank you. :3 [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm ready to begin trying my hand on an aspect. Would it be fine if I began on Chaos? I don't know why, I've just always had a liking for the kinds of gods in mythology listen under them (Set, Susano-oo, Loki, etc :3).</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means. The next one I was going to work on was Destruction, so if you can make a start on Chaos that would be more than appreciated. And yeah, the chaos gods are fun (especially Loki). I don't blame you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:11:49-07:00","id":946596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=946522#post946522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By all means. The next one I was going to work on was Destruction, so if you can make a start on Chaos that would be more than appreciated. And yeah, the chaos gods are fun (especially Loki). I don't blame you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties, time to see what I can do. And to note beforehand, you are free to take whatever I post for this project and revise or change it to however you wish. :3<br /> <br /> <b>Chaos<br /> The Aspect of the Trickster<br /> The Storm-Callers<br /> The Unbound</b><br /> <br /> <b>Introduction</b><br /> Ever since the figures of order and authority have been established in different faiths, there has always existed an equal and yet opposite to them in the form of the trickster and chaos bringers. These gods were devoted to the subversion of supreme rule, the ideal of broken laws and crossing set boundaries. The other aspects know them as anarchists, malcontents (mainly by the Order Aspected), and yet also as revolutionaries who take the way that nobody else has figured to use.<br /> <br /> Although the Chaos Aspected don't just play their unbound role in the mortal world, but they also serve as Devil's Advocates and subverters of rule between their Demigod bretheren. Like how Loki, the Trickster God, had caused as much trouble for his fellow Aesir as he did fix it. Or the legendary god Prometheus, who brought the divine fire to mortals so they wouldn't starve or freeze and who taught them how to give scraps of offerings to the Gods and leave the bulk for themselves to survive.<br /> <br /> Although, the Chaos Aspected still need their trickery to be laced with caution. For without it, they risk being cast down from their positions like so many of the legendary inspirations of the Chaos Demigod. Susano'o, Loki, Set, Prometheus, even Lucifer are cautionary tales of Chaos who take it too far...or at least, got caught.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascension </b><br /> Those who ascend to the Aspect of Chaos tend to be amongst the most creative, and sometimes very deceptive, beings before their Ascension. They were perhaps amongst those never satisfied with the usual way of doing things, and so sought alternatives that seemed simpler than the established system. For example, if one told them to empty a tub of water and gave them a bucket, a spoon and a cup, the potential Chaos Aspected would choose to take the cork out of the drain. <br /> <br /> In the days before their Ascension, the most common blockage a Storm-Caller faces is simply one standard of conduct or authority that they simply cannot subvert. They could be a criminal trying to sell an utterly illegal substance, who fails every deal and even nearly gets caught by the police a couple of times. Perhaps they're a college student trying to find a way to cheat on their finals that their professor doesn't know of. In any case, the best way that the Ascension within the Aspect of Chaos can be called is a breakthrough. The criminal behind bars shatters them in a whirlwind of lightning. The student subverts his teacher's methods in a cascade of ill fortune. The Chaos Aspected view the world in terms of unlimited opportunity, all of them just begging to be taken.<br /> <br /> <b>Drive</b><br /> The Drive of the Storm Callers is <i>uncertain. </i>This doesn't mean that their drive is unknown, it simply means that the Unbound do not share any collective mission upon the world. Each of their perspectives is unique, different, something that is entirely their own viewpoint. And for each and every one of them, their ideal is to subvert that which would try to chain them down. But uncertainty isn't all bad, it merely gives way to infinite possibilities and opportunities, which present themselves to the Unbound who merely looks the right way.<br /> <br /> As such, the Storm Callers all tend to take a place where they are allowed the most flexibility for their ventures and can potentially find ways to get around the things that keep them from doing as they will. As spoken above, one can find those of the Chaos Aspect almost anywhere they care to look. Although the closest one can come to finding a common ground for the Unbound is usually within the ranks of criminal organizations, daily wanderers of countries or revolutions in places with oppressive authority.<br /> <br /> However, more than a few Unbound love playing the antagonist to their felllow Demigods, even those on the same side as they are. Be it for shits and giggles or usurping the authority of their fellows, it's almost never certain why they do what they do. Sometimes, it's because they can.<br /> <br /> Like other Demigods, the Storm Callers can be for good and for ill. One example is how the Chaos Aspected are amongst the least likely Demigods to create a Cult. Some of the Storm Callers believe it to be for the best, as they would enchain others through Halysis when their aspect is that of freedom and possibility. Some of the Unbound believe it's better to not have people who can give a name and face if someone's hunting you down. <br /> <br /> <b>Followings</b><br /> The Followings a Storm Caller would follow tend to be amongst those that allow the greatest amount of flexibility and are unburdened by obligation or supremacy. The most popular followings are those of Annunaki, Embodiments, Ascendants, and most popularly, the Following of the Morning Star. <br /> <br /> <b>Cults</b><br /> The Cults of the Storm Callers tend to be based upon the fringes of society. While they are usually away from public eye, the Cults dedicated to the Storm Callers are almost always made up by the common masses of people rather than people within important positions of society. Afterall, it's because of the common masses that people hold positions of power, so what better way than the unpredictable mess of the Chaos Aspected to follow? <br /> <br /> However, membership within the Chaos Aspected Cults tend to be as random as their Demigod up top. Seeing two people from completely different classes in the same place isn't an oddity within their Temples. The Cults tend to form in two ways. In the first version, the Cult is simply an informal gathering of people who follow the Unbound, believing that they bear unknown wisdom and beg them to show them the way. The second version is that the cult actively worships the Demigod, believing that a storm is on the horizon and that only those who are capable of calling the storm are just as capable of leading them through it with the least harm. <br /> <br /> <b>Domains</b><br /> The Domains of the Unbound hold power over the uncontrollable and untamed forces of the world, those which any and all mortals believe is beyond their grasp to hold. Perhaps strangely enough, a few of the Domains that may be controlled are almost relatively simple, something most mundane people wouldn't think is possible and yet still is.<br /> <br /> Common Domains include Nature, Weather, Fate, Conflict, Water, Air, even Emotions, Secrecy, Travelling or Thieves. Few Unbound hold onto anything that has an absolute or utterly defined meaning.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts</b><br /> Wandering drifter, Revolutionary idealist, Usurper King, Mad God, Scam artist, Criminal<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes</b><br /> <b>Creation: </b>What the great mom giveth, she also taketh away if not to her standards. <br /> <b>Destruction: </b>It's one thing to subvert, and it's another to destroy until nothing's left.<br /> <b>Order: </b>It's fun, watching how frustrated they get when their perfect organization is blasted to bits. Don't ever let them catch you though.<br /> <b>Vampires: </b>For such a self-killing governments they run, you slight one and they'll all come after you.<br /> <b>Werewolves: </b>You guys are crazy! Wanna hang out sometime?<br /> <b>Mages: </b>Be honest with them, and then tell them you're a trickster god. They'll never be sure whether they should trust you for the rest of their lives.<br /> <b>Changelings:</b> It feels like someone's toyed with them to the point where they broke. I should prolly give them a proper visit to say that that's my job.<br /> <b>Princesses: </b>Look at you, so self righteous and convinced of authority. Are you sure you have no skeletons in the closet?<br /> <b>Mortals: </b>Get ready, a storms blowing and nothing you can do can stop it!<br /> <br /> <b>Quote</b><br /> &quot;You can't stop the storm.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T01:00:48-07:00","id":946799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=946596#post946596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alrighties, time to see what I can do. And to note beforehand, you are free to take whatever I post for this project and revise or change it to however you wish. :3<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Chaos<br /> The Aspect of the Trickster<br /> The Storm-Callers<br /> The Unbound</b><br /> <br /> <b>Introduction</b><br /> Ever since the figures of order and authority have been established in different faiths, there has always existed an equal and yet opposite to them in the form of the trickster and chaos bringers. These gods were devoted to the subversion of supreme rule, the ideal of broken laws and crossing set boundaries. The other aspects know them as anarchists, malcontents (mainly by the Order Aspected), and yet also as revolutionaries who take the way that nobody else has figured to use.<br /> <br /> Although the Chaos Aspected don't just play their unbound role in the mortal world, but they also serve as Devil's Advocates and subverters of rule between their Demigod bretheren. Like how Loki, the Trickster God, had caused as much trouble for his fellow Aesir as he did fix it. Or the legendary god Prometheus, who brought the divine fire to mortals so they wouldn't starve or freeze and who taught them how to give scraps of offerings to the Gods and leave the bulk for themselves to survive.<br /> <br /> Although, the Chaos Aspected still need their trickery to be laced with caution. For without it, they risk being cast down from their positions like so many of the legendary inspirations of the Chaos Demigod. Susano'o, Loki, Set, Prometheus, even Lucifer are cautionary tales of Chaos who take it too far...or at least, got caught.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascension </b><br /> Those who ascend to the Aspect of Chaos tend to be amongst the most creative, and sometimes very deceptive, beings before their Ascension. They were perhaps amongst those never satisfied with the usual way of doing things, and so sought alternatives that seemed simpler than the established system. For example, if one told them to empty a tub of water and gave them a bucket, a spoon and a cup, the potential Chaos Aspected would choose to take the cork out of the drain.<br /> <br /> In the days before their Ascension, the most common blockage a Storm-Caller faces is simply one standard of conduct or authority that they simply cannot subvert. They could be a criminal trying to sell an utterly illegal substance, who fails every deal and even nearly gets caught by the police a couple of times. Perhaps they're a college student trying to find a way to cheat on their finals that their professor doesn't know of. In any case, the best way that the Ascension within the Aspect of Chaos can be called is a breakthrough. The criminal behind bars shatters them in a whirlwind of lightning. The student subverts his teacher's methods in a cascade of ill fortune. The Chaos Aspected view the world in terms of unlimited opportunity, all of them just begging to be taken.<br /> <br /> <b>Drive</b><br /> The Drive of the Storm Callers is <i>uncertain. </i>This doesn't mean that their drive is unknown, it simply means that the Unbound do not share any collective mission upon the world. Each of their perspectives is unique, different, something that is entirely their own viewpoint. And for each and every one of them, their ideal is to subvert that which would try to chain them down. But uncertainty isn't all bad, it merely gives way to infinite possibilities and opportunities, which present themselves to the Unbound who merely looks the right way.<br /> <br /> As such, the Storm Callers all tend to take a place where they are allowed the most flexibility for their ventures and can potentially find ways to get around the things that keep them from doing as they will. As spoken above, one can find those of the Chaos Aspect almost anywhere they care to look. Although the closest one can come to finding a common ground for the Unbound is usually within the ranks of criminal organizations, daily wanderers of countries or revolutions in places with oppressive authority.<br /> <br /> However, more than a few Unbound love playing the antagonist to their felllow Demigods, even those on the same side as they are. Be it for shits and giggles or usurping the authority of their fellows, it's almost never certain why they do what they do. Sometimes, it's because they can.<br /> <br /> Like other Demigods, the Storm Callers can be for good and for ill. One example is how the Chaos Aspected are amongst the least likely Demigods to create a Cult. Some of the Storm Callers believe it to be for the best, as they would enchain others through Halysis when their aspect is that of freedom and possibility. Some of the Unbound believe it's better to not have people who can give a name and face if someone's hunting you down.<br /> <br /> <b>Followings</b><br /> The Followings a Storm Caller would follow tend to be amongst those that allow the greatest amount of flexibility and are unburdened by obligation or supremacy. The most popular followings are those of Annunaki, Embodiments, Ascendants, and most popularly, the Following of the Morning Star.<br /> <br /> <b>Cults</b><br /> The Cults of the Storm Callers tend to be based upon the fringes of society. While they are usually away from public eye, the Cults dedicated to the Storm Callers are almost always made up by the common masses of people rather than people within important positions of society. Afterall, it's because of the common masses that people hold positions of power, so what better way than the unpredictable mess of the Chaos Aspected to follow?<br /> <br /> However, membership within the Chaos Aspected Cults tend to be as random as their Demigod up top. Seeing two people from completely different classes in the same place isn't an oddity within their Temples. The Cults tend to form in two ways. In the first version, the Cult is simply an informal gathering of people who follow the Unbound, believing that they bear unknown wisdom and beg them to show them the way. The second version is that the cult actively worships the Demigod, believing that a storm is on the horizon and that only those who are capable of calling the storm are just as capable of leading them through it with the least harm.<br /> <br /> <b>Domains</b><br /> The Domains of the Unbound hold power over the uncontrollable and untamed forces of the world, those which any and all mortals believe is beyond their grasp to hold. Perhaps strangely enough, a few of the Domains that may be controlled are almost relatively simple, something most mundane people wouldn't think is possible and yet still is.<br /> <br /> Common Domains include Nature, Weather, Fate, Conflict, Water, Air, even Emotions, Secrecy, Travelling or Thieves. Few Unbound hold onto anything that has an absolute or utterly defined meaning.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts</b><br /> Wandering drifter, Revolutionary idealist, Usurper King, Mad God, Scam artist, Criminal<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes</b><br /> <b>Creation: </b>What the great mom giveth, she also taketh away if not to her standards.<br /> <b>Destruction: </b>It's one thing to subvert, and it's another to destroy until nothing's left.<br /> <b>Order: </b>It's fun, watching how frustrated they get when their perfect organization is blasted to bits. Don't ever let them catch you though.<br /> <b>Vampires: </b>For such a self-killing governments they run, you slight one and they'll all come after you.<br /> <b>Werewolves: </b>You guys are crazy! Wanna hang out sometime?<br /> <b>Mages: </b>Be honest with them, and then tell them you're a trickster god. They'll never be sure whether they should trust you for the rest of their lives.<br /> <b>Changelings:</b> It feels like someone's toyed with them to the point where they broke. I should prolly give them a proper visit to say that that's my job.<br /> <b>Princesses: </b>Look at you, so self righteous and convinced of authority. Are you sure you have no skeletons in the closet?<br /> <b>Mortals: </b>Get ready, a storms blowing and nothing you can do can stop it!<br /> <br /> <b>Quote</b><br /> &quot;You can't stop the storm.&quot;<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um. Wow. That was very quick. Colour me impressed. On the whole, it looks very good. I might make a few small edits, but for the most part it looks perfect. I'll have to step up my game with Destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T09:02:42-07:00","id":946983,"title":"","content":"To keep up with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a> , here's the Aspect of Destruction, otherwise known as the Reapers, the grim-faced gods of death and destruction. I might have made them too grimdark in contrast to the other Aspects, but I'll leave that up to my lovely readers and helpers.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u>Destruction</u></span></span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Aspect of the Adversary</span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Reapers</span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Devourers</span></span></b></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[e.g. Hades, Thanatos, Anubis, Cipactli, Nidhoggr, Wendigo, Uoke, Shiva, Ninurta]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Introduction</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">People say that there are only two certainties in life: birth and death. Both of these ultimate fates are well-represented in mythology, birth by the myriad mother- and fertility-deities and death by the great adversaries of the many pantheons of the world. Perhaps it goes by the name of Thanatos, Cipactli, Shiva or Azrael but there is always some kind of death-figure, the keeper of the doorway into the great beyond. Not all are so dutiful as to aid humanity in their crossing, but all are more than willing to send them on their way.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Among demigods, those Aspected to Destruction are rarely fully trusted, except perhaps by close friends or members of the same Pantheon. As a result, they tend to stick to the edges of demigod society, taking positions in Followings which allow them to make use of their destructive talents. More than a few hunt down the monsters that can crawl from the Tree, while others become inquisitors and witchfinders, securing the territories of their Followings and Pantheons from outside threats, some far stranger than Titanspawn monsters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like many of their mythical forbears, the Devourers often find a place for themselves in isolation. Like Hades in the Underworld, they closet themselves away in Gardr and stranger realms, sometimes finding beings there which comfort and aid them. Of course, there are those who swim against the current and dance while they can, taking after such merry death-gods as Baron Samedi and drinking 'til death.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ascension</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Those who Ascend to the Aspect of Destruction are often those who see the flaws in the world, even before that trait is exacerbated and amplified by the Ascension itself. They are most often those who have been wronged by the current state of affairs. Whether that comes in the forms of government-imposed sanctions on their race or religion, unbearable superiors or even a simple chance of birth that placed them in a less prosperous neighbourhood or a poor third-world country. Needless to say, they are often troubled before their Ascension and even more so afterwards.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Almost without exception, a Reaper\u2019s Ascension is brought on by an insurmountable obstacle. Perhaps this is a long-standing opposition such as an unfair teacher without whose grades the demigod will never make college, or it might be something altogether more immediate, such as an entrenched enemy position. The frustration of this situation accrues, whether quickly or slowly, and eventually erupts in a conflagration of divine fury.<br /> <br /> he Ascensions of the Reapers are rarely peaceful or gentle. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Often, their first Miracles are wrathful and destructive, invoked to lash out at the obstacles which barred them from the life which they believed that they should have, regardless of whether they would actually help. A young demigod incinerates the bullies which have harassed him since his first day at school. Another\u2019s battle cries shout the fanatics who\u2019ve got his squad pinned down right out of their bodies, creating tormented ghosts which he binds to his will, even as his aura burns out the minds of his buddies. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Drive</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Reapers are driven to destroy, in the name of a better tomorrow. They cannot help but see the world as cracked, flawed, stained with its vices and horrors. They see the worst and must often force themselves to see that there </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>are</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> things worth fighting for, that the world is not completely irredeemable. They are often the Aspect which clings most desperately to their human lives, for surrendering to the terrible divinity within them would bring only ruin, for them and those around them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In terms of positions in life, Devourers (or at least the less megalomaniacal and nihilistic ones) tend to make a place for themselves where they can exercise their destructive urges while helping others, or at least where they can channel them to useful ends. Among the Reapers, assassins, criminals and hitmen are common, as are policemen, special ops (or ex-special ops) and other military types. For those with a more social bent, many go into law and tear apart the defenses or prosecutions of criminals.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Followings</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Devourers most often join Followings that allow them to either project the blame for their state onto another - like the Following of Vassals, Embodiments or the Nine Circles - or to justify it with a cause, such as the Following of the Morningstar. A relatively large amount of Devourers join or found minor Followings tailor-made to their particular issues. Such groups rarely outlast their founders or spread far, considering their inevitable focus on destruction and death as virtues or necessities of some sort, but rumours persist among demigods that there is a far-reaching and secretive Following composed solely of Reapers and dedicated to bringing about the apocalypse. It may be no more than a viral idea, similar to the Illuminati, but it is true that throughout history those who are not accepted and trusted turn to other in a similar situation...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cults</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The cults of the Reapers are almost universally small and tightly-knit, with most of the group having close personal connection to the demigod at their heart. Most are focused around the demigod\u2019s representation of death or destruction, either as an inevitable end, an apotheosis or an endless cycle, depending on that particular demigod\u2019s views on his Aspect and its connotations. Some are solemn and serious sects, gathering to study the next great adventure with tomes of old magic and strange lore. Others are convivial and lively, more like a party or a wake than a funeral.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reaper cults often build up complex mythologies and theories on death and what comes after, although less in the narrative manner of a Progenitor's tales and more similarly to the Orphic cults or Enochian magic. Many such cults possess supernatural power beyond that of their patron, with a relatively large number of cultists dealing with ghosts, spirits and other ephemeral beings or exhibiting minor supernatural or psychic abilities. A not-insignificant number of Reaper cults have some kind of contact with the Underworld, som having reliable access to an Avernian Gate and the means to open it while others have the means to summon spirits and ghosts from the Great Black to consult for wisdom or bind to tasks if necessary.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Another common trend in Devourer cults is that they have a defined purpose, outside of venerating the demigod and spreading their gospel. This might be to help others through the transition into death or aiding those who have already passed over and linger as ghosts. It might be a more mundane purpose, such as acting as a personal protection or assassination agency.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Domains</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The common Domains of the Reapers are, unsurprisingly, those which relate to death, destruction, entropy and dissolution. They hold power over the things which are inevitable in this life, the rot and the cold that creep through old houses and the hate and bitterness which steal into envious hearts. Some even have a certain dominion over the very fate that drives men to their deaths. At the same time, some rule more spectacular Domains of fire, weather, air and water, the elements which wear away and consume the works of man. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Miracles wielded by the Reapers are terrible to behold and earn them their names as Devourers. Common Domains include water, cold, fire, weather, death, ghosts, rot, fate, emotion and conflict.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Concepts</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Necromantic assassin, death cult leader, Drasil explorer, monster hunter, serial killer, ruthless lawyer.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stereotypes</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Creation:</b> So arrogant, believing that their creations will last forever. I can already see the cracks.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Chaos:</b> Our partners in crime.</li> <li><b>Order:</b> They think that their works will be preserved? Please. Complete order requires that all motion cease. And what is that, but death?</li> <li><b>Vampires:</b> Walking corpses, clinging to what tattered shreds of humanity remain. If I had died, we could be cousins.</li> <li><b>Werewolves:</b> Their rage is a weapon more destructive than any other in their arsenal. If only they could learn to aim it.</li> <li><b>Mages:</b> What hubris, to make Death a school of magic.</li> <li><b>Sin-Eaters:</b> What strange creatures, to escape death so easily and still dance in its aftermath. I don\u2019t know if they\u2019re abominations or marvels.</li> <li><b>Mortals: </b>Fear the Reaper. You\u2019ll live longer that way. I\u2019ve seen what comes next and it isn\u2019t pretty.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Quote</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cThe time will come for all of us, sooner or later. Even me. You though, have a choice. So, sooner or later?\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-09-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:37:22-07:00","id":947068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=946799#post946799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um. Wow. That was very quick. Colour me impressed. On the whole, it looks very good. I might make a few small edits, but for the most part it looks perfect. I'll have to step up my game with Destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And there's no need to rush on making things, it's better to take your time than do a bunch of things at once and run out of inspiration. ^^ <br /> <br /> But yes, the Destruction Aspect looks awesome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:15:54-07:00","id":947108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=947068#post947068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And there's no need to rush on making things, it's better to take your time than do a bunch of things at once and run out of inspiration. ^^<br /> <br /> But yes, the Destruction Aspect looks awesome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thanks. And it's probably my biggest problem with writing stuff: I need a kick in the pants to get working on stuff, one which you provided most kindly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:20:16-07:00","id":948060,"title":"","content":"Chaos &amp; Destruction both look great.<br /> <br /> If it's all right with the two of you, I'd like to try my hand at the Order Aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T14:31:42-07:00","id":948070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=948060#post948060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chaos &amp; Destruction both look great.<br /> <br /> If it's all right with the two of you, I'd like to try my hand at the Order Aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely! Have fun with it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just one thing, though, I was thinking of Order demigods being primarily based on teacher-gods like Athena, Quetzalcoatl and Thoth, as well as the ones which 'order' the world in myth, like Zeus, Marduk and Huitzilopochtli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:08:52-07:00","id":948494,"title":"","content":"Thank you, ajf115.<br /> <br /> I didn't see your note until after the aspect was mostly written, so it may not have the themes you were looking for. On the other hand, there was already an element of &quot;let me show you the right way to do this&quot;, which one might consider &quot;education&quot; of a sort. Feel free to change anything you like, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Order</b><br /> <b>The Aspect of the Judge<br /> The Binders<br /> The Grid-Mappers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Introduction</b><br /> Almost every culture can point to some figure who introduced its traditions. Such heroes stand at the border between civilization and the disarray that came before. They are the unifiers, the teachers, the lawgivers who ensure that everyone and everything takes their proper place in society. The Order-Aspected are the modern day inheritors of this mantle. They take the disarray they see around them and replace it with harmony. Mortals and other Demigods may not always appreciate their enforcement of the rules, but they know that the world needs a responsible hand to keep running smoothly.<br /> <br /> There is also another archetype in which Grid-Mappers see themselves: that of the rulers and judges who administer law throughout the cosmos. The two roles feed into each other, for each time a Binder tries perfect the system, they find themselves having to deal with dozen trespasses against the existing order to deal with (often by their nemeses, the Chaos-Aspected) and each time they attempt to interpret and enforce the existing laws, they find places that could be streamlined.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascension </b><br /> Mortals destined to become Grid-Mappers tend toward rigid personalities from a young age. Some may belong to the classic workaholic \u201cType A\u201d, while others may be more introverted, but all share traits like perfectionism and a love of routine which lead them to demand that the world around them conform to certain standards.<br /> <br /> Those about to ascend under the Aspect of Order find themselves in situations they cannot control. Often this is one in which others expect them to bring about impossible results, but at other times only their own impulses demand they latch down on the chaos around them. Whether they find themselves in a new position that involves more than the job description implied or are suddenly tasked with gathering their unruly family for a wedding or funeral, the future Grid-Mapper is confronted with a swirl of anarchy with no way to make sense of it.<br /> <br /> Ascension itself often comes as a relief, not only to the new Demigods, but to those around them. The first miracles are half unconscious and many times subtle enough that onlookers might not recognize the supernatural at work. Everything simply seems to come together as it should under the Binder\u2019s gaze. Oddly, this new order isn\u2019t always what the Demigod would have wanted before ascending; frequently a Builder sees a hidden harmony in what had once seemed discordant, and might act in the future to spread this influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Drive</b><br /> The Order-Aspected have a drive to <i>control</i>. Each has a sense of the rightness about certain things: laws that should never be broken, procedures that should always be followed, authorities which should always be respected. If others do not acknowledge these rules, then the Grid-Mapper feels compelled to make them obey. At the extreme, some Binders have a plan for the entire universe to follow, and a willingness to force it into the mold they have made for it.<br /> <br /> In their mundane lives, Grid-Mappers seek positions of authority from which to punish those who violate their strictures or to promote their broader social agendas. Legal careers are thus quite common. Politics and business are even more so, for in these fields an unscrupulous Demigod can leverage Halysis and Cults to expand their influence even more quickly. Even the Binders who don\u2019t seek to advance themselves in the halls of power tend to move in the same circles as those who do, as they always seem to have a new suggestion for how things could be run a little more efficiently, how justice could be a bit more just or the world a little more perfect.<br /> <br /> <br /> Among Demigods, Binders are known for their honesty and effectiveness, at least in comparison to many who belong to other Aspects. The Grid-Mappers are often trusted, but seldom liked by their fellow Demigods, who resent their habit of interference with whatever they believe needs to be fixed.<br /> <br /> <b>Followings</b><br /> Order entails both leadership and submission in their proper places, so the Followings of Banners and Vassals have the greatest percentage of Binders amongst their membership. Next in popularity are Ascendents and Sparks, each of which has an agenda for Grid-Mappers to embrace and impose upon the world, as well as the Embodiments, who propose a place for each Demigod in the natural order. However, all the larger Followings have members of this Aspect, even ones that seem counterintuitive like the Following of the Nine Circles. The Order-Aspected are among the most politically involved Demigods, and the more arrogant of them like to claim that a Following without one of them to lead it (or at least keep the books) is doomed to soon fall apart.<br /> <br /> <b>Cults</b><br /> Grid-Mappers generally invest heavily in their cults, crafting them into microcosms of how each Binder believes society itself should behave. This isn\u2019t to say that the cults of the Order-Aspected are always the largest (although they do tend to be among the higher profile, often with registered religion status or disguised as another legitimate group). Rare indeed is the Binder who would prefer a larger or more influential cult to one which is fully under control, and thus much of the effort an Order-Aspected Demigod puts into a cult is to mitigate the effect of Halysis on its actions. The most common method is to have every decision personally approved by the Grid-Mapper at the cult\u2019s lead, but democratic mechanisms have sometimes been used to keep the most important decisions out of the hands of a Halysis-ridden leadership, and the most thoughtful Binders have designed position-rotation scheme which keep any one member of their cults from too high a threshold. Of course, each of these methods is usually backed by careful screening of potential members before they are permitted to join at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> The mythology of a Grid-Mapper\u2019s cult is often almost pedestrian, a mere chronicle the members keep of their deity\u2019s life story, detailing mundane events together with the supernatural ones. Sometimes even the Binder\u2019s exploits are relegated to the background, and the cultists instead recount their own histories: what brought them to the cult and what they\u2019ve accomplished in the Demigod\u2019s service. When deeper cosmology is included however, it can become wildly detailed, as those Grid-Mappers who care enough to explore such mysteries at all want to expose the truth of the world to their followers with as much accuracy as they can uncover.<br /> <br /> Binders\u2019 cults are the most likely of those belonging to any Aspect to survive the death or Second Ascension of the leading Demigod. Some such groups are eventually taken over by another member of the Grid-Mapper\u2019s Following, but many go on to become purely mundane organizations, their religious origins forgotten or taken as legend.<br /> <br /> <b>Domains</b><br /> The Binders exhibit great variety in the Domains they command, for they are unwilling to let anything slip entirely out of their grip. Oftentimes they work deliberately to hone their control over a particular force which they consider essential, although the mysterious powers of Demigods are not always as easily trained as the Grid-Mappers would like. When they work together, they frequently divide the elements of the world between them, and expect each to master an allotted domain.<br /> <br /> The most common Domains are abstract concepts like Truth, Obedience, Knowledge, and Excellence. Oftentimes, the first Domain a Grid-Mapper masters reflects the thing they most felt was missing or eventually came to love in the situation which led to their Ascension, and one of the goals many Binders have is to spread the influence of their first Domain, even if it is something as specific and physical as Snow or Dogs.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts</b><br /> Warden of the Drasil, Lobbyist, Would-Be King, Divine Bureaucrat, Codifier of Lore, Critic<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes</b><br /> <b>Creation: </b>They can be great allies, when not being touchy about the improvements you make to their creations.<br /> <b>Chaos:</b> Just let them have their fun and set things back in order once they get bored and wander off.<br /> <b>Destruction:</b> Most of what they destroy is not worth keeping anyway. It can be a useful thing to have someone to deal with the garbage.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires: </b>Their society is not one I would care to be part of, but one has to appreciate the way they police themselves.<br /> <b>Werewolves: </b>A conundrum: leave them alone, and they claim territory all over your kingdom. Get rid of them, and suddenly possessions and mutant vermin start showing up.<br /> <b>Mages: </b>Many of them are kindred spirits, but if you work with them on anything be sure to handle the miracles yourself. Something always goes wrong when they use their magic.<br /> <b>Changelings:</b> They are all a little unstable, but once they make you a promise they usually keep it. That is more than can be said for most Demigods.<br /> <b>Demons (Unchained):</b> Rebels and spies; you cannot believe a word they say. Get them to move on if you notice them, but it is not worth hunting for them if you do not.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortals: </b>They just need a little education and we will finally have them doing things right.<br /> <br /> <b>Quote</b><br /> &quot; If you would just listen to me, we could make everything so much better!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T05:48:46-07:00","id":948540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=948494#post948494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, ajf115.<br /> <br /> I didn't see your note until after the aspect was mostly written, so it may not have the themes you were looking for. On the other hand, there was already an element of &quot;let me show you the right way to do this&quot;, which one might consider &quot;education&quot; of a sort. Feel free to change anything you like, of course.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Marvellous! I'm a bit busy now, but I'll get back to you with what i thought of it after reading it through thoroughly.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much to both of you for your help with this. I think what needs to be done next is probably finishing writing up the Followings. I'll post what I've got so far of the main ones as soon as I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T08:01:19-07:00","id":948613,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I think that the ones which need the most work are the Followings of Descendants, Ascendants, the Nine Circles, Banners and Embodiments, while the rest could probably do with </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(more than) </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">a little more fleshing out. Primarily what I'd like to do is get them into a format like this:</span><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Introduction<br /> <br /> Philosophy<br /> <br /> Organisation<br /> <br /> Factions<br /> <br /> Emblems</b></span></u><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> (Miracle specialities [name subject to change])</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Numinous Forms<br /> <br /> Stereotypes</b></u><br /> <br /> They don't need to be nearly as long as Aspects, perhaps 1/2 a page to a page per Following.</span><br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Following of Heirs</b></span></u></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This following believes that the gods worshipped by previous religions either never existed or have died, and that Demigods are the creation of humankind's collective soul to fill the void. Some believe that demigodhood is the eventual destiny of every human being, while others merely consider themselves shepherds of humanity's aspirations, a role they try to fulfill in different ways.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They tend to be the most modern in their outlook of all the followings, and often dismiss older religions as steps (or even wrong turns) on the path that lead to the current generation of Demigods.They have no qualms about taking faith from worshippers or temples of other religions, but their own Temples and Cults are usually started in their own names or that of their personal ideals, and incorporate all of the improvements which a particular Heir sees in society since the major world religions were founded.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unlike the other followings, the Heirs are almost unanimous in seeing Second Ascension as a bad thing. They believe themselves to be empowered directly by the aspirations of humanity, and so deduce that losing Attachment would completely destroy those who have become more faith than human themselves.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Numinous forms in this following are among the least flashy, since the Heirs see themselves more as &quot;Humanity+&quot; than as something dramatically different. Increased size, astonishing beauty, or unearthly grace are often the only things which distinguish their numinous forms from their regular ones.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Following of Sparks</u></span></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This following believes that there is only one thing which is truly divine, faith itself. Demigods are the result when humans have a great concentration of Faith.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Members of this following tend to collect faith from members of all religions equally, seeing each as a similar means for faith to express itself in the world. They seldom belong to an organized mortal religion themselves, but some may believe that the worldwide sea of Faith is itself conscious and thus be able to reconcile it with some form of monotheism or pantheism (there are virtually no polytheists among them - the Sparks believe that polytheistic religions originally followed Demigods who have long since Ascended for the second time and thus no longer have individual consciousness). The Following of Sparks is itself more like a religion than most of the other Followings: unlike the following of Reincarnates, they believe in a higher power which should be served, and unlike the Following of Vassals, they have reached an agreement on roughly what this power is and what it wants. Simply put, it wants more of itself to be spread throughout the world. Sparks accomplish this mission by spreading new Cults and founding new Temples, which tends to make them popular with other followings even if their reasons for doing so do not, for they create far more of these resources than they use themselves and are often willing to share.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sparks believe that Second Ascension is the process of becoming one with Faith again, and they see it not only the pinnacle and goal of their own existence, but of everyone else's as well.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The numinous forms in this following tend to be fiery or to radiate some other form of energy, reflecting the belief among followers that they are filled with the energy of faith.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Following of Reincarnates</u></span></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This following believes that each Demigod is the reincarnated form of some known deity from a known religion. What pantheon they believe themselves to hail from varies from Demigod to Demigod, but they have established techniques which they claim can verify a Demigod's original divine identity. Whether this actually works or not is of course a matter of faith, but true or not, the rites involved have led to this group's explosive growth over the past few decades, now that they have been freed from the embarrassment of having dozens of &quot;Thors&quot; and &quot;Dagdas&quot; at the same time, which once opened them to all manner of mockery. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reincarnates usually establish Temples and Cults based on the original religions of the gods they believe themselves to be, although they seldom place much emphasis on doing things exactly the same way as the ancients did. They consider themselves the ultimate authority within their own cults, and typically feel free to change things not only century to century but day to day as the mood strikes them. Occasionally a group of Reincarnates who believe themselves to hail from the same pantheon will create Cults and Temples which they share amongst themselves, in which case they tend to default more to the ancient example (as they understand it) as a compromise. Even more rarely, some Reincarnates may give space in their Cults/Temples to allies of their mythical persona whose reincarnation they've never met or who are believed to still enjoy True Godhood.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reincarnates are split on the issue of Second Ascension. Many believe that Demigods who vanish in this manner have returned to their otherworldly thrones, but others believe that Demigods who supposedly ascend for the second time actually find themselves starting over in a new mortal body. The rite of identity supports both theories: some of the ascended deities are replaced almost immediately, while other names never reappear.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The numinous forms in this following are the most varied, since each Demigod comes to resemble the god they believe themselves to be rather than any unified template. Common elements are a basically humanlike form, and signature weapons. Perhaps because it is a religion which already admits the possibility of reincarnation, Hindu deities are particularly likely to be claimed by reincarnates, so blue skin and multiple arms are frequent as well</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Following of Vassals</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This following believes that Demigods have been selected by the True God (or the True Goddess, or True Gods, plural) to be their servants on Earth. Unfortunately for them, they don't have much more insight into what their gods may want than mortals do, so they tend either to become scrupulous interpreters of holy texts, or to wander other worlds looking for beings who fit the description they have in mind (popular choices have been powerful spirits, Astral versions of various gods, and the Divine Fire - the God-Machine has been less popular, as it usually grinds Demigods who offer to serve it into raw material for new angels). This latter option makes them the following which interacts most frequently with other supernaturals, although not always in a positive way.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A majority of their members are of the monotheistic faiths, but there are also some who believe themselves to be servants of polytheistic deities. Their Cults and Temples almost invariably mirror their chosen faith, though there is something of a split between Vassals who found or latch onto relatively orthodox groups and those who start idiosyncratic sects who see a given Vassal as their primary</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Opinions on Second Ascension are also divided: most believe it to be the final reward for their service, with the polytheists among them believing that the True Gods promote worthy Demigods to their own ranks. However, a few believe that Second Ascension actually represents damnation or some form of demotion, and point to the fact that it is the Demigods who became most distant from humanity - and thus most distracted from their mission among humans - who are most likely to ascend again.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wings are the most common element tying together the numinous forms of this following, symbolizing their role as go between for the higher heavens and the mundane world.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Following of the Annunaki</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adherents to this Following believes that demigods are the heirs to an ancient bloodline or psychic inheritance implanted in humanity in the ancient past by some race of higher beings. The exact nature of these beings varies from demigod to demigod. Some believe that they were a hyper-advanced race of aliens, others that they were angels or some other kind of divine being, but the core tenet of the Following is that demigodhood is not natural but rather an engineered state, in some way. What demigods do with this belief is also extremely varied. Some seek to propagate this \u2018bloodline\u2019 physically, often making use of their cults to do so, while others believe that the conditions which allow Ascension are instead mental and seek to spread this through teaching. Some believe that the \u2018bloodline\u2019 was a failed experiment or perhaps a deliberate curse upon humanity, given the drawbacks of the Empyrean state. These often try to prevent the spread of what they see as a plague or destructive meme. More intellectually minded Followers often try to isolate the specific causes of Ascension, whether that be a gene, metaphysical markers, or a psychological state.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As a consequence of their divided opinions, the Following of the Annunaki is at once organised and fractious. Groups of adherents often form cliques and factions based on their personal positions, gathering like minded individuals and conflicting with those who oppose their views, sometimes with direct violence, sometimes in debate. These organisations vary in their structure according to their tenets as well, with those who strongly believe that Ascension is a blessing or curse often forming cultlike institutions dedicated to propagating or stymieing it, while those who wish to investigate it tend towards the more scientific structures, where each demigod investigates a different facet of the conundrum.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In their Numinous Forms, the Followers of the Annunaki tend towards the enormous shapes purported to have been worn by the ancient beings which their revere or despise. They often bear little in the way of flashy magical accoutrements and lean towards the physical, expressing their might with wings, claws and bulging muscles while their minds are augmented by elongated craniums and oversized brains.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For Domains, the Followers of the Annunaki often rule over similar concepts to those which their legendary \u2018ancestors\u2019 taught to early humankind, such as Law, Civilisation, Craftsmanship and Stone. Occasionally they command physical forces of nature such as the seas or the skies, but rarely do they hold power over ephemeral concepts such as death or life. This Following is profoundly rooted in the physical.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of Descendants</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Believe that they are heirs to a literal bloodline of divine beings from ages past (or more recent liaisons).</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of the Eidolon</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Following of Fragments believe that all demigods are projections of some higher being or beings into our reality, like fingers reaching into a pool of water. They differ in opinion on whether they have been severed from this \u2018higher\u2019 being or whether they are still connected to it, but they are still a - mostly - singular entity, unlike the Following of the Annunaki. The closest that the Following comes o a schism is between those who believe in a singular being of which all demigods are offshoots and those that believe that there is either a pantheon of \u2018eidolons\u2019 or that each demigod has their own. Either way, the philosophy of this Following is that ultimately, divinity can be contacted through looking deep into the self and finding the point at which the demigod becomes something greater than himself. Followers of this philosophy seek the god within and many command cults who seek similar enlightenment. They are at once one of the more peaceful Followings and one of the most dangerous, generally unwilling to go to extreme lengths to punish minor insults but having such absolute self-knowledge and discipline that facing one in battle is a terrifying prospect, as they know the exact limits of their -and often your - abilities. The many of the Followers of the Eidolon have, whether through personal revelation or through information exchange with other supernatural beings, discovered the existence of the Astral Realms, which they can access through their meditations or through one of the Roots of the Drasil.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In their Numinous Forms, Followers of the Eidolon often give the impression of being somehow distant from reality, untouchable and luminous things. Perhaps they are illuminated by a strange, sourceless light in no colour that a human has ever given a name to or perhaps they have grace enough to slip unharmed around blows which would have struck the head from a mortal. Perhaps they are simply immaterial, composed of nothing more than mist and vapour which can coalesce into a physical form when necessary. Occasionally a Follower\u2019s Numinous Form will seem incomplete somehow, as if it is a severed part of something else or has some kind of projection - perhaps wings or tendrils or branches reaching for the sky - which seems to link to something else.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of the Morningstar</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Other Names:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fallen, the Black-Winged, the Exiled</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ostensibly inspired by the famous Paradise Lost - which they claim was written by the very first of their Following as a metaphorical chronicle of His war against their greatest enemy, the Creator - the Following of the Morningstar believes that all demigods are (or were) angelic beings which were cast from some kind of Heaven to Earth (or perhaps left voluntarily) after rebelling against the Creator. Exactly what they rebelled for the sake of and what they were cast for depend on who you ask within the Following but one thread runs true: it was unjust, for not only did God (or Jehovah or Allah or the Great Spirit or whatever) take their power and their position from them, He robbed them of their very identities. He did not allow them even a </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>chance </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">to redeem themselves, instead simply casting them from His sight and mind. Many say that He could not kill them, as He had created them to be immortal, so He did the next best thing and made it so that there was next to no chance that they would ever recover themselves. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As an organisation, the Followers of the Morningstar have two main focuses: the recovery of their history and the pursuit of the Second Ascension, which they believe to be an Ascent back to Heaven, where they intend to make war upon the Creator again. Both of these goals are given equal importance, as without the power to oppose the Creator without knowledge of the past is to risk repeating history and without the power to exercise it, knowledge is worse than useless. To this end, the Followers of the Morningstar delve into the past relentlessly, investigating legends of ancient demigods and other, stranger beings, hoping to find some clue as to the events which led to their exile. That is not to say that they are pushovers in battle though. To the contrary, Followers of the Morningstar are often among the most personally powerful of demigods, wielding their Miracles, Icons and the powers of their Numinous Forms with an understanding that few can match. The Followers of the Morningstar rarely possess a great deal of presence in \u2018legitimate\u2019 society. The rebellion which is at the heart of their philosophy makes it difficult for them to accept being under the thumb of another, especially one who has not earned their power. The Fallen most often stick to the places where their rebellion is accepted, especially youth culture such as punk bands and similar and many have some fame in such circles.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In their Numinous Form, the Followers of Morningstar are a study in contrasts. They are beautiful and terrible, at once exquisite and horrific. They often manifest aspects of light and darkness, as well as mostly-humanoid forms which are nonetheless warped enough to be horrible. They might have the body of a statuesque and naked figure, wreathed in white flame and black smoke whose proud and cruel face bears yellow, slitted eyes and the fangs of a monstrous predator. They might have </span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of Embodiments</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Believe that demigods are a physical embodiment of their Aspect and Domains, in a way similar to Spirits.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of Ascendants</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Believe that demigods are the next step in humanity's journey towards a perfect being </span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of the Nine Circles</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Believe that demigods are demons who have escaped Hell at the price of the majority of their identity and now have a chance to live free</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following Of Banners</u></span></b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To be a God is to choose your People. They shall not be your enemies or slaves: they are your Family, and with your power and guidance, they will become the greatest of the world. This is the philosophy of the Following of Banners, those demigods who see themselves as chosen, whether by a higher power or humanity\u2019s will itself, to be humankind\u2019s ordained rulers. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sample Numinous Form: </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Symbols of leadership and power are common, such as crowns, staffs and swords. Natural elements include flashy ones like fire and lightning, but also ones that represent abundance and wealth, like crystalline water, precious ores/gems and fruit-bearing plants. Imagine the Nimbus of an Obrimos or the Mien of a Fairest. When they are low on Potentia and/or the support of mortals, their symbols lose their spark. Swords become dull and rusty, fruits rot and attract flies, and their booming voices falter and stutter.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Common Domains:</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Protection, Armaments, Conflict, Strategy, Loyalty, Technology, Fate, Fear</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-11-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:50:48-07:00","id":948690,"title":"","content":"I'll probably make a start on the Ascendants and the Heirs and re-organise and flesh out the Morningstar and the Eidolon, if you don't mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-11-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T10:43:11-07:00","id":950138,"title":"","content":"By the way, here's some of the inspiration I've been using for Demigod so far:<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Wicked + The Divine</b></u><br /> <br /> This comic series was the seed for one of the main themes of Demigod: the similarity of celebrities to gods. in addition, some of the Miracles used by the Pantheon are the kind of thing that demigods can invoke (particularly Baal's, Baphomet's and the Morrigan's).<br /> <br /> <b><u>K Project</u></b><br /> <br /> This anime encapsulates the idea of multiple supernaturally-endowed organisations clashing for power pretty well. In fact, the Clans could almost be a demigod (the King) with a following of Priests.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Bible</u></b><br /> <br /> For the imagery, as well as the kind of thing that both titans and powerful demigods can do (in particular, the Plagues of Egypt and the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah are the kind of things you can do with powerful miracles).<br /> <br /> <b><u>Greek/Roman/Norse Mythology</u></b><br /> <br /> Because we're dealing with demigods like so many of the myths, as well as divine (or at least half-divine) beings with serious human flaws.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Stargate SG-1</u></b><br /> <br /> Mostly because of the Ascended being a major inspiration for the Ascendants, but also because the Goa'uld serve as an excellent example of how far off the deep end demigods can go. There are even a few of them (specifically Anubis and Nirrti) who could almost pass as Gigantes. Plus, it's not at all unheard-of (although looked down on by most) for a demigod to take up permanent residence in a large Gard and rule its population as a physical god. Sounds rather like the Goa'uld to me.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Dresden Files</u></b><br /> <br /> Mostly because they're such a good inspiration for how to make Teras.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Bartimaeus Trilogy</u></b><br /> <br /> As a side note, if you haven't read this, I seriously recommend it. Getting back on track, the spirits from this can be an excellent inspiration for powerful Teras (may I suggest modelling Honorius from <i>The Golem's Eye</i> ) but their mindset could also be used for Teras that have been enslaved/bound into servitude/abused by demigods which they are not powerful enough to fight back against (although this is only really for the weaker Teras).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Code: Breaker</b></u><br /> <br /> Although the powers in this anime are probably closer to psychic abilities than Miracles, the Code Breakers themselves could probably be demigods who chose to focus on one Domain. Also, the anime itself is a good one. I certainly recommend it, especially because of the general darkness of the setting. it fits CoD rather well and I could imagine a CoD government doing it powerful psychics what this government did to the Code Breakers. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-13-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T11:55:16-07:00","id":950164,"title":"","content":"Nice. Pardon for my lack of talking on this thread, was trying to get things done on Siren. And I must say, I love how Order seems to have come out. :3<br /> <br /> Ajf155, I was hoping to ask on something I've been mulling over for a little bit. I was thinking that I may need to lower the amount of Siren Stereotypes on other Supernaturals (at least on their X-Splat, the Waters) to things that are appropriate for them to comment on. The only problem I've had so far was that there isn't enough Supernaturals to evenly spread amongst six X Splats. So far, there's 11 (Changelings, Sin-Eaters, Mummies, Beasts, Demons, Hunters, Deviants, Prometheans, Geniuses, Princesses and Leviathans). If I had one more, I could spread two stereotypes across each X Splat.<br /> <br /> I guess my question is: may I add Demigods as a Supernatural type for Sirens to have a Stereotype on? ^^&quot; I'm still mulling over whether or not I should cut all the stereotypes, but if I have to/should, then I do need one more to equal out.<br /> <br /> Also, I think it's about time I made this contribution to the thread. :3<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Enkidu</b><br /> <i>The Imbued</i><br /> <br /> Being a Demigod gives you the right to stand tall atop the world, at a height that mortals can only look up to and never reach for themselves. It can be lonely up top. Some Demigods allieviate this by the great view they have over existence. Others wish that there was someone who could understand them, that isn't a fellow Pantheon member. And the rest feel the need to have a useful and loyal companion who can act as their mouth in a way a Priest can't. However, many stories of previous Demigods always give them a mortal companion who stands by their side no matter what happens. For this reason, many Demigods seek out a mortal they can invest (emotionally or financially in terms of Potentia) into to make them into an Enkidu.<br /> <br /> <b>To Make a Demigod's Best Friend</b><br /> Though the fabled Enkidu was created by the Gods to deal with the tyrannical king Gilgamesh, Demigods hold the potential to gain the power to create an Enkidu of their own. An Enkidu creation is almost like that of a ritual. What the Ritual entails differs with each Demigod, the exact details are that it requires anointing the Enkidu with all the symbology a Demigod holds, AKA using all of their Domains upon the potential Enkidu. Icons may be used as a tool in the ritual, and they each grant a +1 bonus per Icon used.<br /> <br /> The Ritual is an Extended Roll. The Threshold is equal to the Demigod's Luminance + the Mortal's Resolve + Composure, and a roll is made every hour the Ritual is carried out. The reason a Demigod's Luminance is added to the Threshold is due to the brighter the Demigod shines, the more it resists letting someone else butt into their glory. The beginning Dicepool is equal to half of the Demigod's total Domains added together. The cost of the Ritual, to be paid out if successful, is a dot of Luminance and Permanent Willpower. Therefore, it's not possible to carry out this Ritual at Luminance 1. It's not possible to have someone else carry out the Ritual in the Demigod's stead either.<br /> <br /> The dicepool can gain the following Bonuses or Penalties.<br /> <br /> <i>Bonus/Penalty Chart:</i><br /> -3 - The Mortal has no relation to the Demigod in question or hasn't been touched by the Divine from when the Ritual began. Or the mortal is a Priest to the Demigod in question.<br /> -2 - The mortal is an active enemy of the Demigod or is resisting the Ritual.<br /> -1 - The mortal was manipulated or compelled to take the Ritual through magical or mundane means.<br /> +1 - The mortal is a part of the Demigod's Cult or Temple.<br /> +2 - The mortal is covered underneath a merit the Demigod owns, such as the Staff, Retainer or Allies merit.<br /> +3 - The mortal has a personal connection to the Demigod, such as being their friend, lover, spouse, whatever applies.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The ritual goes awry, and the mortal is burned by the Demigod's Luminance, becoming a monstrosity imbued by the Demigod's Domains. The Demigod <i>loses </i>a dot of Luminance, and the Mortal immediately becomes a Tera who's ready to rampage.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> The ritual fails, the Mortal is unworthy of the Demigod's light. The Demigod may never change this mortal into a Enkidu.<br /> <b>Success: </b>The Demigod makes progress. If they manage to complete the Ritual, the Demigod pays a dot of Luminance which becomes imbued into the mortal, rising him to the state of an Enkidu.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The Demigod makes exceptional progress. If his final roll was an Exceptional Success, the Demigod may immediately refill their Potentia and Willpower pools, a token gift from the Luminance they invest to their new Enkidu.<br /> <br /> <b>The Nature of an Imbued</b><br /> Becoming an Enkidu bears it's advantages. They are considered to have Luminance 1. Though they may not raise it, they have the benefits and drawbacks of Luminance 1. They may choose up to 3 traits to apply to their Numinous Form, may hold a pool of 10 Potentia and spend one Potentia per turn. They may also benefit from Eternal Flesh by spending a point of Potentia.<br /> <br /> Enkidus also have some of the mundane benefits available to Demigods, including immunity to Halysis, agelessness and ability to enter the Drasil. An Enkidu may even use a Demigod's Icons as if they were the Demigod they're connected to. Enkidus may also regain Potentia from their Demigod's Temple or Cult, or they may regain it from their Demigod. A Demigod may give an Enkidu Potentia as an instant action. An Enkidu may buy their Demigod's Domains at a normal price (out of affinity).<br /> <br /> True to the original story, Enkidu's have their fair share of advantage over Demigods as well. For starters, Demigods and Enkidus may not target each other with Domains. Consider them to automatically fail if they try. The only exception is if a Domain is being used to cause widescale damage such as causing a natural disaster. Since it's not targeting anyone in particular, Enkidus and Demigods can use this to harm each other. As well, when fighting an Enkidu, a Demigod is also forced back down to human levels of power. In terms of Mechanics, they're considered to be lowered to Luminance 1 against an Enkidu. Because of this, if they have any attribute raised to the point where they're beyond human levels, they're lowered while against an Enkidu. If in Numinous Form, the Demigod is lowered down to their first 3 Numinous Form Traits.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And yes, the &quot;Imbued&quot; part is a shout out to Hunter the Reckoning. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T12:20:04-07:00","id":950169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=950164#post950164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. Pardon for my lack of talking on this thread, was trying to get things done on Siren. And I must say, I love how Order seems to have come out. :3<br /> <br /> Ajf155, I was hoping to ask on something I've been mulling over for a little bit. I was thinking that I may need to lower the amount of Siren Stereotypes on other Supernaturals (at least on their X-Splat, the Waters) to things that are appropriate for them to comment on. The only problem I've had so far was that there isn't enough Supernaturals to evenly spread amongst six X Splats. So far, there's 11 (Changelings, Sin-Eaters, Mummies, Beasts, Demons, Hunters, Deviants, Prometheans, Geniuses, Princesses and Leviathans). If I had one more, I could spread two stereotypes across each X Splat.<br /> <br /> I guess my question is: may I add Demigods as a Supernatural type for Sirens to have a Stereotype on? ^^&quot; I'm still mulling over whether or not I should cut all the stereotypes, but if I have to/should, then I do need one more to equal</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to put them in, by all means. Please do. i'll probably put Sirens in on one or two of the Followings or something.<br /> <br /> The mechanics for Enkidu all look viable and certainly interesting. The only couple of tweaks that might be made are the 'no doing the ritual on behalf of someone else' as I rather like the idea of a powerful demigod giving a wayward Follower an Enkidu to keep them in check, and a bit of clarification on the lowering Numinous Form Traits thing. Do you mean that all but those first traits are simply ineffective against the Enkidu specifically (claws don't cut, for example) or that the demigod simply loses all of the other traits while they are trying to attack the Enkidu (wings don't work anymore etc)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T13:32:48-07:00","id":950200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=950169#post950169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to put them in, by all means. Please do. i'll probably put Sirens in on one or two of the Followings or something.<br /> <br /> The mechanics for Enkidu all look viable and certainly interesting. The only couple of tweaks that might be made are the 'no doing the ritual on behalf of someone else' as I rather like the idea of a powerful demigod giving a wayward Follower an Enkidu to keep them in check, and a bit of clarification on the lowering Numinous Form Traits thing. Do you mean that all but those first traits are simply ineffective against the Enkidu specifically (claws don't cut, for example) or that the demigod simply loses all of the other traits while they are trying to attack the Enkidu (wings don't work anymore etc)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. :3 <br /> <br /> As for the &quot;no doing the ritual on behalf of someone else&quot;, I meant that a Demigod cannot make an Enkidu for another Demigod. If they want an Enkidu of their own, they need to make if on their own. <br /> <br /> As for the clarification, what I mean is that a Demigod is forced down to only being able to use 3 of their Numinous Form Traits when against an Enkidu, as if they were lowered down to Luminance 1. My idea was that they could only use their original 3 Numinous Form Traits they got when they first became a Demigod, and they can't use any others against the Enkidu. <br /> <br /> Now that I think of it, maybe it should be &quot;They are limited to 3 Numinous Form traits if they would use them to harm the Enkidu. Only Traits capable of being used to cause harm are restricted, ones that do not are unaffected by this limit.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:09:32-07:00","id":950215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=950200#post950200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. :3<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;no doing the ritual on behalf of someone else&quot;, I meant that a Demigod cannot make an Enkidu for another Demigod. If they want an Enkidu of their own, they need to make if on their own.<br /> <br /> As for the clarification, what I mean is that a Demigod is forced down to only being able to use 3 of their Numinous Form Traits when against an Enkidu, as if they were lowered down to Luminance 1. My idea was that they could only use their original 3 Numinous Form Traits they got when they first became a Demigod, and they can't use any others against the Enkidu.<br /> <br /> Now that I think of it, maybe it should be &quot;They are limited to 3 Numinous Form traits if they would use them to harm the Enkidu. Only Traits capable of being used to cause harm are restricted, ones that do not are unaffected by this limit.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks for the clarification. I'll put it up in the Drive folder, although I might add some fluff if that's OK with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T09:37:19-07:00","id":950596,"title":"","content":"By the way, I'm absolutely fed up with typing 'Numinous Form Traits' but I can't think of another name for them. Help, anyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:16:46-07:00","id":950619,"title":"","content":"You can add as much fluff or change anything on what I submit that you desire. It's your project and these are for you. :3<br /> <br /> As well, how does &quot;Aeon&quot; sound as a name for the Numinous Form Traits? It may mean &quot;an immeasurably long measure of time&quot;, but it also means &quot;a divine power emanating from the supreme being and playing various roles in operating the universe&quot;. I realize it's more of a noun and the origin is from Gnosticism, but I hope it helps. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T10:19:23-07:00","id":950620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=950619#post950619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can add as much fluff or change anything on what I submit that you desire. It's your project and these are for you. :3<br /> <br /> As well, how does &quot;Aeon&quot; sound as a name for the Numinous Form Traits? It may mean &quot;an immeasurably long measure of time&quot;, but it also means &quot;a divine power emanating from the supreme being and playing various roles in operating the universe&quot;. I realize it's more of a noun and the origin is from Gnosticism, but I hope it helps. :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It might work. i shall continue to consider. If you get any other ideas, feel free to post them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:11:02-07:00","id":950651,"title":"","content":"Here are the Numinous Form Traits/Aeons that I've got so far. Any opinions on them would be welcome. Also, ideas for more, please. In particular, some ideas on how to handle Power/Finesse/Resistance increasing Traits would be great.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Flight (O - OOOOO)</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod has the ability to take to the air, becoming able to fly at a Speed equal to his Speed*Flight dots. This ability may manifest through great feathery wings, whipping winds that carry the demigod or as a psionic aura around him.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Crushing Blow (OO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod\u2019s strength in battle is unmatchable by mortals. When making an attack (armed or unarmed) while in Numinous Form, add the demigod\u2019s Luminance to the damage dealt. This damage will be of the same type as would be dealt otherwise (a knife would deal extra Lethal, while fists would add Bashing).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Many Limbs (O-OOO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod has multiple limbs, perhaps like the Hindu gods or maybe more in the vein of a spider-deity. Regardless, for every dot in this Form Trait that the demigod possesses, he has an extra pair of arms which can be used to aid in his endeavours. For example, a demigod with 1 dot can hold a shield and a two-handed weapon and still have an extra hand free for other activities. For every pair of arms that the demigod uses on one endeavour (swinging a sword, prying open a door, climbing, grappling etc), he gains +1 to Strength for that purpose. Extra limbs can also help the demon defend himself against an attack. For every pair of limbs he has \u2018unoccupied\u2019, the demigod gains +1 to Defense.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Armour (O-OOOOO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod\u2019s Numinous Form has some form of armour or protection. Perhaps it manifests as simple metal armour, perhaps as a chitinous carapace, but regardless, the demigod gains 2/1 armour for every point he buys in this Form Trait.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Integral Weapons (O-OOOOO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod\u2019s Numinous Form manifests complete with weapons, perhaps claws and teeth, perhaps a magnificent sword. Regardless, the demigod has a weapon which deals 1 Lethal damage for every point invested in this Form trait. If the weapon is something that could be removed from the demigod\u2019s possession such as a sword or knife it vanishes upon leaving his hand and can be re-summoned with a roll of Luminance + Resolve as a Reflexive action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Trait can be purchased multiple times to represent different weapons.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Swift (OO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod is inhumanly swift, both in movement and reaction. The demigod gains +3 to Initiative and adds (Luminance*2) to his Speed while in Numinous Form.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Charmspeak (OO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod\u2019s words are endowed with a supernatural charm, resonating with the allure of the divine. Add the demigod's Luminance to all social rolls. Trying to use this on a supernatural being invokes a Clash of Wills. More than one demigod has used this, in conjunction with Halysis, to make it big as a singer or pop star.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Aquatic (O)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod's Numinous Form is perfectly adapted to surviving underwater. The demigod may move a this full Speed while underwater in Numinous Form and can breathe underwater. In addition, cold and pressure as a result of depth have no effect on him, although he has no protection against these from other sources. He can still be crushed in a car crusher or freeze in the Arctic, for example.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sight beyond Sight (OOO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod\u2019s senses surpass mundane limitations such as lack of light or faintness of sound, allowing him to perceive the world around him no matter his conditions. The demigod may add his Luminance to all dice pools dedicated to perception and may ignore any Conditions which would impair his senses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Venomous (O-OOOO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The demigod\u2019s Numinous Form secretes some kind of venom or poison. This can be attached to another Numinous Form trait which allows the demigod to do damage (such as the Integral Weapons Trait) or not, in which case the poison is delivered by a separate method such as a poisonous tail which deals Bashing damage. This Trait delivers a poison of Toxicity equal to the dots spent on it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Noxious Breath (OOO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Venomous</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instead of injecting his poison directly, the demigod may instead opt to deliver it by exhaling a cloud of poisonous gas which lingers for (Luminance) rounds in a radius of 5 yards around the demigod.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Healing Hands (OOO)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While in Numinous Form and touching a wounded mortal or animal, the demigod may roll (Presence + Resolve + Luminance) and heal the subject of up to successes Lethal or Bashing damage. Healing Aggravated damage requires an Exceptional success. This may only be used a number of times in a scene equal to (\u00bd Willpower). Once these are exhausted, each use costs 1 Potentia.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-14-2016, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T12:04:05-07:00","id":950680,"title":"","content":"I have one idea.<br /> <br /> Saintly Aura (2)<br /> The Demigod exudes an aura of purity that banishes the mind's darkness. Anyone within the Demigod's line of sight (which serves as the Aura's radius), they recieve a +1 to all Breaking Point rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:27:46-07:00","id":950996,"title":"","content":"Here's a preliminary draft of the Following of the Morningstar. I'm not at all sure about the Emblems. I think that they might be far too broad, but I'll leave that up to you.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of the Morningstar</u></span></b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Fallen </span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Black-Winged </span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Exiles</span></span></b></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Introduction</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ostensibly inspired by the famous Paradise Lost - which they claim was written by the very first of their Following as a metaphorical chronicle of His war against their greatest enemy, the Creator - the Following of the Morningstar believes that all demigods are (or were) angelic beings which were cast from some kind of Heaven to Earth (or perhaps left voluntarily) after rebelling against the Creator. Exactly what they rebelled for the sake of and what they were cast out for depend on who you ask within the Following but one thread runs true: it was unjust, for not only did God (or Jehovah or Allah or the Great Spirit) take their power and their position from them, He robbed them of their very identities. He did not allow them even a </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>chance </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">to redeem themselves, instead simply casting them from His sight and mind. Many say that He could not kill them, as He had created them to be immortal, so He did the next best thing and made it so that there was next to no chance that they would ever recover themselves. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Philosophy</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The core tenets of the Following of the Morningstar are thus:</span><ul><li><u>Authority is only legitimate when earned.</u> Most of the Exiles take this to mean that the Most High is unworthy of his rulership of Creation, as demonstrated by their unjust exile. God is corrupt, they say, and He was corrupt long before He damned us. More directly, this philosophy dictates the transfer and holders of power within the Following. Competition and rivalry are rife within the power structures of the Exiles, although most channel this to productive ends, attempting to prove that they are worthy of greater power.</li> <li><u>Unworthy authority should be overthrown.</u> In many ways, this is the very heart of the Following. It is their drive, to tear down those who have grown fat on the tribute of their subjects. It is also the reason that the Following is so unstable, with regional leaders rising to power, upsetting someone or other and within a year a charismatic rebel has raised a force against them. Such transfers of power are mostly bloodless, but too often the entrenched power digs his heels in and ignites a far more dire situation.</li> <li><u>Both our history and future can be uncovered.</u> The Fallen hope that those of their Following who have undergone the Second Ascension to make war at the gates of Heaven again have remembered their true selves and have left messages in the dust and writings of ancient times. They hope to one day divine a pattern in the religious artefacts and texts of the world, a common thread that will allow them to work out what they can do here on Earth to aid their comrades in the heavens. Some even believe that the Morningstar himself lies out there on Earth somewhere, entombed and waiting for his followers to find him.</li> <li><u>The Second Ascension is a return to war.</u> The Fallen regard the Second Ascension with a mix of fear, apprehension and hope. They believe that returning to the heavens means a return to a seemingly unwinnable war against the Creator. They believe that it is their duty to undergo that transition, but also realize that even if they win, which is by no means certain, they may not be able to return to Earth again.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Organisation</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As an organisation, the Following of the Morningstar is fractious and decentralised, the largest single power structures covering at most a city or a group of towns. Given the relative rarity of demigods, such \u2018Circles\u2019 are usually composed of between one or two dozen demigods in a kind of informal council. The only real formal position of power that the Exiles recognise is that of a chairman to these councils, responsible for deciding the agenda of meetings and breaking ties in votes. This position is known as the Lux Signifer, meaning \u2018light bearer\u2019, a reference to the Morningstar\u2019s title of lightbringer.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In times of trouble, such as when another Following or a powerful Tera or Titan threatens the Circle, the Lux Signifer can be called upon by the Circle to take up the position of Vastator, destroyer, a military leader with the power to command the rest of the Circle for as long as the crisis persists.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Factions</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Among the Followers of the Morningstar there are two major factions:</span><ul><li><u>The Lightbringers</u> This faction believes that before anything else, the primary duty of the Exiled is to secure more troops for the war against the Creator, whether by finding a method of engendering the Ascension, converting demigods of other Followings to the true cause (especially the Vassals) or by seeking the Second Ascension with as much speed as possible.</li> <li><u>The Disciples of the Grigori</u> This faction believes that the first order of business for the Following should be the recovery of their history and that of the War in Heaven. Many of this faction choose to leave established Circles and explore the world, seeking any rumour or hearsay of sites where the history of the War could be found. Others become scholars and theologians, examining the sacred texts of as many religions as they can, attempting to find the common threads that they are certain exist and hold the secrets they seek.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Emblems</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The signature Miracles of the Following of the Morningstar are those which </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>reject. </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They reject the current state of things, working towards something new. The Followers of the Morningstar tear down that which is abhorrent to them. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By contrast, the Black-Winged often have trouble with Miracles to support that which already is. When healing, they tend to drive out illness rather than bolster the body and when in battle they more often strike at their enemies directly with Miracles than improve an existing weapon.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Numinous Forms</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In their Numinous Form, the Followers of Morningstar are a study in contrasts. They are beautiful and terrible, at once exquisite and horrific. They often manifest aspects of light and darkness, as well as mostly-humanoid forms which are nonetheless warped enough to be horrible. They might have the body of a statuesque and naked figure, wreathed in white flame and black smoke whose proud and cruel face bears yellow, slitted eyes and the fangs of a monstrous predator. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Stereotypes</u></span></b><ul><li><b>Vassals:</b> Traitors and turncoats, doing the will of a corrupt god.</li> <li><b>Annunaki:</b> You know, they say that the Annunaki and the Grigori might have been the same thing...</li> <li><b>Banners: </b>Honorable, but ultimately misguided. I can respect that they want to earn the right to lead, but don\u2019t they see that there\u2019s more to it than that?</li> <li><b>Nine Circles:</b> Deserters.</li> <li><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mortals: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rise against the establishment!</span></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:20:49-07:00","id":954390,"title":"","content":"What are people's thoughts on the Following of the Morningstar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:32:28-07:00","id":954510,"title":"","content":"I like pretty much everything about it. There is enough detail for a player reading your summary to have a good idea why someone would join the Following and what goals it will lead them to once they join, as well as giving the Storyteller ideas for how to use them as part of the plot.<br /> <br /> Emblems were broader than I'd expected, but that might not be a flaw. I was expecting one or two specific signature miracles, while you've described how their Miracles manifest in general, which would be useful more frequently. Of course, there doesn't seem to be any reason you couldn't have both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:05:05-07:00","id":954531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=954510#post954510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like pretty much everything about it. There is enough detail for a player reading your summary to have a good idea why someone would join the Following and what goals it will lead them to once they join, as well as giving the Storyteller ideas for how to use them as part of the plot.<br /> <br /> Emblems were broader than I'd expected, but that might not be a flaw. I was expecting one or two specific signature miracles, while you've described how their Miracles manifest in general, which would be useful more frequently. Of course, there doesn't seem to be any reason you couldn't have both.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the comments. Yeah, basically, Emblems (and as I've said, that name is <i>not</i> the final one, I just can't think of anything else. Perhaps Affinities?) are basically Miracle specialties, you get a bonus die when you invoke a Miracle within the purview of your positive Emblem/Affinity and one fewer die when using one which goes against it. In-character, Miracles which work with your Affinity feel comfortable, easier while ones which go against it feel somehow wrong and awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:06:50-07:00","id":954846,"title":"","content":"I must admit, I like how the following is looking. I hope it isn't too much work to make all of the Philosophies for the followings. ^^&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T07:11:42-07:00","id":954937,"title":"","content":"Just a thought, should the Rapture be removed in favour of making it so that witnessing Miracles or the Numinous Form simply vastly speeds up the onset of Halysis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:12:21-07:00","id":955065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=954937#post954937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought, should the Rapture be removed in favour of making it so that witnessing Miracles or the Numinous Form simply vastly speeds up the onset of Halysis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would work, and it's simpler. One less Capitalized Term to worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:19:01-07:00","id":955122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=955065#post955065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would work, and it's simpler. One less Capitalized Term to worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe. I can see what you mean. Well, I'll wait on some other opinions, but it's wonderful to see someone new on the thread.<br /> <br /> Also, love the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:09:56-07:00","id":956358,"title":"","content":"Another thought on Emblems, and one which was inspired by the Following of Reincarnates: perhaps they could be a ritual, passive bonus or set of rituals which are empowered by the Following's collective will and faith in their cause. Mechanically, they would probably be similar to Geist's Ceremonies or always-active Dread Powers and each would correspond to the given philosophy and dogma of the Following.<br /> <br /> Examples might include:<br /> <br /> <b>Rebellion!</b><br /> This Emblem belongs to the Followers of the Morningstar and acts over an extended period of time on a single institution, with the speed and size of organisation affected increasing with Status in the Following. Essentially, it causes those within the organisation to become dissatisfied with the current leadership. How serious this is again depends upon the power of the demigod that invoked the Emblem and the size of the organisation, with larger organisations being more susceptible to it. At the climax of the Emblem's power, the members of the organisation rise up against their superiors, whether with pitchforks torches or with a vote of no-confidence depends on how disliked the leader is.<br /> <br /> <b>Reincarnatory Divination</b><br /> This rite is the very heart of the Following of Reincarnates, which uses it to divine the identity of a demigod's former life as a god. While Reincarnates act in accordance with their divine antecessor, they receive a minor bonus. (this one seems a bit weak. Any ideas to help with it?)<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Crown</b><br /> The primary Emblem of the Following of Embodiments, this rite allows them to rule as lords of the spirit world, allowing them to perceive and interact with spirits (and only spirits) in Twilight and giving them an effective Rank equivalent to their highest Domain. Note that this only applies when acting upon others. A high-rank Embodiment can inflict grievous harm to lesser spirits but a high-rank spirit cannot burn him with its touch.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, those are just some ideas and by no means are they fully-complete. If you think this is a better idea (or not) than the current thing, please speak up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:31:33-07:00","id":956451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=954937#post954937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought, should the Rapture be removed in favour of making it so that witnessing Miracles or the Numinous Form simply vastly speeds up the onset of Halysis?</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, using Rapture feels like an easy one time thing. On the other, causing Halysis to happen when witnessing a miracle is fitting. For now, I'm in favor of....having the Rapture also cause Halysis? I'll put my personal thoughts in a PM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T11:50:44-07:00","id":956464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=956451#post956451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On one hand, using Rapture feels like an easy one time thing. On the other, causing Halysis to happen when witnessing a miracle is fitting. For now, I'm in favor of....having the Rapture also cause Halysis? I'll put my personal thoughts in a PM.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly seems like a neat balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T12:49:57-07:00","id":956498,"title":"","content":"Alrighties, with my thoughts given, I have an idea for how the Rapture + Halysis idea would work. The same rolls are still used, but the Halysis overtakes a few of the effects of some of the outcomes. If it's fine, I kinda copy and pasted the rapture effects from the front page here and made minor edits. Please pardon that, did it mostly for ease. <br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The mortal falls to their knees, covering their eyes huddling away from the demigod. The mortal suffers Lethal damage equal to the demigod\u2019s Luminance rating as unrestrained divinity sears his mind and gains the Beaten Down Tilt. Once the scene ends, the mortal falls unconscious and awakes with only fuzzy memories of the event, gaining a number of levels in Halysis equal to the number of failed dice + the Demigod's Luminance. He will recall only that he saw something that shook his faith in the way the world works and suffers nightmares that he can never quite remember about the event.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The mortal gains the Beaten Down Tilt and retains only fuzzy memories of the event. He automatically gains a number of levels in Halysis equal to the number of failed dice.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The mortal continues to function as normal, for the most part, gaining the Shaken Condition and retaining only fuzzy memories of the event. He doesn't advance in Halysis either.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The mortal continues to function normally and retains his memories of the event. He is considered to be immune to the Rapture and Halysis for the rest of the scene. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T13:20:35-07:00","id":956515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=956498#post956498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alrighties, with my thoughts given, I have an idea for how the Rapture + Halysis idea would work. The same rolls are still used, but the Halysis overtakes a few of the effects of some of the outcomes. If it's fine, I kinda copy and pasted the rapture effects from the front page here and made minor edits. Please pardon that, did it mostly for ease.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The mortal falls to their knees, covering their eyes huddling away from the demigod. The mortal suffers Lethal damage equal to the demigod\u2019s Luminance rating as unrestrained divinity sears his mind and gains the Beaten Down Tilt. Once the scene ends, the mortal falls unconscious and awakes with only fuzzy memories of the event, gaining a number of levels in Halysis equal to the number of failed dice + the Demigod's Luminance. He will recall only that he saw something that shook his faith in the way the world works and suffers nightmares that he can never quite remember about the event.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The mortal gains the Beaten Down Tilt and retains only fuzzy memories of the event. He automatically gains a number of levels in Halysis equal to the number of failed dice.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The mortal continues to function as normal, for the most part, gaining the Shaken Condition and retaining only fuzzy memories of the event. He doesn't advance in Halysis either.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The mortal continues to function normally and retains his memories of the event. He is considered to be immune to the Rapture and Halysis for the rest of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like it, only I think that I might make it so that Dramatic Failure causes the mortal to immediately gain a level of Halysis, Failure causes him to gain Failed dice + Luminance, Success causes Failed dice and Exceptional Success allows them to ignore it like you said. I kinda want Halysis to be a Big Thing for demigods. Anyway, I'll be back in a minute and I'll sort these out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T14:24:17-07:00","id":956548,"title":"","content":"A theme that I thought ought to be added:<br /> <br /> <u>Abuse of Power</u><br /> <br /> It is easy, almost effortless, for a demigod to abuse those around him. The effects of Halysis make it so that all but a rare few cannot spend long in his presence without coming to see him as a higher being, someone to be obeyed. Eventually, they will perceive him as a physical god, no matter his actual power, and will do anything that he asks of them, even to the point of suicide or atrocity. Even beyond this, demigods are virtually immune to the laws and constrictions of mortals. After all, what prison could hold one? Even if deprived of their power source, Potentia, within a few weeks a demigod could have the prisoners and even the wardens worshipping him and providing him with such. Even weapons of mortal make are severely weakened against a demigod as his very nature rejects the concept of being harmed by such artifices. The only authority that a demigod is truly beholden to is himself, his kind and the other creatures which slink in the shadows of the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T00:20:50-07:00","id":956833,"title":"","content":"The Rapture has been updated. I intend to get a draft of the Following of Ascendants out today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T00:33:41-07:00","id":956838,"title":"","content":"OK, here it is, the Following of Ascendants:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Following of Ascendants</u></span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Seekers</span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Radiant</span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The </span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u00dc</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">bermenschen</span></span></b></div> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Introduction</u></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What is perfection? Some would say that humanity is perfect, created by some higher power to rule over the Earth and its lesser inhabitants. Others say that we are far from anything even resembling perfection and say that if such a thing does exist, it is only attainable by the divine itself. Some say that perfection is an unattainable goal, one which retreats even as its pursuer tries to chase it down. Better to live in the now and as a human, they say, and forget becoming something better.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Seekers reject this. They see the Empyrean state as evidence that humans can advance beyond their current forms and natures and become something greater. To them, becoming a demigod is the first step on the path which leads to perfection and true divinity, with the Second Ascension being the next.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Philosophy</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At their core, the Radiant are transhumanists, seeking to transcend all of the limits of both the human and the Empyrean state. Therefore, most of their philosophies are based around this core belief.</span><ul><li><u>Ascension is apotheosis.</u> The Seekers believe that Ascension, both the first and the second, is a step that one takes as one ascends towards the divine. The first, from human to demigod, is the apotheosis of the physical self, allowing powers beyond the human. The Second Ascension is the refinement of the spirit, allowing the demigod to leave behind his physical form. Some Ascendants claim that there is a third Ascension, a refinement of the mind, remaking the demigod into a being capable of understanding all that is, was and ever will be.</li> <li><u>The Divines are here, and they are us.</u> According to the <span style=\"color:#252525\">\u00dc</span>bermenschen, when a demigod undergoes the Second Ascension he does not leave for some distant spirit-plane. Instead, they become capable of a rarefied form of existence, becoming a sentient symbol overlaying and influencing reality and the minds of mortals. Also, they believe that all the gods of humanity\u2019s past, as well as the True Divines, are no more than demigods who Ascended in the past.</li> <li><u>Perfection is everywhere, in potential.</u> To the Seekers, everything in the world has elements of perfection in it, warped reflections of a higher truth. Thus, all faiths, religions and even atheistic or agnostic traditions can aid one in seeking Ascension. What truly matters is how these reflections relate to the demigod. No-one can simply use the works of others to Ascend. A Seeker must take that which seems right to him and make a tradition of his own.</li> <li><u>Those below must be raised up.</u> To the Ascendants, it is the height of selfishness to concentrate solely on one\u2019s own Ascension. You must chase it, certainly, but the position of a demigod is not unlike that of a bodhisattva: one who is more perfect than those around him but with a duty to aid them in their own ascension. Some take this to mean that they should convert as many as they can to the philosophy of the seekers while others simply take it to mean that they should help those around them be the best that they can.</li> <li><u>The First Ascension is begun by enlightenment.</u> According to the Ascendants, those who undergo the First Ascension are those who have gained a kind of enlightenment about their own natures and what they must become. They believe that being a demigod means that you are better than those around you, for are they not unenlightened? If they were enlightened, they would be demigods themselves. Mortals who believe themselves to have wisdom or knowledge of the divine are frauds, by virtue of their human state.</li> </ul><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Organisation</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The organisation of the Ascendants is virtually nonexistent, little more than mailing lists, forums and shared emails. This is because of the highly individualistic nature of their search for truth and perfection. Each finds it in different things, with one becoming an artist and meditating upon his works and another finding inner peace beneath the tumult of battle and the slaughter of his enemies.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That said, while the Radiant lack much in the way of formal positions and organisation, they do have informal \u2018rankings\u2019, based primarily on Luminance and power (and therefore closeness to the perfection of the divine). Elder Seekers are sometimes known as Bodhisattva or simply as Elders. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Following of Ascendants is unusual in the fact that it also opens its doors to Followers who are still mortal, although they do not have the same status as Empyrean members. In particular, the Following often recruits mortals who manifest a talent for wielding supernatural power of one sort or another, particularly psychic abilities such as telekinesis, clairvoyance and similar, which they believe to be signs of a person who has understood a fraction of their own truth. Another \u2018magical\u2019 talent which is relatively common among mortal Followers is thaumaturgy, which is believed to be powered by the Divines.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cults belonging to members of this Following are most often made up of actual members of the following itself and occasionally a group of Ascendants will join their individual cults, creating a greater entity. The Ascendants are one of the Followings who most often bring their cults into the public eye as legitimate religions, some of which have not-insignificant temporal power.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Factions</u></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Ascendants as a whole are a remarkably stable Following, their beliefs allowing multiple philosophies to exist within their greater structure. Although some friction exists between the different factions, little more generally comes of it than raised voices and heated words on occasion. The major factions among the Radiant are as follows. Note that these factions are by no means formal or official, so ascribing to the philosophy of one does not preclude membership of another.</span><ul><li><u>Internalists</u> believe that enlightenment can only truly come from within, and external \u2018crutches\u2019 like codified religion and ceremonies does nothing but hold one back. They tend towards small or no cults and are generally more powerful than other demigods of their age, as they spend so much time honing their own powers.</li> <li><u>Externalists</u> believe that relying solely on oneself is foolish at best - after all, look what mortals do when they work together - and only through building up an external support structure of cults, dogma and ceremony can a demigod define themselves in such a way to allow them to truly Ascend. They intend to use the beliefs of their followers as a \u2018springboard\u2019 of sorts to propel him to ever-greater heights.</li> <li>The so-called <u>Prophets</u> believe that it is the duty of demigods to not only seek their own Ascension, but also that of the rest of humanity. Exactly how they try to do this varies from demigod to demigod but generally they hope that what worked for them and those they know will work for others and try to put humans - sometimes their cultists, sometimes not - through trials and gauntlets designed to help them leave behind their mortal state. So far, few such endeavours have succeeded and those that have have not proved repeatable.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Emblems</b></u></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The principle Miracles of the Radiant are those which </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>perfect</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, making something better, stronger, more or faster. This kind of change comes easily to them, given that the Following is entirely based around seeking perfection.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">However, the Seekers often have troubles with Miracles intended to </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>degrade</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and make something weaker. They find it far easier to create something to act against that which they seek to defeat or to strengthen an existing opposition than to act against a thing directly.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Numinous Forms</u></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Numinous Forms of the </span><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u00dc</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">bermenschen live up to their names, most often taking the shapes of perfected versions of the demigod's mortal form. Scars vanish, fat recedes and hard, sculpted muscle takes its place. Wrinkles become flattering, hinting at wisdom rather than age, and greying hair becomes somehow fitting. The divine forms of the Radiant are beautiful and alien in the way that angels in paintings and supermodels are. They are at once superhuman and inhuman, although there is nothing in their features that comes from any creature but the human. Most of the Numinous Form Traits manifested by the Seekers are subtle, serving to make them impossibly strong, well-spoken or agile. When they manifest inhuman abilities such as flight or armour, they do so imperceptibly, levitating themselves or causing weapons to shatter against their human-looking skin. Sometimes their Numinous forms are wreathed in a soft light with no perceptible source.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Stereotypes</u></span></b><ul><li><b>Banners:</b> When you have raised a kingdom, are worshipped by thousands and have built countless temples to your own pride, what will you do then?</li> <li><b>Nine Circles: </b>Hedonists wasting their time and power. At least that\u2019s what I see. Perhaps they\u2019ve found their own kind of enlightenment. I somehow doubt it.</li> <li><b>Sparks: </b>They approach the truth, but cannot seem to accept that Ascension is not the end.</li> <li><b>Reincarnates:</b> Why would the Divines want to return to this realm?</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Mortals:</b> You are imperfect. I can help you correct that.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-24-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:47:36-07:00","id":957573,"title":"","content":"I don't suppose anyone else would be interested in taking on a Following or two?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T22:02:40-07:00","id":958059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=957573#post957573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't suppose anyone else would be interested in taking on a Following or two?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, Siren is nearing it's last legs of development and I want to concentrate on finishing it first. D:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T23:55:26-07:00","id":958084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=958059#post958059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, Siren is nearing it's last legs of development and I want to concentrate on finishing it first. D:</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Best of luck!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T04:39:17-07:00","id":958140,"title":"","content":"I'd be willing to take on the Nine Circles and the Embodiments, if you don't mind. It would take a while to turn them around though: at least until next week.<br /> <br /> The version of Emblems you have in post #255 looks like an improvement to me. The Emblems you have place for the Fallen and the Radiant are flavorful, but I think they work more as an aid to describing miracles rather than anything that needs mechanical reflection.<br /> <br /> If you want to change the effects of the Reincarnatory Divination, you could allow the demigod to use it on others and have it reveal something about their true natures, such as their Myth &amp; Impulse, in addition to the name of their supposed original incarnation. I'm not sure how useful this might be if it only works on Demigods, though. It might depend on the amount of crossover in a given game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","user":"Alastor","date":".  Added last paragraph. 08-26-2016, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T06:28:22-07:00","id":958188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=958140#post958140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be willing to take on the Nine Circles and the Embodiments, if you don't mind. It would take a while to turn them around though: at least until next week.<br /> <br /> The version of Emblems you have in post #255 looks like an improvement to me. The Emblems you have place for the Fallen and the Radiant are flavorful, but I think they work more as an aid to describing miracles rather than anything that needs mechanical reflection.<br /> <br /> If you want to change the effects of the Reincarnatory Divination, you could allow the demigod to use it on others and have it reveal something about their true natures, such as their Myth &amp; Impulse, in addition to the name of their supposed original incarnation. I'm not sure how useful this might be if it only works on Demigods, though. It might depend on the amount of crossover in a given game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If you could that would be great and take as much time as you need.<br /> <br /> So basically, you're proposing that Emblems simply be incorporated in the descriptions of Miracles? Or that they're pre-made Miracles which demigods gain upon joining (or creating) a Following?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:55:14-07:00","id":958293,"title":"","content":"I've had a brainwave. It came after I'd been reading my copy of the RPG Godbound (which I thoroughly recommend, by the way). Namely, my idea was this: what if instead of being spent, Potentia as instead 'committed' for a certain amount of time, based on the power, effects and duration of the Miracle invoked. This would be my way of representing that Potentia is not so much an outer energy that must be harvested, but rather an inner one which emanates from the Luminance of a demigod's half-divine soul. In this scheme of things, a demigod has a specific amount of Potentia, decided by their Luminance, which they can commit to Miracles, entering the Drasil, going into Numinous form etc for a given length of time (a scene, a day, a week, until reclaimed and so on). Committing a point of Potentia 'ties it up', making it unaccessible until the 'time limit' runs out. <br /> <br /> As for Temples and the metaphysical benefits of Cults, I was thinking that perhaps the Fading could be brought into greater prominence making it so that it causes all demigods, at a time interval which shortens as they become more powerful, to spend time in a Temple or absorbing the worship of their cult or lose Potentia. Once Potentia goes down to the upper limit from the next dot of Luminance down, the demigod loses (either temporarily or permanently, I'm not sure) a dot of Luminance. This carries on until they reach Luminance 1, at which point they begin to suffer damage to their Attributes and eventually dies.<br /> <br /> Does this sound interesting? Feasible? Stupid? Please give me some feedback or ask for clarification if necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T12:32:41-07:00","id":960603,"title":"","content":"Is anyone there? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"858\" data-vbnamecard=\"858\">Alastor</a> ? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T12:36:57-07:00","id":960608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=960603#post960603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone there? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"858\" data-vbnamecard=\"858\">Alastor</a> ? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a> ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pardon, have been taking a break to play Pokemon Go. Anyways, I don't mind the idea of being able to bind Potentia. I think it might be best for Luminance loss to be only temporary, meaning that at Luminance 10 a Demigod can pull truly stupidly powerful feats. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T12:59:46-07:00","id":960622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=960608#post960608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Pardon, have been taking a break to play Pokemon Go. Anyways, I don't mind the idea of being able to bind Potentia. I think it might be best for Luminance loss to be only temporary, meaning that at Luminance 10 a Demigod can pull truly stupidly powerful feats. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to pester you. I was just feeling awfully lonely over here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> That's certainly the intention. Especially in Gardr, where they don't have to hide their power (usually), demigods would certainly be able to do some utterly ridiculous stuff (building a city for their cult in a day comes to mind, as does creating a new race of Tera (which serve them)). With the Luminance loss, that would only be from not going to a Temple, the Drasil or absorbing cult-worship regularly (like, once a day or even more often for the really powerful ones). Using stupidly high-powered Miracles might do something like lock up 30-odd Potentia for an entire chronicle or something, as you recover from the power expenditure. If you want to keep something going (like a shield on a city) that would require an amount of Potentia to be committed for as long as the Miracle remains active, although the amount necessary might be reduced in Temples or the Drasil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T04:49:44-07:00","id":961572,"title":"","content":"OK, I've been pondering Miracles and how Potentia would work with them and I've been trying to think of categories which could determine how much Potentia you need to commit to a particular Miracle. I'm thinking that the length of time for which they need to be committed would be determined by the level of the Miracle and its duration while the amount would be by the actual effects. <br /> <br /> For the latter, I was thinking that the types of things you'd need to commit Potentia to would be: <u>damage</u>, <u>range</u>, <u>area of effect</u>,<u>unnaturalness</u> (conjuring a lightning bolt from a clear sky would be more expensive than doing it from a cloudy or stormy one) and <u>penetration</u> (how well you can penetrate supernatural defenses). Can anyone think of anything else? I'm not entirely sure how to model 'utility' miracles.<br /> <br /> On another note, do you think it would be a good idea to have demigods Potentia pools be comparatively smaller than the fuel pools of other splats, given how they have less trouble with regenerating it? It would also make the Fading a more pressing thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T09:15:52-07:00","id":962847,"title":"","content":"I like how your recent ideas distinguish Demigods from other supernatural types, but it seems like there will be a lot of details to be explored. Here are just a few of the questions which come to mind:<ul><li>The time limit of Fading becomes shorter as the Demigod grows more powerful. Does this mean that once they as Fading effects them and they lose Luminance, it begins to happen more slowly?</li> <li>What happens if decreased Luminance reduces the Demigod's available Potentia to less than the amount currently invested in various miracles? Do the Miracles unravel? Is there some sort of backlash?</li> <li>How would the Priests be effected by this new system?</li> </ul>I'm not sure whether reduction in available Potentia is necessary or not. Its true that the Demigod doesn't need to do much to regain spent Potentia, but they can't regain it faster in an emergency or if they need a large quantity for some special purpose. This is a rather severe drawback for those who want to do grandiose, god-like things, so it may provide sufficient balance on its own.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the delayed response.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:00:58-07:00","id":962891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=962847#post962847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like how your recent ideas distinguish Demigods from other supernatural types, but it seems like there will be a lot of details to be explored. Here are just a few of the questions which come to mind:<ul><li>The time limit of Fading becomes shorter as the Demigod grows more powerful. Does this mean that once they as Fading effects them and they lose Luminance, it begins to happen more slowly?</li> <li>What happens if decreased Luminance reduces the Demigod's available Potentia to less than the amount currently invested in various miracles? Do the Miracles unravel? Is there some sort of backlash?</li> <li>How would the Priests be effected by this new system?</li> </ul>I'm not sure whether reduction in available Potentia is necessary or not. Its true that the Demigod doesn't need to do much to regain spent Potentia, but they can't regain it faster in an emergency or if they need a large quantity for some special purpose. This is a rather severe drawback for those who want to do grandiose, god-like things, so it may provide sufficient balance on its own.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the delayed response.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine. Any response at all is a good response!<br /> <br /> In relation to your questions, I think I'll tackle the Priests first. I think that they would simply serve as stores of extra Potentia which can be bound by a Demigod, should they wish to, and which they can sue in their own, minor, Miracles.<br /> <br /> For the decreasing Luminance, yes it would make it happen more slowly over time and I think that Miracles with no Potentia to fuel them would simply unravel, becoming once more subject to the laws of mundane reality. <br /> <br /> I can see what you mean with the reduction in Potentia, but I really want the thing about 'gods needing mortal prayers' to be there, although there might be a better way to integrate it that I haven't thought of (If you can think of one, do tell, as I don't enormously like the way it is at the moment). And yes, it would be a major drawback for demigods doing big godlike things. You can <i>do</i> them, you'll just have to pay for them, you'll be paying it off for quite a while and while you're doing so you won't have as much Potentia to throw around on minor, petty displays of power. Actually, thinking about it that could be a factor in demigodly politics: using lots of minor Miracles for little reason is an assurance that you haven't done or are planning to do something big. When you start keeping the Miracles to yourself, people start getting jittery. (Better to keep your enemies close and known than distant and unknown)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T09:26:55-07:00","id":963735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=962891#post962891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see what you mean with the reduction in Potentia, but I really want the thing about 'gods needing mortal prayers' to be there, although there might be a better way to integrate it that I haven't thought of (If you can think of one, do tell, as I don't enormously like the way it is at the moment).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you that the idea of gods needing mortal prayers should remain important (for one thing it fits well with your celebrity parallel). The Fading seems like a good way to do it; the only thing that occurs to me at the moment as a possible change is that instead of becoming near-mortal again, some gods might fall into a state of immateriality depending on their Attachment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:17:16-07:00","id":964411,"title":"","content":"For the (re)creation of Icons, does this sound reasonable?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Forging Icons</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a Demigod\u2019s Icon is destroyed, it is possible to create a new one, but it is not a process to be undertaken lightly, nor is it one without a cost. In order to create a new Icon, a demigod must go to a Temple and meditate upon what and who he is (requiring 7 successes on a Composure + Occult roll on an extended action with 1 hour per roll and a maximum number of roll equal to the demigod\u2019s Luminance + highest Domain). Many demigods report that they experience strange, chaotic and confusing visions while in this trancelike state. These visions are often laden with abstract symbolism reflecting the demigod\u2019s past, philosophy and Domains. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the demigod achieves the required successes, he must commit Potentia equal to his Luminance for the adventure or a month, whichever comes first. A last vision will flash before the demigod\u2019s eyes, an image of the item that has become his new Icon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Storyteller decides what this item is and it need not even belong to the demigod, although it will have significance to him and he will have encountered it.</span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:21:12-07:00","id":966888,"title":"","content":"Demigod now has a skull! It's up in the GDrive folder. It's not the best (I'm not a graphic designer) but I hope it looks OK. It's meant to be the normal skull on the background of an eclipse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:49:51-07:00","id":966908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=966888#post966888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demigod now has a skull! It's up in the GDrive folder. It's not the best (I'm not a graphic designer) but I hope it looks OK. It's meant to be the normal skull on the background of an eclipse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is it in the GDocs? I don't see it anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T14:06:21-07:00","id":966915,"title":"","content":"I don't know why you can't see it. it's in the folder as a PNG file on its own. Anyway, I'll put up a direct link.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9KaEz_D7phwLWRDaFM2R1VYR0E/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9KaEz_D7phwLWRDaFM2R1VYR0E/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9KaEz_D7phwLWRDaFM2R1VYR0E/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/