rection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:31:54-07:00","id":971497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=971449#post971449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps Basilica?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that, but I think that it might be better used for a demigodly meeting place, kind of like a localised UN for demigods and their cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:39:53-07:00","id":971545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=971497#post971497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that, but I think that it might be better used for a demigodly meeting place, kind of like a localised UN for demigods and their cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm....the only other thing I have is Sacellum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:59:24-07:00","id":978520,"title":"","content":"Just an idea, instead of having the generic agelessness, what if demigods simply aged and died of old age like normal, but given their ability to defy death, tend to simply return? That way you could get some stories out of 'reincarnations' of old demigods, as well as cults awaiting the 'return of their god' and such. Any thoughts?<br /> <br /> Also, I've sorted out a proper plan for the thing and have made a start on the introductory chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T03:29:01-07:00","id":979570,"title":"","content":"Here's a link to the first draft of the introductory chapter. Mind you, the lexicon still needs to be done.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1bo-RlgnvzOL9kt183BtbO4IP4FaUyZp5RyQpFcTvhwc\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=1bo...Zp5RyQpFcTvhwc</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T06:09:28-07:00","id":984839,"title":"","content":"And here's the preliminary draft of the system for creating Domains. As anyone who's read (read: struggled through) that rulebook will recognise, it was heavily inspired by Nobilis. Hopefully this is a little more understandable.<br /> <br /> I intend to add some more example Domains underneath this, so that people can just pick them if they want to. If anyone wants to make some and post them up here, feel free!<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:32px\"><u>Domains</u></span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Within every demigod, there is a shard of divine light and energy. Between this light and the world, though, a demigod\u2019s mind and soul shape that purity into changed emanations, like light refracted through prisms and coloured lenses. These are the demigod\u2019s Domains, the aspects of reality over which they possess power and the very representations of their being. Occult-minded demigods and scholars of Luminance sometimes liken Domains to the Sephirot, the ten emanations of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>En Sof</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, the Kabbalistic Infinite. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Regardless of what they truly are, Domains are possessed by all demigods and allow them to work Miracles, projections of their power into the outside world. There is no definitive list of Domains, as demigods are as unique as any other person and, thus, their Domains are unique as well. Even Domains which outwardly seem the same might be understood and manifested by different demigods in different ways. An example might be a Japanese demigod, who understands Water as a negative, cold entity and manifests it in drowning floods and stagnant water, while a demigod raised as a Wiccan might understand water as being a life-giving things and work Miracles accordingly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bequeathing Power</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When creating Domains, whether at character creation or later, there are several steps that must be followed. Indeed, a Domain is not unlike a miniature character in themselves.</span></span><br /> <br /> 1. First, the basic concept of a Domain must be agreed between Storyteller and player. As a rough rule of thumb, a Domain can be anything that can be said to exist, even conceptually, but should not be vastly broad. \u2018Life\u2019 is far too broad, while \u2018Plants\u2019 or \u2018Animals\u2019 is pushing it somewhat. \u2018Trees\u2019 or \u2018Canines\u2019 are well within acceptable bounds. Also, nothing kills the feeling of divine power quicker than a useless or silly Domain, so try to steer clear of \u2018Earthworms\u2019 or \u2018Teddy Bears\u2019, no matter how cool an army of animated, evil teddy bears might seem to you.<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Example: Joshua is creating a character who was a soldier before his Ascension and has become a kind of vigilante. He decides that he wants his primary Domain to be based around conflict and proposes that to the Storyteller. The Storyteller is a bit leery of such a broad Domain, able to be applied to all forms of conflict and asks Joshua to narrow it down a bit. After some thinking, He comes up with the Domain of War, which the Storyteller deems more appropriate.</i></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> 2. Once the basic concept has been established, the Domain\u2019s Attributes should be decided upon. Domain attributes are not numerically-defined, but rather serve as a narrative description of what that Domain does. These are important, as they define your character\u2019s understanding of that Domain and dictate what kind of things he can do with it. Attributes are also your opportunity to add conceptual elements to concrete Domains, such as saying \u2018Fire purifies\u2019. Each Domain can have up to five attributes, and these may be altered during play with the expenditure of Experience and an altered point of view.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Example: Having come to a decision on his Domain of War, Joshua now needs to come up with some attributes for it. He decides on</i></span></span><ul><li><i>War hurts people</i></li> <li><i>War is ugly</i></li> <li><i>War divides winners from losers</i></li> <li><i>War drives progress</i></li> <li><i>War makes people less than they would be</i></li> </ul>3. Assign your Domains a numerical value, from 1 to 5 dots. This defines the power of the Miracles which you can invoke with this Domain, from 1-dot miracles which might conjure a small flame to 5-dot miracles which call down rains of fire and sulfur.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Example: After assigning his Domain attributes, Joshua decides that his character\u2019s power over War is, while not vast, significant and so decides to give him 3 dots in the Domain.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-10-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T13:50:38-07:00","id":985050,"title":"","content":"That looks really good. Keep up the good work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:38:30-07:00","id":985077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985050#post985050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That looks really good. Keep up the good work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, it's nice to 'see' you again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:28:53-07:00","id":985186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985077#post985077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, it's nice to 'see' you again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. :3 Anyways, doing a quick look-see of things. I love how you use choice fonts for things, it practically feels like an official corebook. It makes me a little envious, Siren doesn't have that much detail put into the font facing. Also, thank you for putting me into the credits, even though I didn't do much on this game line. &gt;w&gt;<br /> <br /> As for the old age and reincarnation aspect, I can see how it may work. The only problem I can see at the moment is perhaps &quot;what ways may a demigod defy death&quot;. Do they need specific conditions (such as a virgin mother) to carry the Demigod's new form? Does the Demigod still require the faith of their Cult in order to incarnate anew and their Luminance/Soul goes into a newborn child? Etcetc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T23:42:26-07:00","id":985296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985186#post985186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ditto. :3 Anyways, doing a quick look-see of things. I love how you use choice fonts for things, it practically feels like an official corebook. It makes me a little envious, Siren doesn't have that much detail put into the font facing. Also, thank you for putting me into the credits, even though I didn't do much on this game line. &gt;w&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww... Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I feel so flattered. And you're more than welcome for the credit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985186#post985186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the old age and reincarnation aspect, I can see how it may work. The only problem I can see at the moment is perhaps &quot;what ways may a demigod defy death&quot;. Do they need specific conditions (such as a virgin mother) to carry the Demigod's new form? Does the Demigod still require the faith of their Cult in order to incarnate anew and their Luminance/Soul goes into a newborn child? Etcetc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was less that demigods actually reincarnate and more that their returning-via-Icons thing works even if they die of old age. Basically, when a demigod dies, from whatever means (so long as they have Luminance left), they return to their primary (oldest) Icon as a bodiless, unconscious spirit, not unlike an unawakened spirit from the Shadow.<br /> <br /> If a person comes into possession of the Icon, its Halysis aura acts upon them and as they go deeper into Halysis the demigod's spirit becomes more and more cognizant. By the 3rd Threshold, the demigod has two choices: if they stay in the Icon until its bearer reaches the 5th Threshold, they can commit (Luminance) Potentia for a month to take over the body of the bearer in a way not unlike spirit-claiming, save that the mind of the host does not survive in any way, save in the leftover memories that the demigod assimilates into their own mind. On the other hand, they can also choose to sacrifice 1 Luminance to remake the Icon that they are in into a new body, at the cost of destroying the Icon.<br /> <br /> The idea was that the first option looks, from the outside, to be the Icon-bearer becoming more and more faithful to the demigod, until the demigod 'returns through them'. And as for the virgin births thing, I'm not sure about the 'virgin' part, but if the Icon-bearer is a pregnant woman, the baby would be affected by the Halysis too, and the demigod could enter it if they really wanted to.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T10:25:32-07:00","id":985495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985296#post985296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awww... Thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I feel so flattered. And you're more than welcome for the credit.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. ^w^ <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985296#post985296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea was less that demigods actually reincarnate and more that their returning-via-Icons thing works even if they die of old age. Basically, when a demigod dies, from whatever means (so long as they have Luminance left), they return to their primary (oldest) Icon as a bodiless, unconscious spirit, not unlike an unawakened spirit from the Shadow.<br /> <br /> If a person comes into possession of the Icon, its Halysis aura acts upon them and as they go deeper into Halysis the demigod's spirit becomes more and more cognizant. By the 3rd Threshold, the demigod has two choices: if they stay in the Icon until its bearer reaches the 5th Threshold, they can commit (Luminance) Potentia for a month to take over the body of the bearer in a way not unlike spirit-claiming, save that the mind of the host does not survive in any way, save in the leftover memories that the demigod assimilates into their own mind. On the other hand, they can also choose to sacrifice 1 Luminance to remake the Icon that they are in into a new body, at the cost of destroying the Icon.<br /> <br /> The idea was that the first option looks, from the outside, to be the Icon-bearer becoming more and more faithful to the demigod, until the demigod 'returns through them'. And as for the virgin births thing, I'm not sure about the 'virgin' part, but if the Icon-bearer is a pregnant woman, the baby would be affected by the Halysis too, and the demigod could enter it if they really wanted to.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. I believe that system of returning from death is fitting. I should ask then since these don't seem to be covered, what happens if someone manages to break an Icon before the Demigod is reincarnated? What if the Demigod with the broken Icon has multiple Icons, do they move on to the next oldest available or do they simply die? Furthermore, given the Living Icon Merit a Demigod may use, if said living icon is a human, can the Demigod replace the human (as if they were replacing the bearer of a normal Icon) and retain the Icon's power until they &quot;grant&quot; it to someone else? Or can they have the human lose their &quot;Living Icon Status&quot; and the Demigod gains a new body out of ephemeral energy becoming material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:29:48-07:00","id":985604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985495#post985495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see. I believe that system of returning from death is fitting. I should ask then since these don't seem to be covered, what happens if someone manages to break an Icon before the Demigod is reincarnated? What if the Demigod with the broken Icon has multiple Icons, do they move on to the next oldest available or do they simply die?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Icons that a a demigod is inhabiting is destroyed, they die. However, a demigod can transfer from one Icon to another if they are in physical contact, provided that the demigod is cognisant enough to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985495#post985495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, given the Living Icon Merit a Demigod may use, if said living icon is a human, can the Demigod replace the human (as if they were replacing the bearer of a normal Icon) and retain the Icon's power until they &quot;grant&quot; it to someone else? Or can they have the human lose their &quot;Living Icon Status&quot; and the Demigod gains a new body out of ephemeral energy becoming material?</div> </div> </div> </div>Living icons aren't human. They're either a normal animal, or an intelligent supernatural animal or creature of some sort. And no, a living Icon can't be a Vampire. I'm not sure if that should be changed, though. Do you think a living Icon could be a person? It's just that seemed to be more a minor-Template thing, like the Enkidu and Priests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:20:36-07:00","id":985624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985604#post985604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Living icons aren't human. They're either a normal animal, or an intelligent supernatural animal or creature of some sort. And no, a living Icon can't be a Vampire. I'm not sure if that should be changed, though. Do you think a living Icon could be a person? It's just that seemed to be more a minor-Template thing, like the Enkidu and Priests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, pardon me on that part. The text in the merit only specified that it could be a living being and didn't say it couldn't be a human. Given Vampires are undead, I wasn't thinking to ask if they could be since they kinda required &quot;life&quot;. As for the possibility of being a human, I think it might be best to keep it towards animals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T13:50:33-07:00","id":985646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985624#post985624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, pardon me on that part. The text in the merit only specified that it could be a living being and didn't say it couldn't be a human. Given Vampires are undead, I wasn't thinking to ask if they could be since they kinda required &amp;quot;life&amp;quot;. As for the possibility of being a human, I think it might be best to keep it towards animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. The idea was to have something close to Athena's owl, a living symbol of the demigod's power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:44:16-07:00","id":985692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985646#post985646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. The idea was to have something close to Athena's owl, a living symbol of the demigod's power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the idea the merit gave. Perhaps just specifying the merit applies to animals only? How does &quot;Sacred Animal&quot; sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T23:36:30-07:00","id":985973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=985692#post985692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was the idea the merit gave. Perhaps just specifying the merit applies to animals only? How does &amp;quot;Sacred Animal&amp;quot; sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. I'll edit that when I get around to it and I'll post it up here for people to have a look at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T03:51:35-07:00","id":986029,"title":"","content":"Here's the revised Merit.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sacred Animal (OOO)</u></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One of the demigod\u2019s Icons is a living creature, usually a natural animal. The demigod may use them as an Icon so long as they are within line of sight. The Miracle emanates from the sacred animal, so their position should be used for the sake of range and area of effect. The sacred animal may use its imbued Miracles independently of the Demigod, although it must spend Willpower to do so, as per the usual rules for using Icons. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The animal is simply that: an animal, albeit one with unusual intelligence and the power to telepathically communicate with its master, so long as they are within (Luminance * 100) metres. This communication is more in terms of sensations, feelings and emotions than actual words.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Animals, even sacred ones, have their own minds and although they are loyal to the demigod they may simply wander off or have their eye caught by a pretty item. Also, the creatures can use the Miracles imbued within them independently of the demigod\u2019s wishes, if they want to. Lastly, if the demigod mistreats them, they may simply leave him, as they are under no particular compulsion to stay by his side.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-12-2016, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:41:33-07:00","id":986216,"title":"","content":"Here's a first idea of how the Disciple Merit could look. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Disciple (OOOO)</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisite</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mortal</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Through some quirk of fate, strange ancestry or simply a powerful soul, this mortal is immune to the Rapture and is resistant to a demigod\u2019s aura of Halysis. When calculating a Disciple\u2019s Halysis Tolerance, calculate it as ((Resolve + Composure + 2) * 2). A Disciple need only roll for gaining Halysis if the demigod in question has demonstrated miraculous powers obviously. Lastly, being a Disciple makes a mortal eligible to purchase Supernatural Merits of other kinds</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demigods are intensely interested in Disciples, as they are one of very few ways that they have to interact with the mortal world without Halysis running rampant. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Note:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The biological children of demigods gain this Merit for free, as their divine ancestry inures them to the influence of a demigod\u2019s Luminance. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:30:34-07:00","id":986696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=986216#post986216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a first idea of how the Disciple Merit could look. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Disciple (OOOO)</u></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisite</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mortal</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Through some quirk of fate, strange ancestry or simply a powerful soul, this mortal is immune to the Rapture and is resistant to a demigod\u2019s aura of Halysis. When calculating a Disciple\u2019s Halysis Tolerance, calculate it as ((Resolve + Composure + 2) * 2). A Disciple need only roll for gaining Halysis if the demigod in question has demonstrated miraculous powers obviously. Lastly, being a Disciple makes a mortal eligible to purchase Supernatural Merits of other kinds</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Demigods are intensely interested in Disciples, as they are one of very few ways that they have to interact with the mortal world without Halysis running rampant. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Note:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The biological children of demigods gain this Merit for free, as their divine ancestry inures them to the influence of a demigod\u2019s Luminance. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting...but playing into the idea raised by the word &quot;<b>disciple</b>&quot; you ever consider that these particular mortals could maybe not just resist Halysis, but maybe also help direct, enhance, or add nuance to the phenomena, much like disciples of old help spread messages of those they followed?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:38:48-07:00","id":986698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=986696#post986696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting...but playing into the idea raised by the word &quot;<b>disciple</b>&quot; you ever consider that these particular mortals could maybe not just resist Halysis, but maybe also help direct, enhance, or add nuance to the phenomena, much like disciples of old help spread messages of those they followed?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely in interesting idea. i'm not sure how you'd represent that, or exactly what that would do, for that matter. Perhaps they can add or remove levels of Halysis from others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:52:32-07:00","id":986705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=986698#post986698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely in interesting idea. i'm not sure how you'd represent that, or exactly what that would do, for that matter. Perhaps they can add or remove levels of Halysis from others?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea--also, maybe Demigods could channel miracles <i>through</i> disciples, a conduit to apply their powers at a distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 10-13-2016, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T05:54:52-07:00","id":986706,"title":"","content":"Side note...I've noticed you referred to Demigods as some sort of antithesis to Beasts, would that imply perhaps that Demigods can strengthen regular mortals against supernatural powers like beasts share kinship with monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T06:21:18-07:00","id":986712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=986705#post986705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good idea--also, maybe Demigods could channel miracles <i>through</i> disciples, a conduit to apply their powers at a distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of what Priests do, as well as the Sacred Animal Merit. Disciples are kind of an equivalent of Leviathan's Atolls. They're more immune to powers than having them themselves. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=986705#post986705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side note...I've noticed you referred to Demigods as some sort of antithesis to Beasts, would that imply perhaps that Demigods can strengthen regular mortals against supernatural powers like beasts share kinship with monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant it in the sense that Beasts are the 'Things In The Dark' while Demigods are the 'Torchbearers'. Demigods can imbue mortals with power by making them Priests and with what you said I'm considering making it so that mortals add their Halysis Threshold to resistance rolls against supernatural powers (&quot;My faith will protect me!&quot;). Sound interesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T10:39:25-07:00","id":986838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=986712#post986712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant it in the sense that Beasts are the 'Things In The Dark' while Demigods are the 'Torchbearers'. Demigods can imbue mortals with power by making them Priests and with what you said I'm considering making it so that mortals add their Halysis Threshold to resistance rolls against supernatural powers (&quot;My faith will protect me!&quot;). Sound interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T00:50:39-07:00","id":987135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=986838#post986838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think it would work to add it to any rolls to Abjure or Ward against ephemerals as well? (&quot;The power of *insert god here* compels you!&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T01:08:19-07:00","id":987142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=987135#post987135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think it would work to add it to any rolls to Abjure or Ward against ephemerals as well? (&quot;The power of *insert god here* compels you!&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps...You might make it a resistance to supernatural entities just in general (whether they be spiritual, material, both, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:35:24-07:00","id":987227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=987142#post987142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps...You might make it a resistance to supernatural entities just in general (whether they be spiritual, material, both, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea is that, as both Warding and Abjuration are basically the act of setting the power of one's soul against the entity, having a spark of Heavenly light in there would aid the mortal in their struggle. Warding and Abjuration are separate from directly resisting a supernatural effect. And yes, the resistance bonus would apply both to powers used by physical and ephemeral supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:41:33-07:00","id":987229,"title":"","content":"On another note, having re-red my Deep Meta, I find myself unsatisfied with it and am probably going to be significantly re-tooling it, keeping Mage's 'humanity has one shared soul' concept in mind (there's a hint for you ;D ).<br /> <br /> That said, any ideas anyone has will be taken into account and used if they thematically fit and are interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T02:16:21-07:00","id":992857,"title":"","content":"I don't suppose I could have some thoughts on these Domains, could I, as well as possibly some help with the unfinished ones (specifically Knowledge, and I'm not very happy with Technology)?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sun</u></span></span><ul><li>The Sun purifies</li> <li>The Sun brings light and hope</li> <li>The Sun beats down on those beneath its glare</li> <li>The Sun reveals what is hidden</li> <li>The Sun is pitiless</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Water</u></span></span><ul><li>Water brings life</li> <li>Water soothes</li> <li>Water carries away those caught in its flow</li> <li>Water seeps through cracks</li> <li>Water erodes</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Knowledge</u></span></span><ul><li>Knowledge reveals that which is</li> <li>Knowledge reveals that which was</li> <li>Knowledge can be gained and lost</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Death</u></span></span><ul><li>Death awaits</li> <li>Death brings the end of all things</li> <li>Death cannot be cheated</li> <li>Death may be held at bay</li> <li>Death allows only shades to exist beyond it</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Winter</u></span></span><ul><li>Winter slows things down</li> <li>Winter brings scarcity</li> <li>Winter drives men and beasts before it</li> <li>Winter comes again</li> <li>Winter brings the cold and the dark</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Technology</u></span></span><ul><li>Technology makes things easier</li> <li>Technology is created by humans</li> <li>Technology does not think</li> <li>Technology is complex</li> <li>Technology results from the application of knowledge</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fire</u></span></span><ul><li>Fire heats things</li> <li>Fire makes things more active</li> <li>Fire comforts</li> <li>Fire brings light and drives back the dark</li> <li>Fire changes things\u200b</li> </ul><br /> Some other ideas for other Domains would be nice too, if people want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-25-2016, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:30:25-07:00","id":993073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=992857#post992857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't suppose I could have some thoughts on these Domains, could I, as well as possibly some help with the unfinished ones (specifically Knowledge, and I'm not very happy with Technology)?<br /> Some other ideas for other Domains would be nice too, if people want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind me noting, Domains sorta feel like Siren's Opuses in that they use physical and conceptual connotations to show how they can work, only in that Demigods only require the Domain to do their miracles whereas Sirens require Conclusions to direct their Opuses.<br /> <br /> What I mean to say is: I'm offering the full list of Opuses if it helps on this project. :3 Slightly edited of course to account for Domains instead of Siren Verses.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Animal<ul><li>Animals are man's best friend.</li> <li>Animals are the life of the wild world. (Covers all Animals and Insects)</li> <li>Animals do not have Morality</li> <li>Animals do not have the same societal norms as civilization</li> </ul>Beauty<ul><li>Beauty is in the eye of the beholder</li> <li>Beauty dictates what is beautiful and what is ugly.</li> <li>Beauty tends to be depicted with goodness.</li> <li>Beautiful people are among the elite</li> <li>The depiction of beauty changes with societies and the times</li> </ul>Blood<ul><li>Blood is what flows through all living beings (including things that don't exactly fit &quot;blood&quot; as in human blood. For example, the fluid that transports water and nutrients in plants can count as &quot;Blood&quot;.)</li> <li>Blood is what keeps us alive (Like the above, doesn't need to be entirely physical. For example, in this context, Money can count as &quot;Blood&quot; for the purposes of Corporations and business since that's what keeps them alive, or even emotions found in a relationship)</li> <li>Blood is the life of supernatural beings (I imagine this mostly messing with the Fuel Stat of other supernaturals, like Siren's Pneuma, Vampire Vitae, Princess Wisps and the like)</li> </ul>Chaos<ul><li>Chaos is a state of unrest amongst the populace.</li> <li>Chaos is the unforseen accidents and opportunities in life</li> <li>Chaos is major natural disasters</li> <li>Chaos is mental insanity and emotional disruption</li> </ul>Darkness<ul><li>Darkness is the absence of light and the source of all shadows</li> <li>Darkness is in the sleep of night and death</li> <li>Darkness keeps secrets and hides things within it</li> <li>Darkness is negativity in emotions</li> <li>Darkness is despair</li> </ul>Earth<ul><li>Earth is the element of order and stability</li> <li>Earth is the foundation of all homes and structures of humans</li> <li>Earth is the largest graveyard that houses innumerable bodies</li> <li>Earth hides secrets and treasures beneath the surface</li> <li>The Earth is made up of all kinds of soil and rock</li> </ul>Fate<ul><li>Fate is the mother of all possibility</li> <li>Fate is what binds people together and breaks people apart</li> <li>Fate follows the law of equivalent exchange</li> <li>Fate is what the Lost and the Others are embroiled in</li> <li>Fate makes much use of the TvTropes pages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Fate punishes those who harm and blesses those who bring good</li> </ul>Nature<ul><li>Nature is from where all things grew from, even humanity</li> <li>Nature is generous, having bountiful harvests for all to take from</li> <li>Nature includes all plants, bacteria and disease</li> <li>Nature is an amoral circle of life where everything eventually feeds each other</li> </ul>Humanity<ul><li>Humanity is the creator of all social order</li> <li>Humanity is what created civilization</li> <li>Humanity is what all supernatural beings arose from</li> <li>Humanity creates and destroys</li> <li>Humanity is sapient and holds morals</li> <li>Humanity is skeptical</li> </ul>Light<ul><li>Light is the herald of morality</li> <li>Light beats back the darkness</li> <li>Light brings hope</li> <li>Light brings inspiration</li> <li>Light is all positive emotions</li> <li>Light may return out of the darkness</li> <li>Light is the truth</li> </ul>Sound<ul><li>Sound is the confirmation of existence</li> <li>Sound is the breaking of silence</li> <li>Sound is what makes us notice</li> </ul>Spirit<ul><li>Spirit is animism</li> <li>Spirit is the foundation of the soul</li> <li>Spirit is what each and every physical object and concept has</li> <li>Spirit is the appropriate mood in a situation</li> </ul>Taint<ul><li>Taint is the rot and corruption of physical objects and morality</li> </ul>Weather<ul><li>Weather is what sets the mood for a day</li> <li>Weather is a physical event</li> </ul>Wind<ul><li>Wind dances through the sky</li> <li>Wind is a destructive force of nature</li> <li>Wind is what holds all gases</li> <li>Wind cannot be contained</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/77986