t took those Opus and fully converted them to Domains?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it. :3 But yes, feel free to do as such with them.<br /> <br /> JUST to note though, I would like to say that Opus descriptions are different from how I listed them here. Pretty much, in Siren they are like this.<br /> <br /> *Insert Opus Name Here*<br /> *Insert Small Description*<br /> Physical: *Add in what the Siren may use as part of the opus in a physical or tangible form*<br /> Conceptual: *Add in description for what the Siren may use as part of the Opus in a conceptual or symbolic form*<br /> <br /> The reason it's not in that format when I posted them here for you to use was because I edited them to fit in the Domain format you posted. Just noting this to be absolutely clear. ^^&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:12:51-08:00","id":999366,"title":"","content":"You ever thought about making the concept of &quot;Fate&quot; a bit more of an enemy?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps making it more of an Achilles' Heel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:31:05-08:00","id":999406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=999366#post999366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You ever thought about making the concept of &quot;Fate&quot; a bit more of an enemy?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps making it more of an Achilles' Heel?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an idea, but I'm not sure how it might be done. Do you see entities birthed from 'Fate' like the Furies? A passive, subtle force that drives demigods towards something? One problem I can see with that, though, is it being too similar to Scion's Fatebinding stuff, as well as their cosmic concept of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:18:58-08:00","id":999454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=999406#post999406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an idea, but I'm not sure how it might be done. Do you see entities birthed from 'Fate' like the Furies? A passive, subtle force that drives demigods towards something? One problem I can see with that, though, is it being too similar to Scion's Fatebinding stuff, as well as their cosmic concept of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like concepts of Fate should come up more in a...let's say Changeling-Demigod Crossover, seeing as Changelings deal with it more. <br /> <br /> Oh god (pardon that pun), I now wonder on how True Fae and Demigods would get along. I imagine the True Fae would treat them like any other True Fae, and in turn that would make Changelings pretty leery around them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T20:24:57-08:00","id":999552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=999406#post999406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an idea, but I'm not sure how it might be done. Do you see entities birthed from 'Fate' like the Furies? A passive, subtle force that drives demigods towards something? One problem I can see with that, though, is it being too similar to Scion's Fatebinding stuff, as well as their cosmic concept of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm suggesting it to amp up the paranoia factor a bit...this is the World of Darkness after all--paranoia, desperation, and darkness kind of fall wherever you are and to whomever. <br /> <br /> In old stories demigods often have glorious fates awaiting them, but their destiny is almost always guaranteed to bite them in some fashion. Perhaps you could arrange it that for every success Demigods build for themselves a tragedy is sure to strike...or part of their glorious destiny entails a revoking of their very free will as they become less mortal and more part of some greater tapestry--they don't know where their power comes from, so whose to say they aren't just being turned into puppets for something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:36:10-08:00","id":999679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=999454#post999454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like concepts of Fate should come up more in a...let's say Changeling-Demigod Crossover, seeing as Changelings deal with it more. <br /> <br /> Oh god (pardon that pun), I now wonder on how True Fae and Demigods would get along. I imagine the True Fae would treat them like any other True Fae, and in turn that would make Changelings pretty leery around them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with that, both the Fate thing and the thing with the True Fae. I think, though, that the Gentry would likely regard demigods as being almost like a ghost in the machine, Fae essence trapped and warped in and by a meat-prison. A well-meaning Fae attempting to 'free' a demigod from their body might be an interesting storyline to make use of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:40:16-08:00","id":999681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=999552#post999552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm suggesting it to amp up the paranoia factor a bit...this is the World of Darkness after all--paranoia, desperation, and darkness kind of fall wherever you are and to whomever.<br /> <br /> In old stories demigods often have glorious fates awaiting them, but their destiny is almost always guaranteed to bite them in some fashion. Perhaps you could arrange it that for every success Demigods build for themselves a tragedy is sure to strike...or part of their glorious destiny entails a revoking of their very free will as they become less mortal and more part of some greater tapestry--they don't know where their power comes from, so whose to say they aren't just being turned into puppets for something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoilers for the deep meta, but<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"S