 of authority culminate in a council of Demigods nine steps beneath the rank and file members, who make important decisions for the group Others insist that there are no lower levels, and that underseers are assigned to others of the same rank in a semi-random fashion. A few Demigods (usually not members of the following themselves) allege that the most powerful members still reside in Hell itself, though whether they are part of its official power structure or rebels varies from teller to teller.<br /> <br /> The ideology of the following is such that authority is seen more as a burden than a privilege, hence the reason the group is ranked downward. The highest Status Demigods in the group may not even have the rank of underseer, which often nets more resentment than respect.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Factions</u></b><br /> There are three major factions among the Followers of the Nine Circles:</li> <li><u>The Hedonists</u> This faction seeks simply to enjoy the fruits of life in the mortal world. They are the most common.</li> <li><u>Collectors of the Unholy Tribute</u> This faction treats their time in the mortal world as a working vacation of limited extent. They seek to keep themselves out of Hell by sending others in their place, and it is to this end they lead their cults and other followers. Their sense of exactly what Hell is and what sins are necessary to arrive there vary - some claim that Heaven is really no better than Hell, and they are at least encouraging mortals to make the most of life.</li> <li><u>Parole Board</u> This faction hopes to release others from Hell. The methods used vary, and typically end up summoning beings from the Inferno or the Abyss rather than new Nine Circles Demigods. This is the faction that runs afoul of the Underseers most frequently, with some of the Branded arguing it should be banned completely. If the Parole Board was ever truly successful, the fears are, it would only result in drawing the attention of Hell\u2019s jailers.<br /> <b><u>Emblems</u></b><br /> The defining Miracles of the Following of the Nine Circles are those which <i>release. </i>Whether by unleashing natural forces or the inner nature of other sentient beings, the nature of these Demigods seems to strive against constraints. They are accordingly not very skilled at rebinding whatever forces they set free.<br /> <br /> <u>Myself am Hell</u> Although, the Liberated are no longer imprisoned within their native soil, its taint remains with them. An area within Luminance x feet of the Demigod has a hazardous environmental tilt of the Demigod\u2019s choice. By default this is a resonance with some negative emotion, but it can be changed with a Willpower point at any time. The Branded are not necessarily immune to the negative effects of any such tilt, in fact they may be more vulnerable, being at the epicenter of the effect.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Numinous Forms</u></b><br /> The numinous forms of the followers of the Nine Circles are grotesque. They often have features which seem stretched or distorted, such as cruel smiles which extend past the limits of a normal face. Their more inhuman attributes are rarely reminiscent of any particular animal, but combine the nature\u2019s arsenal of horns, fangs, and spines with a distinctly unnatural aesthetic. Many also are marked as if by past punishments, bearing brands and scars.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Stereotypes</u></b><br /> <u>The Morningstar</u> They would drag us into a war lost centuries ago. Why risk losing all that we\u2019ve managed to get back?<br /> <u>Vassals</u> They turn this life into servitude nearly as bad as what we escaped. As long as they don\u2019t try to make us do the same, they\u2019re welcome to it.<br /> <u>Ascendents</u> What more are they striving for? This state has everything we need.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hopefully, this will be an inducement to resume working on the other Following.<br /> <br /> Please share your suggestions on what should be done to modify the Nine Circles write-up above (of course, ajf115 has the final say).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the write-up. I'm very grateful that people are still interested in this. I haven't had time to read it over properly, but I'll do so as soon as I can.<br /> <br /> As a bit of a warning, though, I'm intending to go over what's been done for Demigod so far and re-assess many parts, particularly the mechanics for Miracles, the whole deal with the Drasil, Titans, Teras and similar. I want to try and remodel the whole to be more closely connected to the human world, to make demigods' power more fragile and reliant on power bases (e.g. cults, arcane geometries of ley lines, churches, places of power etc) to wield anything beyond their basic powers. I like the idea of demigods being like the guys you traditionally try to foil the plans of in urban fantasy RPGs, the ones who pull strings and organise things <i>oh-so-carefully</i> to gain grater power. And yes, the parallels to the God-Machine's Infrastructure are entirely deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T20:39:20-07:00","id":1124155,"title":"","content":"Can I suggest a antagonist idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T23:03:26-07:00","id":1124192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=1124155#post1124155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I suggest a antagonist idea?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Certainly, although it may not be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T06:04:11-07:00","id":1124270,"title":"","content":"Ah, I'm afraid I've got some <b>important news</b> related to <i>Demigod</i> which could be construed as either a good thing or a bad one. So here goes.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1868\" data-vbnamecard=\"1868\">hellovg</a> and I are going to be abandoning our respective fansplats (my<i> Demigod </i>and his <i>Celestial: the Reclamation</i>) in favor of combining our efforts on one combined splat, of a name not yet decided upon but with a shared concept of 'earthly divinity'. We're not recruiting for help <i>per se</i> at the moment, but if anyone's interested feel free to send me a PM to signal such and we'll see how things go. It may be a little while before we post a full thread for the thing, as I'd like to get at least the basics in order beforehand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T07:56:12-07:00","id":1124301,"title":"","content":"Can i still post my idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T08:24:07-07:00","id":1124309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=1124301#post1124301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can i still post my idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can, and it'll likely be helpful, as following our initial brainstorming we're still a bit short on the 'common' antagonists for the splat (equivalent of spirits for Werewolf).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T14:29:55-07:00","id":1126451,"title":"","content":"Congratulations to both of you to merging your ideas: hopefully the result will be even stronger and more interesting than the sum of its parts!<br /> <br /> I do hope that that a good portion of the material from this thread makes it through to the final cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T01:55:04-07:00","id":1126620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=1126451#post1126451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congratulations to both of you to merging your ideas: hopefully the result will be even stronger and more interesting than the sum of its parts!<br /> <br /> I do hope that that a good portion of the material from this thread makes it through to the final cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's hoping! Also, I can tell you that there are a number of things being kept, in particular Icons (they're being reskinned a little and made more 'spiritual' as Astra) and Aspects, again being retooled a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T17:49:48-07:00","id":1126902,"title":"","content":"I have to kind of admit, I kinda liked Demigod as it was, but I hope that you guys do well together. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T09:16:59-07:00","id":1128480,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, I'm going to ask a question, and the answers (please, anyone who has an opinion, give me an answer) will likely effect the splat hellovg and I are hashing out at present. <br /> <br /> Namely, what parts of Demigod did people like best, or think worked especially well, or thought was cool? And more importantly, what did people think were its problems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:04:40-07:00","id":1128558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=1128480#post1128480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, I'm going to ask a question, and the answers (please, anyone who has an opinion, give me an answer) will likely effect the splat hellovg and I are hashing out at present.<br /> <br /> Namely, what parts of Demigod did people like best, or think worked especially well, or thought was cool? And more importantly, what did people think were its problems?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in general demigods are easier to relate to, since they're potentially more down to earth than the otherwise cosmic beings that true gods are. =3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T19:27:20-07:00","id":1128673,"title":"","content":"I liked the Aspect System, it feels like it covered the types of gods nicely. I also liked the ideas for Icons as well as Halysis and the Rapture, as well as Enkidus as a subsplat. Attachment as a morality also felt like it did well in order to represent how the Divine and Mortal natures interacted or how one could fall (or rise) too far from the other extreme.<br /> <br /> I also like the Domains and Miracles section, if mainly in how it covers versatility for powers as well as how versatile a god's coverage on a domain is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T02:53:42-07:00","id":1128740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=1128673#post1128673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Aspect System, it feels like it covered the types of gods nicely. I also liked the ideas for Icons as well as Halysis and the Rapture, as well as Enkidus as a subsplat. Attachment as a morality also felt like it did well in order to represent how the Divine and Mortal natures interacted or how one could fall (or rise) too far from the other extreme.<br /> <br /> I also like the Domains and Miracles section, if mainly in how it covers versatility for powers as well as how versatile a god's coverage on a domain is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we're keeping the Aspect system with minimal changes, and Icons are being kept, albeit somewhat revamped into the quasi-spiritual symbols named Astra (don't worry, they can still be made physical). I... don't think we'll be keeping Halysis, although Rapture is likely to persist in some fashion (mind you, we haven't really discussed that part yet). The morality-type is likely to remains similar to Attachment, although probably with more of an element of 'responsibility and lack thereof'.<br /> <br /> The powers are still very much up in the air. We've had ideas, played around with them, swapped them out for new ones, played around with those... I'll have to get back to you on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/853975-demigod-the-empyrean-fansplat?p=1128558#post1128558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in general demigods are easier to relate to, since they're potentially more down to earth than the otherwise cosmic beings that true gods are. =3</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of a spoiler (maybe? I think?) so I'll be putting it in spoiler isolation here.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The new demigods (whose name we still haven't decided on) are essentially a symbiotic being composed of a human with a damaged soul and a transcendent spiritual being which can probably best be defined as an entity composed of living Resonance, exiled from its 'waveform' existence and forced to live as a singular thing. They act as a kind of spiritual life-support for one another, consciousnesses and bodies mingling. The only issue is that the human part - which is the part of the conjoined being which does most of what could be considered by, y'know', humans as 'thinking' - is more or less incapable of comprehending the memories and experiences of the other half, having to resort to interpreting them through the lens of their own beliefs. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:34:34-07:00","id":1141042,"title":"","content":"The thread for the new fansplat <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1868\" data-vbnamecard=\"1868\">hellovg</a> and I have been working on has been posted! You can find it here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141041-empyrean-the-redemption-collaborative-fansplat\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ative-fansplat</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}